{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want","id":444750,"title":"Which New Pantheons do you want?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T12:37:14-07:00","id":444750,"title":"Which New Pantheons do you want?","content":"Now, new in this case means that The Greek, Egyptian, Norse, Aztec, Voodoo, Japanese, Persian, Irish, Vedic, and Chinese, pantheons are already covered. Which other non-fictional pantheons do the people on these boards want? Note: Fictional Pantheons would describe the Atlantean Pantheon and the Nationalistic Pantheons in the WWII setting in the Scion Companion. It would also cover Tolkien's elvish pantheons or anything by Moorcock or Fritz Lieber. This thread focuses on mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:47:05-07:00","id":444789,"title":"","content":"An Official Mayan, Inuit, or Arabic Pantheon might be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:54:54-07:00","id":444798,"title":"","content":"A Native American pantheon would be cool and an official slavic/russian would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:06:07-07:00","id":445041,"title":"","content":"Inca first and foremost. Then Maya, personally. Less personally, Polynesian, Mesopotamian, and Inuit. And, in my dream-world, Guarani","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:29:01-07:00","id":445063,"title":"","content":"Mesopotamian. Hands down. I've become obsessed with them in recent years. They are just the coolest!<br /> <br /> Polynesian would also be welcome. As would the various Native American pantheons. Slavic/Russian are also cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:27:32-07:00","id":445096,"title":"","content":"Cherokee, Navajo, Iroquois, or Russian would all be really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:20:11-07:00","id":446122,"title":"","content":"I would like a Polynesian Pantheon, but it's not like you can really encapsulate that much difference in just one. It's not quite &quot;American Indian&quot; bad, by any means, but the myths of Aotearoa (New Zealand) and Tahiti are about as different as those of Greece vs. Rome, Russian vs. Polish, Germanic vs. Norse, so one pantheon for both might work there. But those two together are distinctive from Hawaii that it's probably too much glomming together of things that are pretty different. More like Irish and Welsh or Baltic and Slavic. Distinctive enough that it's probably a disservice to mush them up together. Then you have something like Rapa Nui (Easter Island) which has gone it's own weird way from either of those. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, in no particular order: Mesopotamian (which is big, messy and chronologically deep, but can probably work as one pantheon, just like I don't see the need for Mycenean AND Greek pantheons), Hopi, Navajo, Inuit, Inca, Cherokee, Slavic, Canaanite, Lakota, Welsh, Tengriist...<br /> <br /> And, more generally: An Australian Aboriginal pantheon, something from West Africa, something from Central Asia (one, at least), something from Melanesia, something from the Amazon basin, something from the American/Canadian Northwest Coastal region<br /> <br /> And, of course, always.... Hittite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:08:05-07:00","id":446735,"title":"","content":"I'd like something...animist-like. Archaeologists continue to find evidence of animal worship, and as they seem to have been among the the first deities I'd like to see some representation...hmm. There are typically 6 early civilizations that probably deserve mention; Mesopotamia (Sumer which becomes Babylon a few millennia later); Egypt we already have; Indus Valley (India) we also have here; China (primarily Majiayao culture); Norte Chico civilization (Ancient Peru); And Mesoamerica (primarily the Olmecs). I have to admit I'm not fond of the word &quot;civilization&quot; in certain contexts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:44:08-07:00","id":446804,"title":"","content":"Good luck with the Indus Valley since there essentially no translated documents. It would be largely fictional with some nice extrapolated artwork. It makes the Gaulish pantheon look like a wellspring flooded with information. <br /> <br /> And Norte Chico is going to be worse. Since there's no names, literature, anything to work with. Essentially, &quot;I'm the son of the Staff God!&quot; <br /> <br /> With the Olmecs, at least you have a LOT of cool art. But nothing else to work with. No language. No stories. Unless you want to backtrack later Mesoamerican myths... which doesn't really help, as you probably have at least one of those pantheons probably in play. And end up with the same problem as with Norte Chico... &quot;I'm the Son of the Maize God&quot;, &quot;I'm the daughter of the Banded Eye God!&quot;, &quot;Yeah? Well, I'm the grandson of the Fish/Shark Monster!&quot; (Or Gods II, VII, VIII respectively.)<br /> <br /> There is a law of dimishing returns with a lot of ancient pantheons for which there is really no supporting information to use to build them up. A game of myths and these cultures don't have anything but the vaguest hints of what their mythologies actually were...<br /> <br /> There are other great examples out there of mythologies that look great, but all we've got is STUFF, no stories: the Anasazi, Cahokia and/or the SouthEastern Ceremonial Cult Complex, the Gaulish/Celtic/Celtiberians, there's a completely new Mesopotamian-era-equivalent culture in Iran that's just being discovered, Lepinski Vir (those cool fish men idols), Gobekli Tepe (sorry, no diacriticals), what may have been some pretty hardcore cool civilizations in the Amazon basin (I'll defer to Griff on this as it's not my area), the Minoans (we've got more on them than Indus or Norte Chico.... even Olmecs really since have SOME clue about names and stories... but not enough), the Vinca culture, etc. (and I'm just too lazy to get up, walk 3 steps and pick up my books on the archaeology of Africa right now). <br /> <br /> Oh, I want to add Tibetan/Bon to my list. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:02:24-07:00","id":446819,"title":"","content":"Oy; where to begin? <br /> <br /> First, I\u2019d like to see the Voodoo Pantheon replaced by one or two of the West African Pantheons from which Voodoo is derived, under the premise that Voodoo is a human-founded religion <i>based on</i> said West African Pantheons. <br /> <br /> Next, let me draw a distinction between \u201cdetailed Pantheons\u201d and \u201coutlined Pantheons\u201d: the former are given enough detail that you can play characters tied to them; the latter are described in just enough detail to give a general sense of what they\u2019re like and, more importantly, what distinguishes them from the detailed Pantheons with which they might otherwise be confused \u2014 but they\u2019re not actually fleshed out to playable status. So, for example, I might pick one Polynesian Pantheon to receive a detailed treatment (say, one based on Hawaiian beliefs), and complement it with \u201cPantheon outlines\u201d for a couple of other Polynesian Pantheons (such as ones based on Easter Island and New Zealand beliefs). The outlined Pantheons could later be turned into detailed Pantheons given sufficient interest in doing so. <br /> <br /> North America should get a detailed Inuit Pantheon (to deal with Alaska and Western Canada), a detailed Algonquin Pantheon (for Eastern Canada and the northeast United States), something from the Great Plains, and something west of the Rockies, in addition to the Aztecs. It should <i>not</i> get a generic blend of Native American mythologies lumped together into a single Pantheon, and \u201coutlined Pantheons\u201d should be used liberally to make it clear that the Pantheons that <i>are</i> detailed are a mere sampling of the North American Pantheons. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d <i>like</i> to get Gaulish and Arabian Pantheons; but given the lack of solid information on these, they\u2019d end up qualifying as fictional Pantheons and thus outside the scope of this thread. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d like a Phoenician Pantheon, a Sumerian Pantheon, a Slavic Pantheon, and a Mongolian Pantheon, with Baltic and Caucasian Pantheons being outlined rather than detailed. <br /> <br /> And I could keep going\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:40:40-07:00","id":447009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=446819#post446819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oy; where to begin?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> North America should get a detailed Inuit Pantheon (to deal with Alaska and Western Canada), a detailed Algonquin Pantheon (for Eastern Canada and the northeast United States), something from the Great Plains, and something west of the Rockies, in addition to the Aztecs. It should <i>not</i> get a generic blend of Native American mythologies lumped together into a single Pantheon, and \u201coutlined Pantheons\u201d should be used liberally to make it clear that the Pantheons that <i>are</i> detailed are a mere sampling of the North American Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>West of the Rockies as in NW Coast (Salish, Tlingit, Haida, Kwakwaka'kawakw, etc.)? Or West of the Rockies as in CA (Chumash, Tongva, etc.)?<br /> <br /> I really want to throw the Hopi/Zuni/Pueblo and/or the Navajo/Dineh in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T06:34:20-07:00","id":447629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=446804#post446804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good luck with the Indus Valley since there essentially no translated documents. It would be largely fictional with some nice extrapolated artwork. It makes the Gaulish pantheon look like a wellspring flooded with information.<br /> <br /> And Norte Chico is going to be worse. Since there's no names, literature, anything to work with. Essentially, &quot;I'm the son of the Staff God!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's ok.<br /> That's ok. I'm not looking for a paper on archaeology. I'm looking to see what stories get created from what does exist. Which means &quot;largely fictional&quot; is fine. (I'm pretty sure this is still a game.) &quot;Creative&quot; and &quot;entertaining&quot; are what I look for. And I haven't been disappointed yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:08:10-07:00","id":447708,"title":"","content":"To butcher Gertrude Stein, &quot;There is no there there.&quot; <br /> <br /> There is just no mythology for those cultures: A picture of a fish man on a cylinder seal is not a mythology. An image of a guy with a head-dress and a stick is not a mythology. An image impressed onto a silver cauldron, a bunch of syncretistic references in another cultures documents that are inconsistent and illustrative are not a mythology. A bunch of glyphs that seem to have something to do with the mythologies we have from subsequent cultures are not mythologies, especially with no accompanying material that associates them with the later myths. A large amount of ceremonial desposits but nothing more than figures, etc. are not a mythology. <br /> <br /> Mention of a &quot;lost&quot; people who are associated with visible remains, considered to be ancestors, &quot;Others&quot;, divine beings, demons, etc. probably gets you a little closer, but, really, what it gets you is what you get for mythologies we do (sorta) have records for... analogues of the Alfar, or Nymphs/Dryads/Satyrs, Djinn, etc. So, sure, you can try to shoehorn the Olmec big heads into Mesoamerican myths as some mythological figures in their mythology or use the Anasazi the way they were perceived by the Navajo and/or the Hopi, but then you are using the memory of the culture/people in a mythical way from someone else's mythology, not as a mythology that you just don't have. The Anasazi pantheon probably has a lot to do with the Hopi pantheon, but who knows? <br /> <br /> You're right though, this is largely NOT about archaeology, so if all we have is archaeology or textual/ethnohistorical information that's tattered onion-skin thin, at best, then those pantheons should go down with the Great Old Ones, the &quot;Folk-Tale&quot; pantheons of WW2, the Atlantean pantheon, the Valar, etc. Pure fiction. <br /> <br /> We do have stories for some really cool weird off-kilter stuff that CAN be done. Hittites LEAP to mind. <br /> <br /> And the OP wanted actual mythologies, actual pantheons. Not fictional creations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:39:32-07:00","id":447816,"title":"","content":"The Gaelic pantheon can't be anything but a fictional creation, as well as the related &quot;druid pantheon.&quot; I certainly hope it won't stop anyone from making one however.<br /> However I agree that the OP wanted to focus on the actual existing myths, so my digression can't be welcome. *bows out*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:03:39-07:00","id":448241,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also not a treatise on comparative religion/mythology, which is why care needs to be taken in distinguishing between which Pantheons should be <i>detailed</i> (because oh wow! There\u2019s something there that players and narrators would love to dig their teeth into) and which ones should just be <i>outlined</i> (because as interesting as they may be, you can\u2019t justify a full write-up for them). <br /> <br /> Frankly, I don\u2019t know enough about most mythologies to make that determination; I\u2019m really only familiar with the Greek and Norse Pantheons. What I\u2019d love to see would be a hundred-Pantheon list of elevator pitches: one sentence about each saying why it deserves to be given a detailed treatment. That would at least give me a sense as to what the options are, beyond geographic region. For instance, you mentioned the Hopi: what do they bring to the table other than being situated in the American southwest? (I\u2019m not disagreeing with the proposal; I just don\u2019t know anything about the Hopi beyond their name and region.)<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s also worth considering the game\u2019s initial focus: as much as Onyx Path has an international audience, its primary audience is still North American \u2014 specifically, the United States. As such, the initial selection of Pantheons ought to be ones whose influence is likely to be found in the United States, as the default game is likely to be set there. Which isn\u2019t <i>nearly</i> as restrictive as it might sound at first, given its \u201cnation of immigrants\u201d nature. This informed my earlier suggestions: you say that there are (at least) three distinct Polynesian Pantheons, based in New Zealand, Hawaii, and Easter Island; I say that if we only get one of those, all else being equal, it should be the Hawaiian one (because Hawaii is a State) \u2014 this coming from someone who lived in New Zealand for a while and would personally be interested in that Polynesian Pantheon. And that\u2019s <i>almost</i> an argument for choosing a Voodoo Pantheon over a West African one \u2014 <i>almost</i>. I still prefer \u201cVoodoo is how [West African Pantheon] manifests itself in North America\u201d. That is, elements of Voodoo should be there; but they should be build on a West African foundation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-18-2015, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:29:17-07:00","id":448278,"title":"","content":"It's hard to boil the Hopi down into a one sentence pitch.... So I won't try. Here's a fast, dirty and messy pitch -<br /> <br /> Unique worldview but some familiar tropes, so easier access than they would otherwise seem. There are definitely some Mesoamerica-esque features - like Pahana, a Quetzalcoatl-like figure (&quot;white&quot; god, went away to east but will come back, thought that he had when the Spaniards showed up, but they TESTED the Spaniard in question so they knew he was NOT Pahana... I bet Monteczuma wishes he'd done that...) - but still very very differen, so it's not retreading old ground. Rich detailed myths with the gods doing lots of cool things (which is something we don't actually have for the Loa... but do for the Orisha): Hahti Wuti - Grandmother Spider, who led people from the last world into this one and made sure they learned what they needed to know in order to live... also patron of the Spider Clan, Masauwu, Lord of Fire and the Dead (the entrance to his underworld is where the 2 rivers meet in the Grand Canyon) with his flaming whips made of braided yucca plants, Pookanghoya and Palongahoya, sort of their version of the Hero Twins from Mayan myths (only not), etc.. Lots of &quot;other beings&quot; to slot in. (Including &quot;witches&quot;, &quot;sorcerers&quot; and &quot;wizards&quot;, oh my, who all do different things) and the Anasazi get some mileage here as well. Potential cool relics. (I want the bag of magic corn meal!) There's enough there to get a good PSP out of (which can be a very key factor in trying to create a new pantheon.... if you don't know enough about them to have them have a power of their own... they are probably going to be too flat to sustain a lot of stories), probably something to do with the religious aspects of the &quot;Kachina dolls&quot; only done with more understanding and reverence for the issues.<br /> <br /> If I were to have to pick an American Southwest tribe to detail out as a pantheon, the Hopi would be my No. 1 choice. Only very slightly edging out the Navajo for that spot. It's a shame to not have all the other very very different groups there detailed as well, but you can't have everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 03-18-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:56:01-07:00","id":449741,"title":"","content":"Polynesian, personally. Focus on either Hawaiian or Maori, as they're probably the most well-documented. Though for islands thousands of miles apart, their mythologies do have a surprising amount of overlap.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, the creation story with Rangi and Papa vs their children really fits the Gods vs. Titans theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T17:43:20-07:00","id":449941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=449741#post449741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Polynesian, personally. Focus on either Hawaiian or Maori, as they're probably the most well-documented. Though for islands thousands of miles apart, their mythologies do have a surprising amount of overlap.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, the creation story with Rangi and Papa vs their children really fits the Gods vs. Titans theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less so than, say, the Irish and Welsh and merging those two would make people scream. <br /> <br /> Papa (Hawaiian) and Papa/Papatanaku (Maori) are very similar, as are Rangi (Hawaiian) and Rangi/Ranginui (Maori), but, to the Maori, they are VERY Titan-like, probably including their oldest son Tawhirimatea as well, to the Hawaiians, they definitely give off a &quot;divine ruler couple progenitor&quot; gods vibe (with a friendly Titan in Kane)<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd go with the Maori because of the absolutely awesome and fitting-for-the-game story about Ranginiu &amp; Papatanaku, Tawhirirmatea, Tumatauegna, Tangaroa, Haumiatiketike, Tane &amp; Rongo. It's lacking in a few goddesses, but with JUST those guys, you almost have enough material for divine parentage right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:55:09-07:00","id":450034,"title":"","content":"I think Mesopotamian is the game's biggest gap. It's an important culture; and it's well-documented, with lots of vivid personalities and stories, making it easy to adapt.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T06:01:46-07:00","id":450347,"title":"","content":"*nods*<br /> Sumer, like Egypt, went through several periods that saw some changes.<br /> I for one would like to see how such changes are made to fit in with today's timeframe. After all humanity has changed over the millennia. It seems fitting that the gods would too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:05:26-07:00","id":450498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=450034#post450034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mesopotamian is the game's biggest gap. It's an important culture; and it's well-documented, with lots of vivid personalities and stories, making it easy to adapt.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It's all of those things and the material is MUCH more accessible than many other pantheons out there. It may not be as widely known as the Greek and Norse, but it's definitely on par with, say, the Irish. And, probably overall, more well known than, say, the Aztec. (The Aztec, however, have high a shock value and people have some idea about the Aztec people, so they are a good choice for the level of interest they can generate as opposed to general knowledge.)<br /> <br /> Having said that, though, there are a lot of cool pantheons out there, like the Yazata, which aren't part of the zeitgeist. I think there needs to be a balance between a culture to culture &quot;popularity contest&quot; vs. accessing the more obscure, but very cool, stuff that is lurking out there. A nice mix (slanted to the popular) would be fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 03-20-2015, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:44:34-07:00","id":453353,"title":"","content":"What I really want, is guidelines for homebrewing Pantheons. Because there's no way they can fit every Pantheon on the world into one book, or even a dozen books. Empowering their fanbase into filling in the gaps just seems like it'd appeal to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:38:05-07:00","id":453740,"title":"","content":"Would Buddhism / Hindu be interesting? You could have Scions walking around with like 6 to 12 arms. Might be a little bit risque because it's a modern day religion, but if they can get away with the Loa, I don't think it would be too complicated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if we're going by real world mythology, I'd like to pose the concept of Cthulhu and friends. <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Yes</b></i></span>, there are actual cults dedicated to worshiping them, so the idea has merit!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cz1ANnhJkPU\" target=\"_blank\">Buddhist / Hindu Scion in Action</a><br /> <br /> <br /> On an additional note, I would also like to see an &quot;independent pantheon&quot; at some point. Gods and goddesses who operate on their own, such as the Lord of the Harvest and so on. I think a monotheism faction could be an effective means of independent Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-24-2016, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T00:07:15-07:00","id":453930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=453353#post453353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I really want, is guidelines for homebrewing Pantheons. Because there's no way they can fit every Pantheon on the world into one book, or even a dozen books. Empowering their fanbase into filling in the gaps just seems like it'd appeal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem there is that the guidelines would be something like &quot;Do hours of research on the subject, attempt to create a PSP based on the central philosophy of the culture, balancing it against dozens of other powers that we're not very good at balancing ourselves, then write up short descriptions of the major deities. Drink heavily.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's equally impossible to nail down a system that can flexibly represent every mythology in history, and WW/OP has <i>never</i> successfully written rules for designing <i>anything</i> mechanical and then been able to stick to those rules, even in their own material that comes out <i>in the same book as those rules</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T05:39:40-07:00","id":454130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=453930#post453930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The problem there is that the guidelines would be something like &quot;Do hours of research on the subject, attempt to create a PSP based on the central philosophy of the culture, balancing it against dozens of other powers that we're not very good at balancing ourselves, then write up short descriptions of the major deities. Drink heavily.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's equally impossible to nail down a system that can flexibly represent every mythology in history, and WW/OP has <i>never</i> successfully written rules for designing <i>anything</i> mechanical and then been able to stick to those rules, even in their own material that comes out <i>in the same book as those rules</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well to cut hours and hours of research out of the work<br /> <br /> Here's the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ob7PfxvJCN0\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu mythos explained</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T23:08:49-07:00","id":463160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=453740#post453740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Buddhism / Hindu be interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the Hindu Pantheon already in the game? That's the Devas from the Companion right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:29:54-07:00","id":463205,"title":"","content":"I remember some Talk back at,Jhons Scion Resources, about a Tibetan Pantheon , i really would like see more about that. Roman,Mayan and Mesopotamian Pantheons would also be Cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T06:14:52-07:00","id":463396,"title":"","content":"Since belief doesn't make a deity, and mankind is over a million years old...<i>BUT</i> we have only representations of pantheons that only go so far back.<br /> <br /> You could shoot in the dark, blindfolded and come up with your own pantheon that could ostensibly be spot on and thousands of years older.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:09:56-07:00","id":463476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=446819#post446819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I\u2019d like to see the Voodoo Pantheon replaced by one or two of the West African Pantheons from which Voodoo is derived, under the premise that Voodoo is a human-founded religion <i>based on</i> said West African Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to go ahead and confirm that we're really looking to integrate Yoruba and the Loa in 2e as a prime example of a how a pantheon reacts to socio-political changes in the World (the Diaspora) and what an &quot;old guard&quot; versus a &quot;new guard&quot; looks like within a pantheon (and how a new guard tends to interact more with Scions or Gods from other pantheons).<br /> <br /> Also, by extension, 2e's &quot;core&quot; pantheons are commentary on how pantheons function in the World, providing GMs with guidelines on how to create their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d <i>like</i> to get Gaulish...Pantheons; but given the lack of solid information on these, they\u2019d end up qualifying as fictional Pantheons and thus outside the scope of this thread. </div> </div> </div>Personally? I'd love to do a Gaulish pantheon as a prime example of a &quot;dead&quot; or destroyed pantheon as a potential Kickstarter goal or further PDF/POD book down the line. They got completely annihilated by a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar\" target=\"_blank\">militant Scion of Venus</a>. What strange strands does Fate weave for the dead...? When you walk in the footsteps of dead gods, do they then walk like you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-31-2015, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:17:54-07:00","id":463486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463476#post463476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally? I'd love to do a Gaulish pantheon as a prime example of a &quot;dead&quot; or destroyed pantheon as a potential Kickstarter goal or further PDF/POD book down the line. They got completely annihilated by a militant Scion of Venus. What strange strands does Fate weave for the dead...? When you walk in the footsteps of dead gods, do they then walk like you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bring it! Take my money please!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:41:40-07:00","id":463531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463476#post463476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally? I'd love to do a Gaulish pantheon as a prime example of a &quot;dead&quot; or destroyed pantheon as a potential Kickstarter goal or further PDF/POD book down the line. They got completely annihilated by a militant Scion of Venus. What strange strands does Fate weave for the dead...? When you walk in the footsteps of dead gods, do they then walk like you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nnnnngh. Yes. Thousands times, yes. My french mind is pleased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:24:19-07:00","id":463636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463476#post463476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally? I'd love to do a Gaulish pantheon as a prime example of a &quot;dead&quot; or destroyed pantheon as a potential Kickstarter goal or further PDF/POD book down the line. They got completely annihilated by a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar\" target=\"_blank\">militant Scion of Venus</a>. What strange strands does Fate weave for the dead...? When you walk in the footsteps of dead gods, do they then walk like you?</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as you put in the caveat that you are essentially making almost the entire thing up, that it's an exercise in reconstruction akin to finding a burned down house in the woods and building something on the foundations that includes pretty much everything left architecturally, but that you are doing it without anything like photograph. <br /> <br /> But you didn't rebuild the house. You built a new house with some old pieces here and there, a general idea of what houses like this were like typically based on some other examples and a whole lot of imagination.<br /> <br /> So somewhere 3 notches up from the Atlantean pantheon. Around where the WW2 pantheons are. (Since some of the &quot;gods&quot; are based on solid, fun folktales.... which are two steps down from myths - myths, legends, folktales.) <br /> <br /> Having said that, sure. Why not? It would be a ton of fun to try to sift through a lot of Roman syncretism, iconography and artwork from archaeological sites (the Gundestrup Cauldron Rules!), retconning from Irish &amp; Welsh myths and some folktales, trying to cobble and shoehorn things together based on similarities in nomenclature (Lugh-Llew-Lugh, Nodens-Nudd-Nuada, etc.) It just needs to be telegraphed as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:31:08-07:00","id":463671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463636#post463636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So long as you put in the caveat that you are essentially making almost the entire thing up, that it's an exercise in reconstruction akin to finding a burned down house in the woods and building something on the foundations that includes pretty much everything left architecturally, but that you are doing it without anything like photograph.<br /> <br /> It just needs to be telegraphed as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> I mean, given that there will be a caveat in the front of the book warning students from using Scion for their myth and religious studies homework.<br /> <br /> To quote something I wrote earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keep in mind, though, that our foremost goal is a playable and enjoyable mythological game allowing players to embody the myths of legend, wear divine mantles of succession and create their own myths in the vein of old in the modern day whilst being a badass, not arguing about who's God K and who isn't. Accuracy and respect are still very high priorities. But if we're looking at Lugh of the Tuatha de Dannen and see the Welsh Lleu Llaw Gyffes and Lugus of the Gauls, there's a judgment call to be made. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-31-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:50:16-07:00","id":463696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463671#post463671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?<br /> <br /> I mean, given that there will be a caveat in the front of the book warning students from using Scion as a basis for their myth and religious studies homework.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I think the idea is to distinguish the theoretical pseudo-Gaul pantheon from how the others are altered, in the sense that, for example, the Lugh example you give in your quote is because you have too much to work with, while the Pseudo-Gauls would have far too little, and thus is noteworthy in its reconstructedness. Sorry if I got anything wrong, Mr or Ms Ajax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:37:14-07:00","id":463728,"title":"","content":"The Sumerian pantheon would be really cool. Especially Inanna, Enki and Utu. If the gods of Kemet are not too old-fashioned for the setting, neither are the sumerians.<br /> The Hittite empire would have been be a rich mine of ideas, but frankly, all those gods, cultures and languages colliding is just too much for a roleplaying game, and simplifying things would make the &quot;Hittites&quot; too generic.<br /> Some more variety for the Celts would be appreciated as well. Some juicy Welsh lore, perhaps? Manannan, Gwyn, Rhiannon, mmmmm...<br /> Bushman lore, like the kukummi Bleek and Lloyd collected? Incredible, but unlikely to make it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:01:57-07:00","id":463760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463671#post463671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?<br /> <br /> I mean, given that there will be a caveat in the front of the book warning students from using Scion for their myth and religious studies homework.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? <br /> <br /> You're a writer Don't you want credit for the cool stuff you make up? When you take little pieces of next to nothing a come up with something cool that is NOT actually just you doing a synthesis and a translation into a workable game format. That's a lot more of YOU in that.<br /> <br /> Plus, you can throw in a caveat on page after the title and say that, but that doesn't mean people will pay attention at all. People who get their Welsh mythology from Evangeline Walton are going to be getting something closer to Welsh myths that people who read Patricia Keneally Morrison's Celts-in-Space pastiche. Neither is hardcore slogging through the translations and trying to extract out &quot;noise&quot;. (Or, for real fun, reading the Old Welsh.) For the most part and most people, that's pretty boring, if not impossible (depending on how good your Old Welsh is). Evangeline Walton threw in a very short Appendix highlighting the changes she made or when she made things up. It didn't detract from the books at all. <br /> <br /> People WILL get their mythology from Scion. They already do. Particularly when it comes to the less accessible pantheons. So, even with the caveat, people think the Gaulish pantheon is what the people in Gaul were worshiping before Julius came through. And it's not. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:10:27-07:00","id":463763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463696#post463696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the idea is to distinguish the theoretical pseudo-Gaul pantheon from how the others are altered, in the sense that, for example, the Lugh example you give in your quote is because you have too much to work with, while the Pseudo-Gauls would have far too little, and thus is noteworthy in its reconstructedness. Sorry if I got anything wrong, Mr or Ms Ajax.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that sense, the Gauls would be noteworthy, but as Ajax noted that's actually something of a bonus to us writers, in that we've got a bit more freedom to work with. Myths, legends, folktales, and yes, fantastical reconstructions all have a place in Scion and the modern myths PCs play through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:42:43-07:00","id":463897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463760#post463760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evangeline Walton threw in a very short Appendix highlighting the changes she made or when she made things up. It didn't detract from the books at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, you know, that topic could make for a few good blog posts. I'll keep it under my hat. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T16:45:47-07:00","id":464012,"title":"","content":"You're welcome. <br /> <br /> Really, I'm not asking for anything huge. I'm not talking footnotes or anything. Something like:<br /> <br /> &quot;There really isn't much left to the Gaulish mythology, except for some fascinating artifacts and some vague references in the words of their conquerors. What follows is something built on those foundations.&quot; <br /> <br /> Up to a small sidebar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T06:26:42-07:00","id":491598,"title":"","content":"I konw it was mentioned only in passing, but making a phoenician pantheon might be a curious thing as their religion might be said to be the definition of potpurri pantheon, the way they adopted, bastardized or mashed any and cultural influences they came across in their travels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:53:34-07:00","id":491652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=491598#post491598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I konw it was mentioned only in passing, but making a phoenician pantheon might be a curious thing as their religion might be said to be the definition of potpurri pantheon, the way they adopted, bastardized or mashed any and cultural influences they came across in their travels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh.... Not moreso than lots and lots of other folks (Romans, Hittites, Han LEAP to mind). The vast majority of polytheistic religions typically weren't really as interested in anything like orthodoxy. Ecumenicism was the general rule.<br /> <br /> Which is one of the things that makes setting up a historical pantheon tough. You have to aim for a &quot;core&quot; that never existed in a massive 3D matrix of time and space. Probably 4D with a &quot;cultural interaction&quot; axis. And get a result that is readily recognizable (if the pantheon is one with good modern press) and is, more importantly, FUN!<br /> <br /> I ran the Phoenician pantheon the same way I ran the Roman pantheon. They were largely later iterations of earlier influential/root cultures. Phoencian :: Canaanite as Roman :: Greek. So I just tossed Tanit on the end of Astarte's list of alternate names like Jupiter gets tacked on to Zeus. And made sure Tanit-specific attributes got included in her write-up. It's not a perfect solution, but it worked and it kept things a little more streamlined than otherwise. (Esp. since RAW is not sensitive to chronological change or syncretism.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:34:02-07:00","id":492309,"title":"","content":"What would be more useful, IMHO, would be a system that gave a set of rules/guidelines for writing up pantheons and Gods on your own. That way, you could create your own version of the Hittites, or the Australians, or the Gauls, or anything else, and know how to make them balanced and consistent in 2nd edition rules. It would be easier to provide this to customers, than to try to decide which pantheons should get &quot;official&quot; write-ups. Not to say that I wouldn't like products with new Gods and Goddesses in them - I just think a &quot;build your own&quot; system would eliminate the wait time, and let you put the work into the pantheons you need for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T02:52:48-07:00","id":492471,"title":"","content":"Step 1 in building a Pantheon tends to be &quot;do hours or days of research&quot; which is generally not something very helpful to put in a step-by-step guide. Considering that White Wolf/Onyx Path have never, not once, been able to provide consistent guidelines to create <i>anything</i>, not even <i>characters</i>, I have strong doubts they'll come up with a unified system to codify any and all forms of world mythology into a playable Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T12:12:50-07:00","id":492787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=492471#post492471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that White Wolf/Onyx Path have never, not once, been able to provide consistent guidelines to create <i>anything</i>, not even <i>characters</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Literally every corebook has character creation rules, Telgar. If you don't think we can do it, wait until the Kickstarter and decide for yourself. Or Gen Con, where we'll be talking about all the pantheons.<br /> <br /> I will say that the ten planned pantheons for Hero are core or Companion pantheons from the prior edition, save one new one that was mentioned on the first page of this thread. The other planned ten for God and Demigod have also been mentioned in this thread, and three more have been brought up as part of the stretch goals we've floated as potentials. So...we're on the right track, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 04-26-2015, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:20:30-07:00","id":493021,"title":"","content":"...and I'll be waiting to help you all reach those stretch goals...dammit!<br /> <br /> *nods firmly*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:55:19-07:00","id":494797,"title":"","content":"It might be good in the Companion or a similar book to explore extreme outliers. A real world example would be the gods of Bali. Bali's religion is a syncretic mixture of Hindu/Buddhist/ and Native Animist tropes. The deties might be allied with the Devas, but very distinct. Wiccan aligned members of the Norse, Irish, Greek, and Egyptian, pantheons would also be interesting. However the main focus would be the odd gods in real pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:50:58-07:00","id":495327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=464012#post464012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome. <br /> <br /> Really, I'm not asking for anything huge. I'm not talking footnotes or anything. Something like:<br /> <br /> \u201cThere really isn't much left to the Gaulish mythology, except for some fascinating artifacts and some vague references in the words of their conquerors. What follows is something built on those foundations.\u201d <br /> <br /> Up to a small sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go bigger, dedicating a whole supplement to Lost Pantheons (i.e., Pantheons that pretty much have to be fictional because there's not enough there to do something that isn't). Each would have its own in-setting reason why they're rarely seen or even known within the setting. At the very least, I'd put the Gauls and the Arabians in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T11:06:30-07:00","id":496477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=495327#post495327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go bigger, dedicating a whole supplement to Lost Pantheons (i.e., Pantheons that pretty much have to be fictional because there's not enough there to do something that isn't). Each would have its own in-setting reason why they're rarely seen or even known within the setting. At the very least, I'd put the Gauls and the Arabians in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly an idea. I like the Gauls being a core-ish pantheon as the typical example of a dead pantheon, but we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:26:49-07:00","id":496820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463671#post463671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, given that there will be a caveat in the front of the book warning students from using Scion for their myth and religious studies homework.</div> </div> </div> </div>We both know there will still be countless people who think the information in Scion is an accurate presentation. Back when Scion first got a White Wolf forum, they were overflowing with people who thought that stuff was accurate. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:01:53-07:00","id":496880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=496477#post496477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's certainly an idea. I like the Gauls being a core-ish pantheon as the typical example of a dead pantheon, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yessssssss. Do it. I'm even willing to help by translating the rare texts we have in french on this pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T06:58:21-07:00","id":497420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=496880#post496880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yessssssss. Do it. I'm even willing to help by translating the rare texts we have in french on this pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the Nemetondevos PDF by Bibliotech Interdite, or other French texts? Either way, toss me a PM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:21:53-07:00","id":497798,"title":"","content":"Either way, i'd be happy to help. PM sent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T09:24:01-07:00","id":498990,"title":"","content":"Is it still possible to purchase the Screen/Nemetondevos pdf? If so, I'll still hold with the trust of not passing along the translation I have. If not, I think my hands are untied and I'd be willing to give over, unless the original translator (who shows up from time to time) has issues with it.<br /> <br /> The other French materials I'd hand around freely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:27:22-07:00","id":499392,"title":"","content":"i just looked at drivethrurpg, and sure enough, it's still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:33:03-07:00","id":501894,"title":"","content":"Babylonian definitely. Gilgamesh, Enkidu, Ea, Sin, Inanna, etc... These mythologies were EPIC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3590-silvernale","name":"Silvernale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3590_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:02:04-07:00","id":503110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=496477#post496477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly an idea. I like the Gauls being a core-ish pantheon as the typical example of a dead pantheon, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gaulish Pantheon survived. It became the French National Pantheon and Marianne leads it. Like several other pantheons, they changed their name and upped their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:42:24-07:00","id":503195,"title":"","content":"No. Please don't. Seriously, please don't do that, it would be terrible. It'll cause so many historical connotations and uncomfortable controversies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 05-04-2015, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:57:43-07:00","id":504524,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a pre-monotheistic Hebrew Pantheon, mainly of the Yehweh/Elohim/Baal theory, but willing to see any others. Although I know such a thing probably isn't a good idea in a country as deeply religious as the US, as it's undermining a core tenant of at least two major faiths using their own deity.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I have none that I desperately love to see, I just can't wait to get access to the game and see how my ancestral pantheon (the Tuatha) are presented, as I love the myths and ideas, and want to explore the clashes between the ancient Irish morality and modern morality, and the idea of how a pantheon reacts to being 'censored' when a new religion dominates (please talk about the changes to the Irish myths when Christianity came). I'd like to see more explored with the current pantheons than new ones added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:19:26-07:00","id":504536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=504524#post504524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see a pre-monotheistic Hebrew Pantheon, mainly of the Yehweh/Elohim/Baal theory, but willing to see any others. Although I know such a thing probably isn't a good idea in a country as deeply religious as the US, as it's undermining a core tenant of at least two major faiths using their own deity.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure, myself. I feel it could be done, but it would require finesse and delicacy. Probably a sidebar or two clarifying that these figures are not the deity worshipped in the modern day, who may or may not be His own thing depending on what you and your group is comfortable with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T14:13:52-07:00","id":504619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=504536#post504536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure, myself. I feel it could be done, but it would require finesse and delicacy. Probably a sidebar or two clarifying that these figures are not the deity worshipped in the modern day, who may or may not be His own thing depending on what you and your group is comfortable with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I totally agree, it would have to be very respectful to three current religions, and would have to be one of the best put together (as well as stating the difference between a god and an angel in-pantheon). It's definitely something that should not be thrown in, and should not appear until a good way into the new edition. I just have a problem with the lack of anything Hebrew in the line beyond a Titan who might be the Abrahamic god or may just have 'borrowed' the religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T15:08:08-07:00","id":504671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=504619#post504619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I totally agree, it would have to be very respectful to three current religions, and would have to be one of the best put together (as well as stating the difference between a god and an angel in-pantheon).</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really seem possible, IMHO. Many Christians and Muslims can get antsy when reminded their deity used to be part of a pantheon, and would see reminding them of that fact, even in a game, to be inherently disrespectful, no matter how it was handled. Again, just IMO, and this obviously doesn't apply to all of them, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T15:32:10-07:00","id":504680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=504671#post504671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really seem possible, IMHO. Many Christians and Muslims can get antsy when reminded their deity used to be part of a pantheon, and would see reminding them of that fact, even in a game, to be inherently disrespectful, no matter how it was handled. Again, just IMO, and this obviously doesn't apply to all of them, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it doesn't apply to all of us, but this is the reason I don't expect an official version to turn up. It saddens me, as it basically says that I can't play a Hebrew Scion unless I'm willing to do enough research to amount to a theology degree. As it is, presenting the 'Hebrew Pantheon' is less disrespectful to modern religions than letting people play a Scion of Jesus, while allowing players to keep the idea of a monotheistic god as being a separate figure being the best way to do it (I'd even suggest officially stating that none of the deities in the Pantheon are the monotheistic god, and that their relationship to it is the same as Aten's).<br /> <br /> I'll probably homebrew a version eventually, because I fully expect to hear Word of God along the lines of 'we don't want to risk annoying a large percentage of the US, so IF we do it it'll be a small thing at most'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:25:21-07:00","id":504832,"title":"","content":"I'm not so much interested in a Canaanite Pantheon that\u2019s presented in a way that\u2019s deeply respectful to Christians, Jews, and Muslims as I am in a Canaanite Pantheon that doesn't <i>go out of its way to</i> offend said groups. As the recent shootings in Texas illustrated, some people will take great offense at even minor things like drawing pictures; and even walk on eggshells won't satisfy themi. They're not the target audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:31:28-07:00","id":504858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=504832#post504832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so much interested in a Canaanite Pantheon that\u2019s presented in a way that\u2019s deeply respectful to Christians, Jews, and Muslims as I am in a Canaanite Pantheon that doesn't <i>go out of its way to</i> offend said groups. As the recent shootings in Texas illustrated, some people will take great offense at even minor things like drawing pictures; and even walk on eggshells won't satisfy themi. They're not the target audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the confusion, that's basically how I define respect. There's things I find offensive in Werewolf: the Apocalypse, but I just work around them or ignore them, as many mature people do. Respectful would be pointing out that no, this is not your god. If a book had to go out of it's way to not offend someone then they aren't being respectful to that group, as they're implying that they basically need to be babysat whereas Hindus don't.<br /> <br /> Bare in mind that I live in a fairly non-religious country, so as long as something is not actually intentionally offensive, I regard it as respectful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T05:29:56-07:00","id":505284,"title":"","content":"*nods at what Dataweaver said...*<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that the &quot;Canaanite&quot; pantheon covers the old Hebrew (Habiru..Hapiru?) pantheon well enough. Mentioning that it <i>might</i> apply to current beliefs is probably the likely route.<br /> <br /> Although I'm on the fence about mentioning Islam for the sole reason that it's kinda new and as far Scion goes it might not be relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T05:55:46-07:00","id":505319,"title":"","content":"Maybe if we get a &quot;Further Pantheons&quot; book or something, the Canaanite pantheon could just kinda...be snuck in there, with no mention of modern monotheisms at all. People who want to play Semitic Scions would get their fix, and strict monotheists wouldn't see too much to ruffle their feathers, as the pantheon would simply be presented as a pantheon like every other one, not directly challenging the religious concept of &quot;Yahweh has always been the only god.&quot; Like it's something completely unrelated, unless you know enough to make the association anyway?<br /> <br /> Just spit-balling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T06:59:00-07:00","id":505396,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I'd vastly prefer it if Scion 2e were largely to treat the issues of a Canaanite Pantheon and of how to address the Abrahamic religions as two largely distinct matters, with the only real overlap being \u201cAbrahamic religions option #3: the god of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob is Yahweh of the Canaanite Pantheon\u201d. That is, present the potential connection between the two as one option among many, and not the first or even the second option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:43:21-07:00","id":505465,"title":"","content":"Personally, I wouldn't include him at all, both for out-of-game reasons(he's the most likely to slip into the outright offensive), and the more important in-game reasons, that is, I'm fairly certain he'd end up being slapped with Fatebonds so hard, his grand-Scions would feel it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:09:15-07:00","id":506235,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.bidstrup.com/bible.htm\" target=\"_blank\">This was an old essay</a> I posted before. It remains relevant I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:45:25-07:00","id":506417,"title":"","content":"That article is a perfect example of what <i>not</i> to do. <b>Scion</b> isn't about \u201ca rational, secular historical perspective\u201d, nor is it about trying to establish the truth behind myths and legends; it\u2019s about a world where myths and legends are real. So whatever you think is true about the real-world origins of Christianity is largely irrelevant to <b>Scion</b>\u2019s handling of the subject \u2014 which in turn is only relevant to this thread to the extent that it informs the viability or lack thereof of a Canaanite Pantheon. Unless and until someone suggests including an Abrahamic pantheon (which, thus far, nobody has), it seems to me that more in-depth discussion of how to handle such a thing belongs in the Abrahamic Pantheon thread. <br /> <br /> Heck, even if someone <i>does</i> suggest such a thing, I think the appropriate response is to point to that thread and be done with it: at this point, I can think of almost nothing on the topic that needs to be said that hasn't already been said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-07-2015, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T07:29:17-07:00","id":506746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=506417#post506417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That article is a perfect example of what <i>not</i> to do. <b>Scion</b> isn't about \u201ca rational, secular historical perspective\u201d, nor is it about trying to establish the truth behind myths and legends; it\u2019s about a world where myths and legends are real. So whatever you think is true about the real-world origins of Christianity is largely irrelevant to <b>Scion</b>\u2019s handling of the subject \u2014 which in turn is only relevant to this thread to the extent that it informs the viability or lack thereof of a Canaanite Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right.<br /> <br /> Something important to actually mention is that while we strive to be respectful and accurate in Scion Second Edition, we're not making a scholarly book on mythology. To paraphrase something I wrote before:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you've got a personal stake in this, so take my reassurance that we've done our homework on American pantheons of all stripes and locales, North and South. When we say the Aztec pantheon is returning for the Hero core, we do mean the actual Aztecs, not a less diverse Mesoamerican one. If Huracan doesn't like an Aztec Scion, it's because he thinks Mexico City doesn't deserve the title of tollan and is sore about Chichen Itza (that is an off-the-cuff example; I'm not writing those pantheons). Keep in mind, though, that our foremost goal is a playable and enjoyable mythological game allowing players to embody the myths of legend, wear divine mantles of succession and create their own myths in the vein of old in the modern day whilst being a badass, not arguing about who's God K and who isn't. Accuracy and respect are still very, very high priorities. But if we're looking at Lugh of the Tuatha de Dannen and see the Welsh Lleu Llaw Gyffes and Lugus of the Gauls, there's a judgment call to be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to add to that: we want to treat real-world pantheons, religions, and cultures with the utmost respect and as much accuracy as we can swing. However, we're also treating them through the lens of fiction - and moreover, a lens of fiction where they're all true to some degree or another. It's a work of fiction and a work of game material - nothing more, nothing less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:46:25-07:00","id":507716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=506746#post506746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right.<br /> <br /> Something important to actually mention is that while we strive to be respectful and accurate in Scion Second Edition, we're not making a scholarly book on mythology. To paraphrase something I wrote before:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And to add to that: we want to treat real-world pantheons, religions, and cultures with the utmost respect and as much accuracy as we can swing. However, we're also treating them through the lens of fiction - and moreover, a lens of fiction where they're all true to some degree or another. It's a work of fiction and a work of game material - nothing more, nothing less.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think any reasonable person expects a doctoral thesis in cultural studies or every single mythological story ever. That said, Much of what actually goes into the book affects the default stance of how people play and interpret the game. A sidebar suggesting that the game writeups are just a taste and that people who want more info can read the actual real world stories would be greatly helpful.<br /> <br /> Its probably unfair to assume you guys are going to screw up and be offensive to other religions and cultures and even flatout factually incorrect, but im sure you can see why people are concerned considering how the first book came out. Things like the Aztecs being treated canonically as a strange Religion of Evil where being an Aztec Traditionalist (A choice supported by the game mechanics even) is &quot;Bad&quot; or completely inaccurate things like Thor being good friends with the Dwarves despite mythologically despising them to the point of casual murder.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that if the writers don't understand the traditions/myths of a culture then you A) Find someone who does, or B) Not include them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T08:14:50-07:00","id":508064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=507716#post507716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">r completely inaccurate things like Thor being good friends with the Dwarves despite mythologically despising them to the point of casual murder.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Freyr - &quot;WHY did you smash that dwarf's head with your massive giant-killing hammer at your brother's funeral?&quot;<br /> <br /> Thor - &quot;He was standing in front of me... His head was in the way....&quot;<br /> <br /> Freyr - &quot;He was a DWARF.... that's... just.... not possible.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thor - &quot;Right. He was a dwarf. His head was in the way of my hammer.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T08:35:15-07:00","id":508118,"title":"","content":"You can do a Canaanite pantheon and get all the goodness of Levant religion in a way consistent with how Scion has handled other pantheons without even mentioning Yahweh. He was a peculiarly Hebrew deity and/or he was heavily syncretized with El. El has his own set of issues for those who want to be offended, but he is definitely identified with the larger Canaanite pantheon explicitly in the myths we do have and Yahweh, per se, doesn't appear in those myths (i.e. the Baal Cycle, etc.). (Unless you buy the very very tenuous identification between Yahweh and Yaam, which is kinda hard to do for me.... since Yahweh definitely is portrayed as a dragon-killer type in the Old Testament.... even explicitly says so in Job and it gets more than a nod in a couple of Psalms and Yaam is pretty much a sea dragon). <br /> <br /> In fact, there is very little about Yahweh as a member or associate of the pantheon even in the bits and pieces you can draw from archaeology - a candle stand here that depicts El and Asherah and possible Yahweh (by his absence), a bit of graffitti in the Sinai with Baal, Yahweh and Asherhah all depicted and noted as such with little &quot;name tags&quot;, etc. He would probably rate about as much room in a description of the Canaanite pantheon as, say, Janus, Fevrus, etc. do with a Graeco-Roman pantheon, e.g. a deity of a people who are strongly associated with the pantheon (Latin/Romans) in question, but not one that was a part of the larger-scale and better known core group. The Hebrews definitely were worshiping Asherah, Baal, etc. (which occasioned much gnashing of teeth and fury) but the other Canaanites weren't worshiping him. <br /> <br /> You could just avoid the whole issue altogether by not ever using &quot;yahweh&quot; or just tack it on as &quot;d.b.a&quot; on El and be done with it as far as matters Canaanite go. I'd definitely go for option 1. <br /> <br /> I would love to see a Canaanite pantheon. Hands down. There are some really good stories that aren't super hard to track down that tell myths that can really be associated with the names of the deities in question. It's more than we have for, say, the Slavic pantheon, where it's a sad mash of bits and pieces with a lot of the juicier bits actually sucked up into later Russian fairy tales all layered over with a thick frosting of pure romanticized fiction. <br /> <br /> Oh, and you can also kill two birds with one stone and make it a Canaanite/Phoenician pantheon as well. Very similar to the Graeco-Roman pantheon covering both cultures fairly effectively. Or else end up with the same issues you have trying to pry those two apart. After all, the &quot;-bal&quot; in Hannibal (and Hasdrubal) IS Baal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T09:09:25-07:00","id":508138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=507716#post507716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any reasonable person expects a doctoral thesis in cultural studies or every single mythological story ever. That said, Much of what actually goes into the book affects the default stance of how people play and interpret the game. A sidebar suggesting that the game writeups are just a taste and that people who want more info can read the actual real world stories would be greatly helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan is to have a reading list for each pantheon alongside a more general one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its probably unfair to assume you guys are going to screw up and be offensive to other religions and cultures and even flatout factually incorrect, but im sure you can see why people are concerned considering how the first book came out. Things like the Aztecs being treated canonically as a strange Religion of Evil where being an Aztec Traditionalist (A choice supported by the game mechanics even) is &quot;Bad&quot; or completely inaccurate things like Thor being good friends with the Dwarves despite mythologically despising them to the point of casual murder. </div> </div> </div>Poor Alv\u00edss!<br /> <br /> I will say that if we change things from the myths, I'd vastly prefer it to be because the game needs it to be changed rather than because the research wasn't done.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Put another way, we care more about respect and authenticity for the myths than we do about strict adherence to accuracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would suggest that if the writers don't understand the traditions/myths of a culture then you A) Find someone who does, or B) Not include them. </div> </div> </div>I won't disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-08-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:01:10-07:00","id":509201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463486#post463486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bring it! Take my money please!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been asking them to do that for months. They're not listening. smh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:26:37-07:00","id":509242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=508118#post508118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can do a Canaanite pantheon and get all the goodness of Levant religion in a way consistent with how Scion has handled other pantheons without even mentioning Yahweh. He was a peculiarly Hebrew deity and/or he was heavily syncretized with El. El has his own set of issues for those who want to be offended, but he is definitely identified with the larger Canaanite pantheon explicitly in the myths we do have and Yahweh, per se, doesn't appear in those myths (i.e. the Baal Cycle, etc.). (Unless you buy the very very tenuous identification between Yahweh and Yaam, which is kinda hard to do for me.... since Yahweh definitely is portrayed as a dragon-killer type in the Old Testament.... even explicitly says so in Job and it gets more than a nod in a couple of Psalms and Yaam is pretty much a sea dragon). <br /> <br /> In fact, there is very little about Yahweh as a member or associate of the pantheon even in the bits and pieces you can draw from archaeology - a candle stand here that depicts El and Asherah and possible Yahweh (by his absence), a bit of graffitti in the Sinai with Baal, Yahweh and Asherhah all depicted and noted as such with little &amp;quot;name tags&amp;quot;, etc. He would probably rate about as much room in a description of the Canaanite pantheon as, say, Janus, Fevrus, etc. do with a Graeco-Roman pantheon, e.g. a deity of a people who are strongly associated with the pantheon (Latin/Romans) in question, but not one that was a part of the larger-scale and better known core group. The Hebrews definitely were worshiping Asherah, Baal, etc. (which occasioned much gnashing of teeth and fury) but the other Canaanites weren't worshiping him. <br /> <br /> You could just avoid the whole issue altogether by not ever using &amp;quot;yahweh&amp;quot; or just tack it on as &amp;quot;d.b.a&amp;quot; on El and be done with it as far as matters Canaanite go. I'd definitely go for option 1. <br /> <br /> I would love to see a Canaanite pantheon. Hands down. There are some really good stories that aren't super hard to track down that tell myths that can really be associated with the names of the deities in question. It's more than we have for, say, the Slavic pantheon, where it's a sad mash of bits and pieces with a lot of the juicier bits actually sucked up into later Russian fairy tales all layered over with a thick frosting of pure romanticized fiction. <br /> <br /> Oh, and you can also kill two birds with one stone and make it a Canaanite/Phoenician pantheon as well. Very similar to the Graeco-Roman pantheon covering both cultures fairly effectively. Or else end up with the same issues you have trying to pry those two apart. After all, the &amp;quot;-bal&amp;quot; in Hannibal (and Hasdrubal) IS Baal...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... If they do such the pantheon as a kickstarter reward, I'd gladly survive on bread alone to contribute to the KS <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> do they except pound sterling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T19:18:33-07:00","id":509427,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a Roman Pantheon.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of people would say &quot;There's already the Greek one, they're the same thing&quot;. No, they're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T00:47:40-07:00","id":509722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509427#post509427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a Roman Pantheon.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of people would say &quot;There's already the Greek one, they're the same thing&quot;. No, they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Actually, this might be one for Neall. We know that Zeus, Jupiter, and Tinia are different in how they present, but they're fundamentally the same god, who's mantling different dots of Legend.<br /> <br /> What's not clear is how that impacts the pantheons. Is it something along the lines of the pantheons parallelling the gods, so you've got the same basic group of gods in three distinct configurations (with gods like Mithra only part of the Roman configuration)?<br /> <br /> <br /> (What should be noted is that this only goes so far, when you can see a close family relation. Zeus, Jupiter and Tinia are all the same god, but Zeus, Perun, and Indra are not. Scion isn't suddenly going to become a game where the same gods make up every pantheon under different guises.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T03:17:22-07:00","id":509763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509722#post509722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Actually, this might be one for Neall. We know that Zeus, Jupiter, and Tinia are different in how they present, but they're fundamentally the same god, who's mantling different dots of Legend.<br /> <br /> What's not clear is how that impacts the pantheons. Is it something along the lines of the pantheons parallelling the gods, so you've got the same basic group of gods in three distinct configurations (with gods like Mithra only part of the Roman configuration)?<br /> <br /> <br /> (What should be noted is that this only goes so far, when you can see a close family relation. Zeus, Jupiter and Tinia are all the same god, but Zeus, Perun, and Indra are not. Scion isn't suddenly going to become a game where the same gods make up every pantheon under different guises.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure he is, it's just a different lightning bolt and fake noses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I would love to see rules for different aspects of gods (here used to say different takes on them), so I could have the PCs meet both Lugh and Lleu in a campaign. Possibly guidelines for when it's just going under different names (Odin/Wodin) and when it is a different aspect (Zeus/Jupiter). This should allow one pantheon to cover two or three closely related ones, stopping pantheon bloat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T05:42:36-07:00","id":509811,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the Orishas from Yoruba mythology, the Finnish pantheon, the Korean gods, and the Hawaiian gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T08:31:42-07:00","id":509865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509763#post509763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure he is, it's just a different lightning bolt and fake noses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I would love to see rules for different aspects of gods (here used to say different takes on them), so I could have the PCs meet both Lugh and Lleu in a campaign. Possibly guidelines for when it's just going under different names (Odin/Wodin) and when it is a different aspect (Zeus/Jupiter). This should allow one pantheon to cover two or three closely related ones, stopping pantheon bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...definitely need to see how the rules go.<br /> <br /> Sticking points:<br /> Gods have always existed independently of culture and people. (Bothersome)<br /> <i>Interpretatio </i>could easily have it as &quot;one world one pantheon.&quot; Or at the very least &quot;one geographical region one pantheon.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think this is where I'm suppose to mention North America... <img src=\"http://www.kurts-smilies.de/zahn.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T08:45:27-07:00","id":509872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509865#post509865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...definitely need to see how the rules go.<br /> <br /> Sticking points:<br /> Gods have always existed independently of culture and people. (Bothersome)<br /> <i>Interpretatio </i>could easily have it as &quot;one world one pantheon.&quot; Or at the very least &quot;one geographical region one pantheon.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think this is where I'm suppose to mention North America... <img src=\"http://www.kurts-smilies.de/zahn.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like setting discussion of the Mortal World to be kept Pantheon-neutral, if only so I can easily run a 'the Tuatha are the only gods' campaign or the like. I'm also supportive of keeping the number of Pantheons down, with ones that are generally identical having notes on how to run the separate versions (e.g Greek/Roman, Irish/Welsh, Voodoo/The various African faiths). I'm supportive of 'one people one pantheon', so we don't differentiate the Celtic Pantheons too much, due to them being from the same 'people'.<br /> <br /> Don't worry about me, I'm wearing Relic Armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:05:08-07:00","id":509893,"title":"","content":"Yup... let's get rid of Greek (&amp; Roman &amp; Etruscan... maybe), Norse (&amp; Germanic), Slavic (&amp; Polish), Irish (&amp; Welsh &amp; Gaulish... whatever that is), Hittite, and, while we're at it, all the Vedic Hindu gods and the Persian. We don't need ANY of them, because, they're all the same folks, right? Just &quot;Indo-European&quot;<br /> <br /> There are levels at which conflation becomes useless because, for the most part, most people who want to play the game (the people who will buy the products) aren't interested in playing a Scion of *Perkwunos, since they don't know who the hell that is, there are no myths about him and he's a retcon that didn't exist for anyone at any time. They want to play Scions of Zeus (can't say Jupiter here, since &quot;Jupiter&quot; is just &quot;Zeus-Pater&quot;, with the Latin substituion of /j/ for the Greek /z/, so, nominally, there is no difference between the two and not much in any other way either) or Thor or, Indra, if you want to go a little outside the Zeitgeist - Perun or Teshub or Taranis (I put that in for the lovers of Gaulish, even though he might not have been a thunder god, since we just don't know enough) or... etc.<br /> <br /> It's going to be hard to slice off the Greek from the Roman the way the myths got recorded. The work around might be to have both an Etruscan and Graeco-Roman pantheon, as a lot of the non-Greek analogue gods of Rome are Etruscan. It's not perfect, as some are pure Latin, but those are hard to tease out, so it's a pretty good card toss in a hat and makes for good play without getting too much in the realm of &quot;splitting&quot; over &quot;lumping&quot;. <br /> <br /> If you go &quot;splitter&quot;, you need to chop Etruscan off &quot;Latin&quot; which is separate from Greek. But then you need too start slicing up Greek... Homeric Achaean vs. Classical Greek. Which really is more complicated than that.... since the E. Anatolian versions are different from the Attic ones which are different from the Peloponnesian from the Arcadian from the Boetian... and that's just from the myths, if you go by cultic differences, the variations and potential pantheons start multiplying. And that's not taking into account the Macedonians, the gods in Thessaly, etc. Or what to do with whatever was going down with the Minoans (if we can throw together a Gaulish pantheon, Minoan would probably work as well...). And cultic Achaean wasn't Homeric Achaean either.... <br /> <br /> While interesting on some levels and to some people, it's not really a useful way to handle identifying playable pantheons for a RPG that needs to work within the knowledge base and at the interest level of its players. So there's a &quot;sweet spot&quot; between pantheons that are abstracted to the level of being uninteresting and nearly unplayable.( e.g. besides Sky, what Purviews would *Perkwunos get? Since there aren't and can't be myths that aren't as reconstructed - actually MORE reconstructed, as his name?) and starting to split the hairs to an equally unpalatable and difficult to approach version of exponentiating pantheons on the other side. <br /> <br /> Maybe this &quot;mantle&quot; mechanic will work all this out to a degree that will satisfy most people. I don't know. I haven't seen it and, so far, the vague hints about it aren't enough for me to have any feelings about it other than a potential queasiness. <br /> <br /> I love the term &quot;pantheon bloat&quot;. Consider it stolen. :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:12:06-07:00","id":509895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509427#post509427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a Roman Pantheon.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of people would say &quot;There's already the Greek one, they're the same thing&quot;. No, they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will be some Roman-only Gods, along with Greek-only and maybe one or two Etruscan-only Gods. It depends on how much room we can get for the Theoi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's not clear is how that impacts the pantheons. Is it something along the lines of the pantheons parallelling the gods, so you've got the same basic group of gods in three distinct configurations (with gods like Mithra only part of the Roman configuration)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithra/Mithras can be part of both the Persian and Roman pantheons. They're not divine bloodlines any longer; more like metaphysical and cultural constructs within Fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all seriousness, I would love to see rules for different aspects of gods (here used to say different takes on them), so I could have the PCs meet both Lugh and Lleu in a campaign. Possibly guidelines for when it's just going under different names (Odin/Wodin) and when it is a different aspect (Zeus/Jupiter). This should allow one pantheon to cover two or three closely related ones, stopping pantheon bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fruitful path of setting design, but one that needs to be walked cautiously, lest you accidentally swallow up gods with similar characteristics (like Taranis and Zeus or Taranis and Thor) or who are culturally very different yet have a potentially similar origin (Mitra and Mithra).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-10-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:34:37-07:00","id":509919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509811#post509811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see the Orishas from Yoruba mythology, the Finnish pantheon, the Korean gods, and the Hawaiian gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're getting the Yoruba in the core, with the Loa being a subset of theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:56:47-07:00","id":509971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509895#post509895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There will be some Roman-only Gods, along with Greek-only and maybe one or two Etruscan-only Gods. It depends on how much room we can get for the Theoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I support this fully, the Roman version of the Dodekatheon should be similar, but with enough differences so it isn't just 'the Roman Dodekatheon'. The same with a theoretical Welsh Tuatha (with alternate name provided, if you go this route), and then my knowledge of similar Pantheons runs dry, but I'm sure you can likely find an example for every one in the Corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mithra/Mithras can be part of both the Persian and Roman pantheons. They're not divine bloodlines any longer; more like metaphysical and cultural constructs within Fate. </div> </div> </div>I assumed this was the case in 1e, I must be a bit ahead of the times. Looking forward to seeing how it comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a fruitful path of setting design, but one that needs to be walked cautiously, lest you accidentally swallow up gods with similar characteristics (like Taranis and Zeus or Taranis and Thor) or who are culturally very different yet have a potentially similar origin (Mitra and Mithra). </div> </div> </div>You're the actual Designer, I'm just an amateur, I won't be disappointed if such a thing doesn't appear because I don't understand how much work would have to go into any one element, but this sounds like a lot of research.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that Pantheon-specific purviews or their equivalent are better balanced this time round, I was on another forum where it was pointed out just how underpowered two (Jotunblut and Itzil) are at the Hero level. I'd rather you focused on getting everything right than including as many Pantheons as you can in the core. Just give me an 'expanded Pantheons' book at come point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T10:36:41-07:00","id":509999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509919#post509919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're getting the Yoruba in the core, with the Loa being a subset of theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know. This is good news! Although the Loa should be a separated pantheon. They're rather different from each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:07:00-07:00","id":510029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509895#post509895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There will be some Roman-only Gods, along with Greek-only and maybe one or two Etruscan-only Gods. It depends on how much room we can get for the Theoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, spoilers! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So we now have confirmation that the Greco-Roman Pantheon is called the \u201cTheoi\u201d (which I was hoping would be true, but hadn't yet been confirmed to my knowledge), that similar-yet-slightly-different mythologies such as Greek vs. Roman vs. Etruscan are being handled by a \u201csame Pantheon, different mantles\u201d approach (actually, I think we had already had this part spoiled), and that not every god in a Pantheon needs to have mantles corresponding to every mythology the Pantheon covers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509895#post509895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithra/Mithras can be part of both the Persian and Roman pantheons. They're not divine bloodlines any longer; more like metaphysical and cultural constructs within Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Would this be related to 1e's Fatebinding concept? As I'm envisioning it now, the gods themselves exist regardless of what humanity's beliefs happen to be (that is, they're not parasites or even symbionts that subsist on human worship); but the mantles they wear are <i>definitely</i> shaped by humanity's beliefs \u2014 though I suspect that it's something of a two-way street, in that Scion posits that humanity's mythologies were largely shaped by the actions of the gods. <br /> <br /> This also potentially has implications for scions: if Pantheons are more like metaphysical and cultural constructs within Fate than they are divine bloodlines, then that argues that you don't necessarily have to be part of a divine bloodline to join a Pantheon: being children of the gods might sometimes be figurative rather than literal. If so, it's a development I'm happy to see: chaste gods would have more options open to them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509895#post509895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fruitful path of setting design, but one that needs to be walked cautiously, lest you accidentally swallow up gods with similar characteristics (like Taranis and Zeus or Taranis and Thor) or who are culturally very different yet have a potentially similar origin (Mitra and Mithra).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026and this is an example of where &quot;we deviate from strict mythological accuracy when the game requires it, not because we failed to do the research &quot;? I'm especially encouraged by the acknowledgment of the perils of this approach: for better or worse, nobody can say that you guys don't know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509971#post509971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that Pantheon-specific purviews or their equivalent are better balanced this time round, I was on another forum where it was pointed out just how underpowered two (Jotunblut and Itzil) are at the Hero level. I'd rather you focused on getting everything right than including as many Pantheons as you can in the core. Just give me an 'expanded Pantheons' book at come point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that Pantheon-Specific Purviews or their equivalents will essentially be a case of \u201cyou can tap into a particular metaphysical construct within Fate to achieve supernatural results\u201d. I'm <i>hoping</i> that this also holds true of magic, a difference being that the former relies on you wielding a mantle that's part of that construct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-10-2015, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T13:47:22-07:00","id":510162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=509971#post509971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I support this fully, the Roman version of the Dodekatheon should be similar, but with enough differences so it isn't just 'the Roman Dodekatheon'. The same with a theoretical Welsh Tuatha (with alternate name provided, if you go this route), and then my knowledge of similar Pantheons runs dry, but I'm sure you can likely find an example for every one in the Corebook.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a Welsh &quot;Tuatha&quot; is probably too lumpy for me. Lleu and Lugh are completely different people. They don't have myths in common. They don't do the same things in their myths. They have different parents, tutors, wives, children, births and deaths. They have a similar name and derive from a similar archetype (probably). I could see an argument that Manannan mac Lir and Manawydan fab Llyr are actually the same guy. When he's done in the Mabinogi, Manawydan settles on his own island, and that's pretty much where Mannanan starts out in the legends of the Tuatha. And the Irish gods think of him as being &quot;like us enough to be one of us, but not really a relative per se&quot;. But if the mantles go far enough that you can make someone like Lleu change into someone like Lugh halfway across the Irish Sea on the ferry trip from Angelesey, that's probably too much. And trying to bridge from Nodens to Nyth to Nuada, etc.<br /> <br /> I guess I could buy it if some kind of reincarnation/metempsychosis was built into the way a sort of uber-Celtic pantheon works. Sure, Lleu was Lleu, but he died, And Lugh was Lugh, and he died. But Lugh and Lleu (and Lug) are the same being in the same way that Taliesin was a sword, a tear, a star, a work and a book and Fintan was a man, an eagle, a hawk, a man and a salmon and Etain was a woman, a pool of water, a fly then a woman again. I guess with Celtic weirdness, it doesn't even have to be consecutive, multiple iterations can be active at the same time and be different people who are actually the same person.... that might make the Morrigan make a little more sense. She IS three people Badbh, Macha, Nemain all at once.... But that would be a strange mechanic to put in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 05-10-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:23:07-07:00","id":510259,"title":"","content":"For such a small region (relatively speaking) the UK region is thick with differences in deities. I am particularly fond of the Welsh. But I do concede a lot of overlap and the likelihood that it would be too much to ask to unravel them all for the sake of a game. (ah..Ceridwen and Taliesin...those stories seem too distant too poetic as if another world...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:32:58-07:00","id":510313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=508138#post508138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The plan is to have a reading list for each pantheon alongside a more general one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Poor Alv\u00edss!<br /> <br /> I will say that if we change things from the myths, I'd vastly prefer it to be because the game needs it to be changed rather than because the research wasn't done.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Put another way, we care more about respect and authenticity for the myths than we do about strict adherence to accuracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I won't disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would agree that some mythological realities might need to be edited for consistency and to fit inside the framework of the games. Awesome, consider my fears sated.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:37:10-07:00","id":510330,"title":"","content":"What overlap? In names? The stories of the Children of Don and Llyr don't really bear any resemblence to those of the Tuatha.... The languages of the two were close, but, like Portugese/Spanish close, that's all. Other than that and the fact that the same root culture produced both strands, there aren't really many areas of overlap. Particularly with characters like Taliesin and Ceridwen who don't even have the linguistic analogues like Lleu/Lugh, Bel/Bel (who should be important in both, and isn't), Don/Danu, Llyr/Lir, Nyth/Nuada, Manawydan/Mannanan, Govannan/Goibniu but there are tons of others that don't even vaguely match up The Morrigan, the Dagda, Brigit, etc. vs. Math, Gwydion, Arianrhod, Rhiannon, Gilfaethwy, Bran, Arawn, etc. If anything, the Welsh and the Irish pantheons have less similarities than the Roman and Greeks do. Lumping them together just because they lived on adjacent islands seems somewhat awkward and difficult. The Egyptians were next door to the Canaanites. Directly. By land. They even shared a few gods at certain points (I'm looking at you Reshef and Qadesh) but no one would suggest that the two pantheons should be jury-rigged together. That's a waste of perfectly good mythology for... for what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:48:38-07:00","id":510422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510330#post510330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What overlap? In names? The stories of the Children of Don and Llyr don't really bear any resemblence to those of the Tuatha.... The languages of the two were close, but, like Portugese/Spanish close, that's all. Other than that and the fact that the same root culture produced both strands, there aren't really many areas of overlap. Particularly with characters like Taliesin and Ceridwen who don't even have the linguistic analogues like Lleu/Lugh, Bel/Bel (who should be important in both, and isn't), Don/Danu, Llyr/Lir, Nyth/Nuada, Manawydan/Mannanan, Govannan/Goibniu but there are tons of others that don't even vaguely match up The Morrigan, the Dagda, Brigit, etc. vs. Math, Gwydion, Arianrhod, Rhiannon, Gilfaethwy, Bran, Arawn, etc. If anything, the Welsh and the Irish pantheons have less similarities than the Roman and Greeks do. Lumping them together just because they lived on adjacent islands seems somewhat awkward and difficult. The Egyptians were next door to the Canaanites. Directly. By land. They even shared a few gods at certain points (I'm looking at you Reshef and Qadesh) but no one would suggest that the two pantheons should be jury-rigged together. That's a waste of perfectly good mythology for... for what?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not particularly versed in mythology, so I wouldn't know about the differences. The pantheons may not be a good idea to have them overlap, but as I don't see a Welsh Pantheon arriving soon, a note that the Tuatha can be used to help extrapolate from the myths if needed is an idea. I see the pantheons as thematically related, although I can see from your post that doesn't apply to all, and I'm okay with that. I stopped responding because I realised I'd made a mistake and had nothing constructive to add. Also, in terms of your average player, if I give them the choice between the Irish Gods and Welsh gods, they likely won't see enough difference between the two.<br /> <br /> Also, the easiest way for the Irish (red or black Irish) to reach Ireland would have been through Great Britain.<br /> <br /> Because we seem to have experts on the Mythology of the British Isles here, are Irish and Scottish myths close enough? What about English and Welsh Myths? Is it better to talk about the myths of a specific area of England thanbit as a whole?<br /> <br /> And is it worth having two different Pantheons instead of saying 'mechanically you can change some epic attributes and purviews around and this pantheon will work okay mechanically' (which is not what I intended, but that was due to ignorance). I'm worried that including such a Pantheon would begin the slippery slope to Pantheon bloat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T23:56:25-07:00","id":510483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510422#post510422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about English and Welsh Myths? Is it better to talk about the myths of a specific area of England thanbit as a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can say definitively No, The English are primarily Anglo-Saxons who are a Northern Germanic peoples. They Worshiped Woden (Wotan/Odin) and the rest of the Aesir with little important changes from continental Germany and Scandinavia. People often forget that Beowulf is an English story.<br /> <br /> Terminology is useful here.<br /> <br /> England is the Kingdom created from the Germanic Invasions and populated by Anglo-Saxons (And later during the Viking Age, the Danelaw was created for a time). Wales and Cornwall are the remnants of the ancient Brythonic peoples who were driven out of their original land by Saxons (Tensions still run high on occasion, it was rather brutal).<br /> <br /> The south of Scotland is largely influenced by the Saxons and Viking invasion while the Highlands (Read north) of Scotland are descended from the Picts (Another Brythonic people).<br /> <br /> Ireland is populated by the Irish, a people of argueable ethnic lineage but indisputably Celtic in Culture. Which is no to say that the Picts, Irish, Welsh and Gaels all share the same Religion. At best they belong to two seperate strands of Celtic Culture that is more different than Norwegians and Germans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:45:00-07:00","id":510563,"title":"","content":"Well, I've never seen any similarities in the Welsh &quot;Math&quot; or &quot;Gwydion&quot; as opposed to &quot;D\u00f4n&quot; (Danu; Danube)...Lot of weird going on that really went stranger when the Romans decided to try and take over.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T07:52:54-07:00","id":510652,"title":"","content":"Very slight corrections (I just like talking about history):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510483#post510483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can say definitively No, The English are primarily Anglo-Saxons who are a Northern Germanic peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angles and Saxons (and Jutes, Frisians and Franks) are/were western Germanic, not northern Germanic (though at the time of the invasions, the linguistic differences would have been faaar less than they'd later become). This might be an important distinction, religiously-speaking, because:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They Worshiped Woden (Wotan/Odin) and the rest of the Aesir with little important changes from continental Germany and Scandinavia. </div> </div> </div>The three most striking differences (to me) between western Germanic and northern Germanic religion are:<br /> <br /> 1) The lack of Loki in western traditions, to the best of our knowledge.<br /> <br /> 2) The lack of a definite Ragnarok concept, though this one is a little less certain than the lack of Loki, especially given the theme's far-wider existence as a reflex in so many other Indo-European, not just Germanic, religious cosmologies. IMO, it existed; as support, I point to the continental references to the fires of Muspelhame scorching us all at the end of the world, and archeological material that almost certainly depicts the battles between Thunor and a serpent/dragon and the slaying of Fenris, two kinda important brawls that the Eddas describe as forseen at Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> 3) Most important to me, the lack of the Frigga/Freyja figures in lieu of a single goddess, Frige (whose name obviously looks like Frigga, but is pronounced like Freyja). This one causes the most friction between heathens, IME, to the extent that some Anglo-Saxon types have adopted the Scandinavian form (two separate goddesses), some Scandinavian types have accepted the argument that the division of the figure into two was a somewhat baroque innovation particular to northern cultures relatively late in the game, as displayed in the Eddas and similar material, and the rest of us sometimes just continue to argue about it. :P<br /> <br /> As far as Scion goes, though, these are just academic distinctions; the northern Germanic forms of the mythology are both most familiar and most accessible to your average joe or jane, so they should obviously stay. At least Scion's Thunderer is a redhead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> England is the Kingdom created from the Germanic Invasions and populated by Anglo-Saxons </div> </div> </div>Technically, England the kingdom was established by the west Saxons after Danes had conquered most of the Anglian kingdoms, then been defeated in turn by the House of Wessex. In a way, the Vikings laid the ground-work for Saxon political ascendency (though that certainly wasn't their purpose).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wales and Cornwall are the remnants of the ancient Brythonic peoples who were driven out of their original land by Saxons (Tensions still run high on occasion, it was rather brutal). </div> </div> </div>Eh. I think those accounts are a bit exaggerated. Germanic culture/language/political control certainly dominated in what's now England, but if you look at the genetics (particularly paternal markers, which should demonstrate at least to some degree the extent of expulsion of the Britons), it's still kinda half-Germanic and half-Celtic. I expect the real dividing point was how willing one was to acculturate; those who were unwilling went west, those who were willing stayed and (eventually) became English, if not Angles/Saxons/etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The south of Scotland is largely influenced by the Saxons and Viking invasion while the Highlands (Read north) of Scotland are descended from the Picts (Another Brythonic people). </div> </div> </div>In the south of Scotland, we're talking about Angles, not Saxons. They seem to have made up most of the invasion; the Saxons mostly settled in the south of England (which we call England because there were so many Angles...it's Angle-land).<br /> <br /> In the north of Scotland (though this is a huge oversimplification), Gaels from Ireland subdued/assimilated the Picts, as typified by the folkloric attributes of An Ferbasach being the first king of Scotland through his royal Gaelic descent (paternal) and royal Pictish descent (maternal). But that's generally considered somewhat mythological at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","user":"Morimaruvik","date":". 05-11-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:45:41-07:00","id":510818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510422#post510422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not particularly versed in mythology, so I wouldn't know about the differences. The pantheons may not be a good idea to have them overlap, but as I don't see a Welsh Pantheon arriving soon, a note that the Tuatha can be used to help extrapolate from the myths if needed is an idea. I see the pantheons as thematically related, although I can see from your post that doesn't apply to all, and I'm okay with that. I stopped responding because I realised I'd made a mistake and had nothing constructive to add. Also, in terms of your average player, if I give them the choice between the Irish Gods and Welsh gods, they likely won't see enough difference between the two.<br /> <br /> Also, the easiest way for the Irish (red or black Irish) to reach Ireland would have been through Great Britain.<br /> <br /> Because we seem to have experts on the Mythology of the British Isles here, are Irish and Scottish myths close enough? What about English and Welsh Myths? Is it better to talk about the myths of a specific area of England thanbit as a whole?<br /> <br /> And is it worth having two different Pantheons instead of saying 'mechanically you can change some epic attributes and purviews around and this pantheon will work okay mechanically' (which is not what I intended, but that was due to ignorance). I'm worried that including such a Pantheon would begin the slippery slope to Pantheon bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your players are interested in actually accessing the myths relevant to their pantheon, they will get very very very confused if you conflate the Welsh and Irish myths. As previously stated, characters with very similar names do very different things. If you &quot;statted them up&quot; as potential parents it would be really difficult to pin down what Purviews, Epics and Favored Abilities they would have in common, so just shifting a few things around mechanically won't work out all that well. Lleu Llaw Gyffes and Lugh Samildanach aren't at all the same dude. Lleu's birth to the brother-sister pair of Gwydion &amp; Arianrhod, being gestated in a magic box, training by his dad/uncle, tricking his mother into arming him, marriage to Blodeuwedd, death at the hands of Gronw after satisfying all the weird conditions necessary to killing him doesn't have much to do with Lugh's birth to the daugther of the Fomor king, fosterage and training with Mannanan, heading off to Tara and defeating everyone in everything, etc. etc. The two mythologies have a significantly different &quot;feel&quot; even where they track similar concepts - geasa vs tyngeddau, for example. <br /> <br /> So, yes, this is not a case of pantheon bloat. These are mythologies from two very different groups of people, cultures, etc. Just because they get thrown together under the envelope of &quot;Celtic&quot; doesn't mean they have to have a lot in common. In fact, it's very likely they don't. The split between the two is likely to have been around 1200-800 BC. (Parallel to the time of the Trojan War, the New Kingdom in Egypt, the collapse of the Hittite Empire - emphatically the Bronze Age) So a millenium before the Romans starting messing around in the area. Or 2000+ years of divergence from the time the peoples and their languages separated and we get the first written versions of these myths (11th Century or so for Irish and 14th for Welsh). It's an accident of geography these two groups ended up next to each other. If things had sorted out differently, you might have have had the Irish in Ireland and the &quot;Welsh&quot; myths could have come from, say, Galatia in Turkey (though they would definitely have ended up different... lots of Greek influence, among other things). Which would probably make it easier for people to see how disparate the two actually are. Sure the mythologies influenced each other because of the proximity and I'm not denying that some crossover is valid, and very cool even, like having Manawydan, perhaps, being the younger version of Mannanan, for example. <br /> <br /> And though there might be something to the idea that the Irish got to Ireland through Great Britain, linguistically and archaeologically, there isn't much evidence to support it. Welsh (Cornish/Breton and possibly Pictish) are more closely related to Gaulish (actually proto-Gaulish) from modern France (extending all the way over to Turkey) and Irish/Gaelic are more closely related to the Celtiberian languages of modern Spain. The archaeology and other aspects of culture (from the preserved myths) track this division. So it's more likely that Ireland was settled by Celts from Spain, not France via Great Britain. (And the mythology tracks this. The Milesians or modern Irish mortal folks are from Spain in the Book of Invasions. The Tuatha proper are from the Scythians (!?!?!) via Ireland via the Otherworld via Irelans)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T10:54:43-07:00","id":510889,"title":"","content":"I might have to write Lugh and Lleu as having a friendly but vitriolic rivalry because people keep getting their names and deeds confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T10:56:24-07:00","id":510891,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda torn on the Gaelic/Brythonic thing, but from a gameability POV, I think the Children of D\u00f4n and the Tuatha D\u00e9 should be separate, with the exception of maybe Manann\u00e1n/Manawydan and Lir/Ll\u0177r, because they really do come across as pretty different in the material we have, more than (say) the Dodekatheon at home or in Rome, or the Aesir/Esa. I think this has a lot to do with the longer period of separation between Celtic cultures, as Ajax mentioned.<br /> <br /> This would be assuming, of course, we ever got an official Brythonic pantheon, which unless we get a <i>huge</i> Book o' Pantheons, might not be the most likely thing in the world. :P<br /> <br /> And because I missed it earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510422#post510422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...are Irish and Scottish myths close enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Between Ireland and Gaelic Scotland, sure. Picts, probably not. Angles in southern Scotland and Irish, no. Angles in southern Scotland and Vikings in Ireland, yes, but by the time the Vikings were in Ireland, the Angles were all Christians, at least on paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T12:40:49-07:00","id":511053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510818#post510818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your players are interested in actually accessing the myths relevant to their pantheon, they will get very very very confused if you conflate the Welsh and Irish myths. As previously stated, characters with very similar names do very different things. If you &quot;statted them up&quot; as potential parents it would be really difficult to pin down what Purviews, Epics and Favored Abilities they would have in common, so just shifting a few things around mechanically won't work out all that well. Lleu Llaw Gyffes and Lugh Samildanach aren't at all the same dude. Lleu's birth to the brother-sister pair of Gwydion &amp; Arianrhod, being gestated in a magic box, training by his dad/uncle, tricking his mother into arming him, marriage to Blodeuwedd, death at the hands of Gronw after satisfying all the weird conditions necessary to killing him doesn't have much to do with Lugh's birth to the daugther of the Fomor king, fosterage and training with Mannanan, heading off to Tara and defeating everyone in everything, etc. etc. The two mythologies have a significantly different &quot;feel&quot; even where they track similar concepts - geasa vs tyngeddau, for example.<br /> <br /> So, yes, this is not a case of pantheon bloat. These are mythologies from two very different groups of people, cultures, etc. Just because they get thrown together under the envelope of &quot;Celtic&quot; doesn't mean they have to have a lot in common. In fact, it's very likely they don't. The split between the two is likely to have been around 1200-800 BC. (Parallel to the time of the Trojan War, the New Kingdom in Egypt, the collapse of the Hittite Empire - emphatically the Bronze Age) So a millenium before the Romans starting messing around in the area. Or 2000+ years of divergence from the time the peoples and their languages separated and we get the first written versions of these myths (11th Century or so for Irish and 14th for Welsh). It's an accident of geography these two groups ended up next to each other. If things had sorted out differently, you might have have had the Irish in Ireland and the &quot;Welsh&quot; myths could have come from, say, Galatia in Turkey (though they would definitely have ended up different... lots of Greek influence, among other things). Which would probably make it easier for people to see how disparate the two actually are. Sure the mythologies influenced each other because of the proximity and I'm not denying that some crossover is valid, and very cool even, like having Manawydan, perhaps, being the younger version of Mannanan, for example.<br /> <br /> And though there might be something to the idea that the Irish got to Ireland through Great Britain, linguistically and archaeologically, there isn't much evidence to support it. Welsh (Cornish/Breton and possibly Pictish) are more closely related to Gaulish (actually proto-Gaulish) from modern France (extending all the way over to Turkey) and Irish/Gaelic are more closely related to the Celtiberian languages of modern Spain. The archaeology and other aspects of culture (from the preserved myths) track this division. So it's more likely that Ireland was settled by Celts from Spain, not France via Great Britain. (And the mythology tracks this. The Milesians or modern Irish mortal folks are from Spain in the Book of Invasions. The Tuatha proper are from the Scythians (!?!?!) via Ireland via the Otherworld via Irelans)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't mean to say the Welsh shouldn't be a Pantheon, I just support them being put on hold for a good bit (say, putting them out a year or two into the run), just so as to not confuse players who would be confused. The rest of my post was just probing for information, I was hoping that pretty much all of it was wrong (because the more you know the more you can use).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510889#post510889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have to write Lugh and Lleu as having a friendly but vitriolic rivalry because people keep getting their names and deeds confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for doing so, I hope it gets as big a chuckle as I had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510891#post510891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between Ireland and Gaelic Scotland, sure. Picts, probably not. Angles in southern Scotland and Irish, no. Angles in southern Scotland and Vikings in Ireland, yes, but by the time the Vikings were in Ireland, the Angles were all Christians, at least on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Because I agree with the rest) Part of the problem with the Tuatha is that Ireland had been Christian for long enough by the time the myths were written down that we might as well label them our 'best guess' as the Irish gods. And I'm saying no more on this matter, because I don't know enough, and I have exams to prepare for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:47:33-07:00","id":511106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510891#post510891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda torn on the Gaelic/Brythonic thing, but from a gameability POV, I think the Children of D\u00f4n and the Tuatha D\u00e9 should be separate, with the exception of maybe Manann\u00e1n/Manawydan and Lir/Ll\u0177r, because they really do come across as pretty different in the material we have, more than (say) the Dodekatheon at home or in Rome, or the Aesir/Esa. I think this has a lot to do with the longer period of separation between Celtic cultures, as Ajax mentioned.<br /> <br /> This would be assuming, of course, we ever got an official Brythonic pantheon, which unless we get a <i>huge</i> Book o' Pantheons, might not be the most likely thing in the world. :P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I concur on Mannanan/Manawydan and Llyr. The Children of Don and the Tuatha De (Dannan) however just don't have the same glom-ability. Even though, mythologically they are equivalent to a degree, since Danu = Don is a pretty good equivalency. However, if you &quot;exalt&quot; Danu/Don a little bit and make her akin to a &quot;Good&quot; Titan, The two could definitely have come from similar sources and followed different paths. <br /> <br /> In the books it even says Mannanan is a remnant of a different, older pantheon... so there is even a hook to have Manannan be Manawydan already in place. And the other Childern of Llyr (well, actually of Penarddun)... well they didn't end up in such good places (Bran's dead-ish head buried under Tower Hill in London, Branwen dead from a broken heart when Efnisien killed her son, 1/2 brother Efnisien dead when he broke the cauldron that resurrected the dead by jumping into it alive, so you have Manawydan and Nisien left and that's a maybe for Nisien) , so Mannanan and Rhiannon went off west and settled on the Isle of Man. Rhiannon went away at some point for some reason (unless you want Fan to be the name she goes by when she's talking to Irish folks). In fact, Manawydan even WENT to Ireland in the Second Branch of the Mabinogion, though he left it a wasteland....So maybe he's trying to make up for the genocide?<br /> <br /> I had a Welsh Scion in one of our games. A daughter of Gwydion. I finally settled on the relatively made-up name &quot;Dau Tylwyth&quot; or &quot;Two Families&quot; for the pantheon. The two families being the Children of Don and Children of Llyr (who are actually related.... Don's husband is Llyr's wife's father). I also picked &quot;Tylwyth&quot; for the Tywyth Teg, the Welsh version of the Aos Si or Sidhe. Probably should have found a way to make it &quot;the two great families&quot; or something, but my Welsh gets strained. I structured out a PSP called &quot;Galanas&quot; which was sort of a variant on Enech, only not. <br /> <br /> Really, the Irish gods and the Welsh gods are equally lacking in press, so the toss up goes to the fact that people are more familiar with Ireland than they are with Wales. So it really comes down to who has the better tourist bureau....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:29:01-07:00","id":511125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510652#post510652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Angles and Saxons (and Jutes, Frisians and Franks) are/were western Germanic, not northern Germanic (though at the time of the invasions, the linguistic differences would have been faaar less than they'd later become). This might be an important distinction, religiously-speaking, because:</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats True Generally Speaking, But I was making an effort not to confuse people with where ancient peoples lived and their associations. West European might be construed as Celtic to those not familiar with ancient migration patterns and I wanted to avoid that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The three most striking differences (to me) between western Germanic and northern Germanic religion are:<br /> <br /> 1) The lack of Loki in western traditions, to the best of our knowledge.<br /> <br /> 2) The lack of a definite Ragnarok concept, though this one is a little less certain than the lack of Loki, especially given the theme's far-wider existence as a reflex in so many other Indo-European, not just Germanic, religious cosmologies. IMO, it existed; as support, I point to the continental references to the fires of Muspelhame scorching us all at the end of the world, and archeological material that almost certainly depicts the battles between Thunor and a serpent/dragon and the slaying of Fenris, two kinda important brawls that the Eddas describe as forseen at Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> 3) Most important to me, the lack of the Frigga/Freyja figures in lieu of a single goddess, Frige (whose name obviously looks like Frigga, but is pronounced like Freyja). This one causes the most friction between heathens, IME, to the extent that some Anglo-Saxon types have adopted the Scandinavian form (two separate goddesses), some Scandinavian types have accepted the argument that the division of the figure into two was a somewhat baroque innovation particular to northern cultures relatively late in the game, as displayed in the Eddas and similar material, and the rest of us sometimes just continue to argue about it. :P </div> </div> </div>Aside from #3 (Which I prefer as a Single person using a Kenning to signify their present Role, similar to the Greeks and using names like Pallas Athena or Phobos Apollo, as even in the Norse myths they share items and their are some hints that they are one person) these are all things that are simply missing but not contradictory. Given the more incomplete Continental Germanic records of the Myths, its reasonable to assume that the things we find in the more complete Norse versions were lost but not originally absent. Things like a lack of Loki could be explained with thet fact that (Despite modern cultural insistence) Loki was not a God and there is no evidence that he was ever worshiped period. No place names or cults or temples, nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technically, England the kingdom was established by the west Saxons after Danes had conquered most of the Anglian kingdoms, then been defeated in turn by the House of Wessex. In a way, the Vikings laid the ground-work for Saxon political ascendency (though that certainly wasn't their purpose). </div> </div> </div>While thats true, I don't think it really counters my point. The nation of England was established by the Anglo-Saxons with some non insignificant influence from the Norse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh. I think those accounts are a bit exaggerated. Germanic culture/language/political control certainly dominated in what's now England, but if you look at the genetics (particularly paternal markers, which should demonstrate at least to some degree the extent of expulsion of the Britons), it's still kinda half-Germanic and half-Celtic. I expect the real dividing point was how willing one was to acculturate; those who were unwilling went west, those who were willing stayed and (eventually) became English, if not Angles/Saxons/etc. </div> </div> </div>That is quite arguable. Evidence from ancient laws shows that Celts were treated as second class citizens in comparison to the Saxons (The same can be said of Romans in provinces that the Germanic tribes conquered, such as Frankia), and research goes back and forth over how much Germanic Paternity is present, it is (Mostly, the areas around wales and Cornwall are the exception) anywhere from 50-100%. <a href=\"http://rspb.royalsocietypublishing.org/content/273/1601/2651\" target=\"_blank\">http://rspb.royalsocietypublishing.o.../273/1601/2651</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the south of Scotland, we're talking about Angles, not Saxons. They seem to have made up most of the invasion; the Saxons mostly settled in the south of England (which we call England because there were so many Angles...it's Angle-land). </div> </div> </div>I just didin't want to Type out Anglo-Saxons :P But yes, thats true.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:00:05-07:00","id":511187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511125#post511125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aside from #3 (Which I prefer as a Single person using a Kenning to signify their present Role, similar to the Greeks and using names like Pallas Athena or Phobos Apollo, as even in the Norse myths they share items and their are some hints that they are one person) these are all things that are simply missing but not contradictory. Given the more incomplete Continental Germanic records of the Myths, its reasonable to assume that the things we find in the more complete Norse versions were lost but not originally absent. Things like a lack of Loki could be explained with thet fact that (Despite modern cultural insistence) Loki was not a God and there is no evidence that he was ever worshiped period. No place names or cults or temples, nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really disagree, though I'm glad to find someone else who agrees about Frige (and the oddness of modern Lokeans, no offence to Loki-followers). I'm one of the less-Norse types that believes the Ragnarok stories were simply lost in western Germanic cultures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is quite arguable. Evidence from ancient laws shows that Celts were treated as second class citizens in comparison to the Saxons (The same can be said of Romans in provinces that the Germanic tribes conquered, such as Frankia), and research goes back and forth over how much Germanic Paternity is present, it is (Mostly, the areas around wales and Cornwall are the exception) anywhere from 50-100%. </div> </div> </div>It's all arguable. Rather than digress into the argument of it, though, I'll simply ask that you do an image search for &quot;R1b U106&quot; (very obviously Germanic) and &quot;R1b L-21&quot; (similarly obviously insular Celtic). They both kinda bleed over each in England (and Scotland), which is why my current conclusion regarding the matter stands as it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just didin't want to Type out Anglo-Saxons :P But yes, thats true. </div> </div> </div>Lol. Fair enough. Sorry for quibbling overly much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:02:35-07:00","id":511189,"title":"","content":"On the topic of Roman Gods: Many people equate Mars to Ares without realizing that they're really not alike. Ares is a god of war. He's into bloodlust, conflict and shit-disturbing. Mars is an agricultural god, grandfather of the founders of Rome - War is attributed to him because he was viewed as a protector of the Roman people rather than a warrior. He's more of a general than a soldier. His is more the <i>art</i> of war and warfare rather than actual combat. In his Mars Sylvanus aspect he's seen as a protector of farmlands, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:37:12-07:00","id":511245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511189#post511189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of Roman Gods: Many people equate Mars to Ares without realizing that they're really not alike. Ares is a god of war. He's into bloodlust, conflict and shit-disturbing. Mars is an agricultural god, grandfather of the founders of Rome - War is attributed to him because he was viewed as a protector of the Roman people rather than a warrior. He's more of a general than a soldier. His is more the <i>art</i> of war and warfare rather than actual combat. In his Mars Sylvanus aspect he's seen as a protector of farmlands, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this topic, the same can be applied to Thor, who was as much a god of agriculture as a god of war (because he's a weather god). I think there needs to be a bit of give into the popular conceptions, but Mars as an agricultural god just sounds too good to ignore (make his Associated Powers include Intelligence, Fertility, and War). I'm interested what the powers for a 1e Roman Dodekatheon would be (instead of the 2e Theoi, because we don't have the 2e mechanics), would Mars have a profile like the following:<br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Dexterity, Epic Intelligence/Perception, Arete, Fertility, War<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Athletics, Command, Fortitude, Melee, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> I tried to focus it more towards agriculture than war on the abilities front, but let me know if anything doesn't fit Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:12:30-07:00","id":511281,"title":"","content":"The discussion about the Celtic deities made me think of the Loa Maman Brigitte (the wife of Baron Samedi and only white Loa that I know of), associated with Saint Brigit, who was herself syncretised with Brigid from the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tuatha. <br /> Would she be counted as being both a Loa and a Tuatha or would Maman Brigitte and Brigid be two different deities?<br /> Will there be a general rule for such cases?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:51:04-07:00","id":511307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511281#post511281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would she be counted as being both a Loa and a Tuatha or would Maman Brigitte and Brigid be two different deities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantles of the same deity, I would think/hope/argue. She's very well-traveled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:53:21-07:00","id":511308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511189#post511189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of Roman Gods: Many people equate Mars to Ares without realizing that they're really not alike. Ares is a god of war. He's into bloodlust, conflict and shit-disturbing. Mars is an agricultural god, grandfather of the founders of Rome - War is attributed to him because he was viewed as a protector of the Roman people rather than a warrior. He's more of a general than a soldier. His is more the <i>art</i> of war and warfare rather than actual combat. In his Mars Sylvanus aspect he's seen as a protector of farmlands, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wellll..... it's not so easy to just separate out the two. In Athens, the place were sober judgments were made in accordance with law and traditions were on the Areopagus, most sacred to Ares. So he's not all bloodlust and plunder in Attic mythology and it's there and in the Iliad where Ares gets his &quot;spoiled bad boy&quot; image. And Mars certainly has a young savage aspect who wanders around in the woods and kills for fun, beyond Mars Silvanus to Mars Ferus and that's not from a post-syncretization standpoint, Mars Ferus is associated with the whole &quot;suckling wolf taking care of his kids&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:38:12-07:00","id":511347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511245#post511245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On this topic, the same can be applied to Thor, who was as much a god of agriculture as a god of war (because he's a weather god).</div> </div> </div> </div>Germanic myth gets incredibly confusing when you attempt to apply Greek Categorical thinking to it. Thor is not &quot;The God of Thunder&quot; or Odin &quot;The God of War&quot;. Thor is Thor, he happens to do thunder things, but also other stuff. They don't have strict categorizations like the Greeks had.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:58:46-07:00","id":511380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511347#post511347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Germanic myth gets incredibly confusing when you attempt to apply Greek Categorical thinking to it. Thor is not &amp;quot;The God of Thunder&amp;quot; or Odin &amp;quot;The God of War&amp;quot;. Thor is Thor, he happens to do thunder things, but also other stuff. They don't have strict categorizations like the Greeks had.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a game, we have to categorise, but we can cheat. We can easily get two things out of Thor, thunder/lightning and being like Thor. Thus we can say that Odin's godly categories are e.g. leadership, wisdom, and being like Odin. Think of it less as 'god of thunder' and more 'god associated with thunder'. I only used the example because I know it.<br /> <br /> The problem with Thor's only defining feature being Thor is that I know someone who, upon discovering this, will go straight for wenches and mead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T18:41:20-07:00","id":511402,"title":"","content":"It depends on the mechanics of the new edition, in 1E it wasn't really possible, but lots of different myth systems weren't (especially non binary Heavens-Underworld systems) which I think they realized and are trying to change.<br /> <br /> Whats wrong with Wenches and Mead? Sounds like something most scions of Thor would jump all over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T20:07:41-07:00","id":511487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511347#post511347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Germanic myth gets incredibly confusing when you attempt to apply Greek Categorical thinking to it. Thor is not &quot;The God of Thunder&quot; or Odin &quot;The God of War&quot;. Thor is Thor, he happens to do thunder things, but also other stuff. They don't have strict categorizations like the Greeks had.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Neither did the Greeks. That's more Bullfinch and D'Aulaire and Deities and Demigods than it has anything to do with cultic practice or how they are portrayed in the various myths. Some of the Greek gods had definite jobs, like &quot;King&quot; or &quot;Herald&quot; but what they were gods of were very fuzzy around a sort of vague center. Artemis in the Iliad vs. Artemis as worshiped by the Spartans vs. Artemis of the Temple at Ephesus vs. Etc. The last of those is so out there from the rest that it seems like it would be hard to handle that via something like a &quot;mantle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T20:11:14-07:00","id":511490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511402#post511402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the mechanics of the new edition, in 1E it wasn't really possible, but lots of different myth systems weren't (especially non binary Heavens-Underworld systems) which I think they realized and are trying to change.<br /> <br /> Whats wrong with Wenches and Mead? Sounds like something most scions of Thor would jump all over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends on the Scion, but in my experience as a player of a Scion of Thor (one of my fav characters of all time) and GMing both NPC and PC Scions of Thor in various and sundry chronicles, most would be cool with the wenches and mead. Sons and daughters both. I'm sure there are some glum, un-fun Scions of Thor out there. It takes all kinds. (My Scion of Thor was rendered permanently deaf during his Visitation and he was STILL a pretty fun guy overall...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:08:28-07:00","id":511670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511490#post511490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably depends on the Scion, but in my experience as a player of a Scion of Thor (one of my fav characters of all time) and GMing both NPC and PC Scions of Thor in various and sundry chronicles, most would be cool with the wenches and mead. Sons and daughters both. I'm sure there are some glum, un-fun Scions of Thor out there. It takes all kinds. (My Scion of Thor was rendered permanently deaf during his Visitation and he was STILL a pretty fun guy overall...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I mean its probably something you might wanna talk over with your table if someone has some kind of objection and Scions are still individuals, but generally speaking thats basically the halls of the Aesir in a nutshell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T00:42:23-07:00","id":511764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511490#post511490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably depends on the Scion, but in my experience as a player of a Scion of Thor (one of my fav characters of all time) and GMing both NPC and PC Scions of Thor in various and sundry chronicles, most would be cool with the wenches and mead. Sons and daughters both. I'm sure there are some glum, un-fun Scions of Thor out there. It takes all kinds. (My Scion of Thor was rendered permanently deaf during his Visitation and he was STILL a pretty fun guy overall...).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511670#post511670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, I mean its probably something you might wanna talk over with your table if someone has some kind of objection and Scions are still individuals, but generally speaking thats basically the halls of the Aesir in a nutshell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant to imply that they'd miss the rest of Thor, especially because it's more of the Asier's theme than Thor's.<br /> <br /> And I know want to play a Scion of the Dagda all about Wenches and Whiskey....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:47:40-07:00","id":512072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511764#post511764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, I meant to imply that they'd miss the rest of Thor, especially because it's more of the Asier's theme than Thor's.<br /> <br /> And I know want to play a Scion of the Dagda all about Wenches and Whiskey....</div> </div> </div> </div>And having a bad-ass killer harp....<br /> <br /> Though whiskey was probably not around in his salad days (who knows what wonderful alcohols the have in Tir nan Og?), I'm sure he was very enthusiastic about it once it arrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:07:28-07:00","id":512920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511189#post511189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of Roman Gods: Many people equate Mars to Ares without realizing that they're really not alike. Ares is a god of war. He's into bloodlust, conflict and shit-disturbing. Mars is an agricultural god, grandfather of the founders of Rome - War is attributed to him because he was viewed as a protector of the Roman people rather than a warrior. He's more of a general than a soldier. His is more the <i>art</i> of war and warfare rather than actual combat. In his Mars Sylvanus aspect he's seen as a protector of farmlands, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, Mars is really more of a God of Adult Male Social Roles. Ares is the lord of Battle Lust. He shares certain traits with Odin. Berserkers would make sense in Archaic Greece, and some scholars think Centaurs were really a form of Berserk or War Shaman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:03:35-07:00","id":513191,"title":"","content":"It might interest you to know that the new <b>Origins </b>book cover signature character (the redhaired lady in the library, on the front page of the main Scion site) is a Scion of The Dagda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T13:05:42-07:00","id":513253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=511307#post511307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mantles of the same deity, I would think/hope/argue. She's very well-traveled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't discussed it with the Yoruba writer, but deities can indeed be in multiple pantheons, so I suppose it's not out of the realm of possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T13:50:58-07:00","id":513272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513253#post513253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't discussed it with the Yoruba writer, but deities can indeed be in multiple pantheons, so I suppose it's not out of the realm of possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it, then, that Virtues are either not a thing anymore or they\u2019re no longer hardwired to your Pantheon? Because in 1e, the Loa Virtues had little in common with the Tuatha de Danaan Virtues; if Virtues worked like they did in 1e, Maman Brigitte/Brigid/Saint Brigit would have a serious personality disorder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:48:16-07:00","id":513335,"title":"","content":"They're no longer entirely hardwired to pantheon, as pantheon can be a fluid thing at times and isn't fixed (though it's not softwired, either).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:16:55-07:00","id":513480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=512920#post512920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He shares certain traits with Odin. Berserkers would make sense in Archaic Greece, and some scholars think Centaurs were really a form of Berserk or War Shaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf Berserkers are basically canon to Achaean Greece as a historically accurate fighting style, and even makes an appearance in Homer in a most unexpected place:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hungry as wolves that rend and bolt raw flesh,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">hearts filled with battle-frenzy that never dies\u2014</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">off on the cliffs, ripping apart some big antlered stag</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">they gorge on the kill till all their jaws drip red with blood,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">then down in a pack they lope to a pooling, dark spring,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">their lean sharp tongues lapping the water\u2019s surface,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">belching bloody meat, but the fury, never shaken,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">builds inside their chests though their glutted bellies burst\u2014</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> so wild the Myrmidon captains...</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:48:10-07:00","id":513511,"title":"","content":"It's pretty well accepted that the various Indo-European werewolf mythologies descend from the memory of (Proto-Indo-European on) warbands that held the wolf as a totem and saw manifesting it as a mark of initiation. In some cultures, like the Hellenic peoples, this gradually became unacceptable as civilisation progressed (probably most famously remembered in the tale of Lycaon); in others, like Germanic cultures, it held on until Christianity took over and called it devilry (less than a thousand years ago, in some places; probably most famously remembered by its cousin, bear-shirting). In almost all cases, it continued to lurk in the psyche of the various peoples (which is why we have things like werewolf games). :P<br /> <br /> The wolf was so important to our (linguistic, for those of you who aren't Germanic) ancestors that we don't even call it by name...&quot;wolf&quot; is an example of taboo deformation, wherein something is so holy/respected/feared/adored that a euphemism is used to refer to it in common parlance instead of the actual term for the thing.<br /> <br /> No relevance to Scion, but the previous post made me think of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:10:27-07:00","id":513551,"title":"","content":"Where would Shakespear's supernatural creations fit into the Scion mythology? Oberon, Titania, Puck, Queen Mab, Ariel, Hecate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:14:04-07:00","id":513664,"title":"","content":"A fictional Pantheon, like the Guardians of Childhood (Santa Claus, the Easter Bunny, the Tooth Fairy, Jack Frost, etc.) I wouldn't mind a \u201cbook of fables\u201d or something of the sort somewhere down the line that addresses such things; but I'd rather the initial wave, at least, to remain focused on mythologies that real people and cultures <i>actually believed</i> at some point or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T21:27:25-07:00","id":513767,"title":"","content":"Hecate is a Greek Goddess, not a creation of Shakespeare. <br /> <br /> More modern figures are pretty easy to explain as simply being re-interpretations (<i>by mortals</i>) of older figures. There may not actually be anyone anything like Santa Claus. Why would there be, when mythic creatures have been absent from the world for hundreds or thousands of years? Ditto Tooth Fairy, Jack Frost, etc. Now, it would be easy for a fae, elemental or nature spirit to slip into the role of Jack Frost, Johnny Appleseed or whatever, but it isn't necessarily that mortal perceptions <i>caused </i>that to happen. Instead it'd be an example of the vast power of human imagination to take something that once was real, and change the stories of it to suit the times. That power does not need to <i>actually affect</i> the mythological figures involved, though. Hades isn't the Greek Devil, no matter how amazing James Woods was in the Disney movie. <br /> <br /> I'm stilly truly hoping that at it's core, Scion will remain a game about <i>mythology</i> instead of an urban fantasy kitchen sink like Dresden Files, Supernatural or Grimm. Those are all great series (ok, maybe not GREAT... Supernatural...) but they're not about <i>mythology</i>. Even American Gods is about <i>modern</i> mythology clashing with the old ones. It's a setting where mythological figures <i>do</i> get their power, their very existence, from the stories, prayers and beliefs of humanity. So is The Iron Druid Chronicles. That's a really cool idea... but it isn't how the ancients ever thought of anything. Zeus didn't exist to the Athenians because they <i>believed</i> in him. He existed because <i>he existed</i>. He was <i>real</i>. If they stopped worshipping him <i>he would smite them</i>, not lose power. <br /> <br /> Truly and really, I appreciate the idea of wanting to use a system you enjoy to play every kind of folklore creature. But there are <i>tons</i> of systems that do that <i>really, really well</i>. There are not tons of systems that just do mythology. Scion 2E might actually do that. Is it limiting to say that Scion should just be about religions instead of fairytales and folklore? Yeaaah. But, then, it's limiting to say that Vampire: the Masquerade should be about playing vampires. <br /> <br /> Now, I do want to point out that I went through the WW2 Pantheons and converted every single figure in them into something that actually <i>fits</i> into Scion. John Henry was a Scion of Hercules who died before reaching Legend 2. He's now a ghostly Guide to other Greek Scions. Betsy Ross was a woman who was granted immortality by a Colonial-era Scion using the Health Purivew, or a Relic. The Citizen is a very powerful ghost who acts a Guide to Russian Scions, possessing mortal soldiers to fulfill his duty to the Motherland. Paul Bunyan is a Jotun who broke free of the Titans' influence. Pecos Bill is a Demigod Scion. Rosie the Riveter is an Avatar of Bridget. Robin Hood is a Demigod. Madame Gullotine is an Avatar of Andarta. It's actually pretty easy to convert that sort of figure into a Scion-friendly form. They just won't be on the same level as Zeus or Odin. That's fine. They shouldn't be. Neither should Santa or the Tooth Fairy. They can still fit, but they should fit into the mythological framework. The framework shouldn't be warped to fit <i>them</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T21:59:54-07:00","id":513795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513767#post513767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecate is a Greek Goddess, not a creation of Shakespeare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hecate is one of those slightly primordial gods that may have been around longer than Zeus and the gang right? Would that maker her more of a Titan? I don't really know how Scion has handled those &quot;older&quot; gods in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513767#post513767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm stilly truly hoping that at it's core, Scion will remain a game about <i>mythology</i> instead of an urban fantasy kitchen sink like Dresden Files, Supernatural or Grimm. Those are all great series (ok, maybe not GREAT... Supernatural...) but they're not about <i>mythology</i>. Even American Gods is about <i>modern</i> mythology clashing with the old ones. It's a setting where mythological figures <i>do</i> get their power, their very existence, from the stories, prayers and beliefs of humanity. So is The Iron Druid Chronicles. That's a really cool idea... but it isn't how the ancients ever thought of anything. Zeus didn't exist to the Athenians because they <i>believed</i> in him. He existed because <i>he existed</i>. He was <i>real</i>. If they stopped worshipping him <i>he would smite them</i>, not lose power.<br /> <br /> Truly and really, I appreciate the idea of wanting to use a system you enjoy to play every kind of folklore creature. But there are <i>tons</i> of systems that do that <i>really, really well</i>. There are not tons of systems that just do mythology. Scion 2E might actually do that. Is it limiting to say that Scion should just be about religions instead of fairytales and folklore? Yeaaah. But, then, it's limiting to say that Vampire: the Masquerade should be about playing vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only half agree on this part, I think folklore is pretty intrinsically tied to mythology. I don't mind seeing werewolves, vampires, leprechauns, and bigfoot in Scion...so long as they give these creatures a logic or origin that works withing the main mythic themes of Scion. Look to something like Hellboy for a good example of how to do this, everything from fairies, to hollow earth mole men, to King Arthur, and extra dimensional horrors share a cosmology and common logic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T22:42:21-07:00","id":513838,"title":"","content":"Telgar: you have my apology; I forgot to attach a disclaimer to my \u201cbook of fables\u201d notion that such a book ought to be a Shard \u2014 a sort of \u201cwhat if you want to do something like <b>Scion</b>, but with folklore instead of mythology? Here\u2019s how\u2026\u201d <br /> <br /> That said, it\u2019s looking like 2e\u2019s framework is going to be far more open than 1e\u2019s was; so the amount of contorting needed to fit folklore, fables, and fairy tales into said framework will be less than it would have been in 1e, and might even be negligible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T23:21:34-07:00","id":513872,"title":"","content":"I think <i>Some</i> folklore is perfectly fine for any Scion game but it depends on how you handle it as most folklore is basically just a de-paganised version of ancient creatures, social customs or beliefs. Werewolves are pretty easy to reconcile with the Aesir, Just about every culture has their own vampire myth, Leprechauns and Fae are overtly Celtic and already have mythological positions, ETC.<br /> <br /> Some of the latter &quot;Story book&quot; Tales would probably require lots of research and/or enough change to make them more or less unidentifiable from their starting point to fit into the setting of &quot;All Gods everywhere actually exist&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, im sure certain alternate settings of Scion could handle it quite fine, Scion: Origins is basically Urban Fantasy by default, But it needs to be an alternate setting and not try to fit it into the Actual Mythological setting of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T04:37:52-07:00","id":514027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513795#post513795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hecate is one of those slightly primordial gods that may have been around longer than Zeus and the gang right? Would that maker her more of a Titan? I don't really know how Scion has handled those &quot;older&quot; gods in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, those primordial deities weren't handled too well. The deities were either mentioned and placed on the side opposing the godly order, or they weren't mentioned at all. Which is a shame really. Hecate was one of those that was less about the pantheon's fight for it's version of structured order, and far more about caring for the human race.<br /> <br /> As for characters out of folklore, I'm fond of the notion that such is the human race's attempt at creating more deities of a minor sort relevant to a particular culture. (Pecos Bill is definitely a cowboy)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T06:23:18-07:00","id":514074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513767#post513767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even American Gods is about <i>modern</i> mythology clashing with the old ones. It's a setting where mythological figures <i>do</i> get their power, their very existence, from the stories, prayers and beliefs of humanity. So is The Iron Druid Chronicles. That's a really cool idea... but it isn't how the ancients ever thought of anything. Zeus didn't exist to the Athenians because they <i>believed</i> in him. He existed because <i>he existed</i>. He was <i>real</i>. If they stopped worshipping him <i>he would smite them</i>, not lose power.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a line to be drawn, but note that American Gods itself includes Buile Suibhne, kobolds, pixies and sprites. The line between mythology and folklore is blurry, not distinct. <b>Scion 2e</b> will sit pretty firmly on the mythological side, but don't be surprised if Baba Yaga rolls up (she even gets mentioned on a roll of Slavic gods, which goes to show you how indistinct the line can be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:51:55-07:00","id":514184,"title":"","content":"What I found kind of cool about Scion was the idea that, as Telgar said, Zeus exists because he exists, not because he was believed in. But, on the other hand, it's been a long time since he was a major power in the world what with the withdrawal of the gods (for the most part, and for their own reasons). A large part of Scion's coolness to me was that the gods were going to come back into the public consciousness, yes, but they would have to do so in a way that remained relevant. Because the rampages that many of them were famous for when they didn't get their way just isn't possible in modern day Scion. Back in the old days it was fine if Zeus wanted to smush Athens into putty. Odin and Horus would all be sitting back going 'Dude wants to blow up his own house what's it to me?'. Now, though, the world is so interspersed and intermixed. When Zeus wanst to throw a hissy fit to get (what he thinks of as) his rightful dues in downtown New York he can't just throw lightning all over the place without half a dozen other pantheons wanting to intervene because it's not just Greeks down there. Gods, in order to get the worship (or at least the respect) they want from a fairly jaded populace are going to have to adapt the way they do things to prevent being ignored by the people or checked by other gods in a mixed world.<br /> <br /> The folklore vs mythology thing has a line down the middle. It's a hard thin line in some places and broad and fuzzy in other places. Certainly I would have to oppose the idea of, say, Pecos Bill existing because mortals believe in him. But a crafty supernatural entity taking on the role to feed off that belief for their own ends (glory, worship, attention, what ever) and pretending that it was them the whole time (&quot;Well, son, I've always been here. Y'all just ain't needed my help for a while is all.&quot;) isn't that hard an idea to sell. Not saying that you need to assign every folklore hero a role (one of the things that always cheesed me off about oWoD is their notion that every major figure in the history of ever was secretly a supernatural creature of some kind) but it's certainly not inconcievable that it would happen. They don't need to be gods in their own right (and why would they be if gods have to be born, not believed into existance) or even Scions. Lots of creatures have a good reason to take on the role.<br /> <br /> Of course for a giggle imagine a Scion of Odin staring slack jawed when he finds out that for fun and games Odin likes to play Santa Claus every so often and they catch dear ol' dour, serious, stuffy, dad in his jolly outfit sneaking toys to kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:01:21-07:00","id":514195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513551#post513551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would Shakespear's supernatural creations fit into the Scion mythology? Oberon, Titania, Puck, Queen Mab, Ariel, Hecate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hecate was an actual goddess widely worshipped in ancient Anatolia and Greece, Titania is an alternate name for Roman Dianna and Shakespeare clearly says she is worshiped as a goddess, Oberon was an ancient spirit know in the German lands, perhaps worshiped as a god. Queen Mab is a form of Maeve, and some think she was a member of the Celtic pantheon. Puck and Ariel are both powerful Lesser Immortals, Puck is a powerful enough Lesser Immortal that any Scion should be very polite to him and avoid irritating him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-14-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:51:58-07:00","id":514237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=513272#post513272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it, then, that Virtues are either not a thing anymore or they\u2019re no longer hardwired to your Pantheon? Because in 1e, the Loa Virtues had little in common with the Tuatha de Danaan Virtues; if Virtues worked like they did in 1e, Maman Brigitte/Brigid/Saint Brigit would have a serious personality disorder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much less whatever &quot;mantles&quot; such a conglomeration of oddities would have. Maman Brigitte might have something to do with St. Brigit and the goddess Brigid might have something to do with St. Brigit, but the chances of them having anything to do with each other are.... remote. They barely have a thing in common. It's not a Zeus/Jupiter/Tinea thing, it's almost wildly bizarre. The best analogy would be saying something like saying that, since Veles is identified with St. Nicholas, and Santa Claus is associated with St. Nicholas, Veles and Santa Claus are the same person (despite the many OTHER gods who can make a much better claim to aspects of Santa Claus-ish-ness). Which means that there are all sorts of trickster stories of Santa Claus vs. St. Elias (aka Perun) out there....<br /> <br /> Maman Brigitte is from the Ghede Nanchon, so her relation to the Yoruba pantheon is pretty attenuated anyway. The tie-in between the Ghede found in the Caribbean and the Orisha of the Yoruba is hard nut to crack. (Probably because it's unlikely there is one. The Loa are not JUST the Yoruba Orisha. Vide the Kongo Nanchon. Where do Papa Ghede, Mamman Brigitte, the Baron(s), Nibo, Masaka, Oussou, Babaco, Doubye, Ti Malis, Lino, etc, come from? It's a REALLY good question)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T00:52:05-07:00","id":514873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=510422#post510422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we seem to have experts on the Mythology of the British Isles here, are Irish and Scottish myths close enough? What about English and Welsh Myths?</div> </div> </div> </div>In later myths, not related to the Gods and the mythological cycle, Irish and Scottish myth diverge, but in the myths relevant to Scion they are identical. Gaelic culture has three independent sets of myths. The Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan and invasion cycles is one set of them, again identical in Ireland and Scotland. The third set is actually more relevant to Changeling the Lost, with many stories of people returning to their old lives after fairy abductions.<br /> <br /> I believe we unfortunatly have very little English mythology left, Ive read much was abandoned at the end of the Stuart period. However what we have indicates little relation to Welsh myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T04:47:45-07:00","id":515047,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigid#Brigid_and_Saint_Brigid\" target=\"_blank\">Brigit and Saint Brigid</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:23:01-07:00","id":515872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=514873#post514873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we unfortunatly have very little English mythology left, Ive read much was abandoned at the end of the Stuart period. However what we have indicates little relation to Welsh myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Brythonic Mythology? England refers to the Kingdom of the Angles and Saxons (Literally Anglaland or sometimes Ingland - refering to Ingvie Freyr) so it would be quite stunning if it resembled Welsh Mythology beyond the Indo-European connection.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:28:29-07:00","id":516112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=515872#post515872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean Brythonic Mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just took TwoDSix's question at face value, i.e. is there much resemblance between the traditional myths of England and those of Wales. Wales has plenty of myths not related to its Brythonic origin, although I'm not as well read on Welsh myth as I'm sure some here are, I think Welsh is like Irish and the vast majority of myths do not have an English translation (I'd like to learn Welsh at some point though, really beautiful language). and we don't know how much of the mythology of England was Brythonic, how much was Anglo-Saxon and how much was unique. All I can say is that what has been preserved of English myth is not similar to Welsh myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 05-16-2015, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:46:26-07:00","id":516215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=516112#post516112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just took TwoDSix's question at face value, i.e. is there much resemblance between the traditional myths of England and those of Wales. Wales has plenty of myths not related to its Brythonic origin, although I'm not as well read on Welsh myth as I'm sure some here are, I think Welsh is like Irish and the vast majority of myths do not have an English translation (I'd like to learn Welsh at some point though, really beautiful language). and we don't know how much of the mythology of England was Brythonic, how much was Anglo-Saxon and how much was unique. All I can say is that what has been preserved of English myth is not similar to Welsh myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example of what you are considering English mythology that is separate from Welsh/Cymric mythology and Germano-Norse (&quot;complex&quot;) mythology?<br /> <br /> I am trying to guess what you are thinking of. Here's a few I can think of as being associated with &quot;English&quot; mythology:<br /> <br /> Wayland Smith.... who is almost certainly a version (mantle?) of Volund, a Germanic/Norse god<br /> Gwyn ap Nudd....who is just as Welsh as Welsh can be, even though he's all over Glastonburymyths, nor does his father, though Nydd is considered a cognate of Nodens &amp; Nuada)<br /> Taliesin... who shows up in Welsh myths, but is also in Y Gododdin - which is sorta Welsh, sorta &quot;English&quot;, sorta Scots (geographically at least), oh and in much more historical, non-legendary/non-mythical contexts as well (which includes Y Gododdin)<br /> <br /> And, of course, the whole King Arthur mythos, if you strip out tons and tons and tons of modernism, Romance embellishment (as in the Romantic Period), later-era Medievalism (specifically interpolation into the whole &quot;courtly love&quot; chanson de geste, etc.) and sort through for the Dark Ages era stuff left over, which does overlap with the Welsh stuff as Arthur does get some play in the shorter stories. <br /> <br /> That's all I can come up with out of my head. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T12:22:34-07:00","id":516382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=516215#post516215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give an example of what you are considering English mythology that is separate from Welsh/Cymric mythology and Germano-Norse (&quot;complex&quot;) mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things like the Redcaps, the Reynardine myths, the Black shuck. A lot of these things ultimately have their etymological origin in older Celtic or Germanic stuff, but they've been twisted or changed enough that I don't think they really are still just those myths but rather something new. Similar to how we don't present the Celtic, Germanic, etc myths as &quot;just&quot; all the same Indo-European myth. Like how the Aos S\u00ed aren't really the Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan. Although historically the Aos S\u00ed do come from the Tuatha, in folklore the Tuatha are presented as separate to the Aos S\u00ed and most Irish people would not have considered them the same. England has several things in its medieval mythology like that. Also some are just extrapolations of local events like the green children of Woolpit.<br /> <br /> Its this body of material I would call the &quot;traditional myths of England&quot;(basically the material on the English mythology Wiki page), maybe it's my lack of knowledge, but it's the only body of mythology I could think of as being English. I think, could be wrong, that most of it isn't really similar to Welsh myth thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 05-16-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T13:39:57-07:00","id":516430,"title":"","content":"Well the relation between the Aos Si and the Tuatha De is pretty explicitly one of being the same people. After the Second Battle of Mag Tuired, the Tuatha agreed to leave Ireland to the Milesians. Those of the Tuatha that stayed agreed to move underground. They became the Daoine Sidh or Aos Si. <br /> <br /> It's not like there aren't a ton of complications, like why is Finnvara the King of the Aos Si when it sure as hell looks like Aengus Og was still hanging around at Bru na Boinne and not having fun back in Tir na Nog? It's hard to see how the son of the Dadga (once king, royal enough that marrying his daughter was enough to make a Fomorian king of the Tuatha De, etc.), who was something complicated with Midhir, one of the kings of the Four Quarters, etc would cede pride of place to someone else (especially since we are talking about Aengus Og here.... subtlety and humility are definitely not his style). <br /> <br /> I think trying to assemble a mythology of Britain/Prydain/Lloegr/Albion is going to be a tough one. Especially if you want it to be separate from Welsh mythology. Welsh myths include lots of things that happened as far north as Scotland, as far East as London). Cornwall and Brittany as well. When Romanized Britain fell, the Britons that could, fell back to Wales (which may or may no have ever been Romanized... there are forts, but Claudius and Vespasian didn't think of it as being a part of the Empire), so a lot of what would have been the &quot;myths&quot; of further East would have been integrated. <br /> <br /> There are bits of Celtic mythology scattered here and there, but a lot of them have some analogue in Welsh legends and folk tales. It would be like, if when Scotland was overrun by the Irish, the Picts had fled to the Orkneys and established themselves there. Then later on, we come along and try to separate out &quot;Orkney-ish mythology&quot; from &quot;Pictish mythology&quot;. They may not be a different enough of a thing for that to work (especially in the context of a game that has lumped together Mycenaean, Classical Greek and Roman mythology... mantles aside).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T21:39:10-07:00","id":516714,"title":"","content":"I think what your describing is properly Folklore rather than mythology. English Myth and Religion was basically a regionalised part of the Greater Germanic Cosmology. (They Worshiped Woden (Odin) and Thunor (Thor)).<br /> <br /> In the context of the game, I would probably record the overlap as Celtic Supernaturals having refused to leave their territorial grounds and are in some stage of assimilation or rebellion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T08:32:02-07:00","id":517035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=514237#post514237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much less whatever &quot;mantles&quot; such a conglomeration of oddities would have. Maman Brigitte might have something to do with St. Brigit and the goddess Brigid might have something to do with St. Brigit, but the chances of them having anything to do with each other are.... remote. They barely have a thing in common. It's not a Zeus/Jupiter/Tinea thing, it's almost wildly bizarre. The best analogy would be saying something like saying that, since Veles is identified with St. Nicholas, and Santa Claus is associated with St. Nicholas, Veles and Santa Claus are the same person (despite the many OTHER gods who can make a much better claim to aspects of Santa Claus-ish-ness). Which means that there are all sorts of trickster stories of Santa Claus vs. St. Elias (aka Perun) out there....<br /> <br /> Maman Brigitte is from the Ghede Nanchon, so her relation to the Yoruba pantheon is pretty attenuated anyway. The tie-in between the Ghede found in the Caribbean and the Orisha of the Yoruba is hard nut to crack. (Probably because it's unlikely there is one. The Loa are not JUST the Yoruba Orisha. Vide the Kongo Nanchon. Where do Papa Ghede, Mamman Brigitte, the Baron(s), Nibo, Masaka, Oussou, Babaco, Doubye, Ti Malis, Lino, etc, come from? It's a REALLY good question)</div> </div> </div> </div>We have to remember than Afro-American religons are syncretic and adopted or assimilated figures from different cultures, African, European, Amerindian, and perhaps even Indian in the cases of some Afro-Caribbean religions. As for Brigitte, she has no link to the Orishas, she's a New World Loa and doesn't have an African counterpart as far as I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:30:26-07:00","id":517093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517035#post517035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have to remember than Afro-American religons are syncretic and adopted or assimilated figures from different cultures, African, European, Amerindian, and perhaps even Indian in the cases of some Afro-Caribbean religions. As for Brigitte, she has no link to the Orishas, she's a New World Loa and doesn't have an African counterpart as far as I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>. <br /> <br /> Most, if not all, polytheistic religions are syncretic, which is problematic for a game that is trying to hit the &quot;target&quot; of a core mythology to represent in game terms that are accessible to someone who picks up the books because the idea of playing a mythologically-based game where you GET TO PLAY THE GODS (eventually). All the comparative mythology, comparative modern religion studies, are informative and interesting, but you finally have to pin down a version of each deity that you are going to detail out, whether you are the game-designer or running a game for you and your friends. It's really really hard, if not impossible to get an accurate read on who &quot;Hecate&quot; would be when she's at home (and your mom) if you try to go with every different myth about her, all the evidence of her cult that we have records of, supplemented by what archaeologists have ground-truthed. That's effectively dozens of different people, many of whom are mutually exclusive. <br /> <br /> As much as one can look at the Loa through the lens of the Orisha or the Orisha through the lens of the Loa, the fact is that they AREN'T the same thing. Parts of the Orisha line up with parts of the Loa (and with those two, it's very nice that the Loa are sub-divided into the Nanchons, which pretty much map out that relationship). If you try to shoehorn the non-Orisha Nanchons into the Orisha, you've made a hard row to how for yourself. Maman Brigitte and pretty much ALL of the Ghede Nanchon fit into that category. There are a few distaff Orisha who are a little Ghede-like, but even they don't match up very well. Maybe as parents? Maybe the Ghede are Scions of the few appropriate Orisha that are associated pretty much exclusively with the New World? I could see some very grim (from &quot;laugh in the face of death&quot; to downright monstrous) figures arising from the awful conditions associated with the development of voudoun and other Caribbean religions. <br /> <br /> I think the whole idea of &quot;mantles&quot; is trying to deal with aspects of this situation. Whether or not they will work remains to be seen. Particularly in the context of moving the game away from a more exclusively &quot;gods&quot; part of mythology to a more &quot;Urban Fantasy&quot; centered around mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:40:36-07:00","id":517174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517093#post517093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Most, if not all, polytheistic religions are syncretic, which is problematic for a game that is trying to hit the &quot;target&quot; of a core mythology to represent in game terms that are accessible to someone who picks up the books because the idea of playing a mythologically-based game where you GET TO PLAY THE GODS (eventually). All the comparative mythology, comparative modern religion studies, are informative and interesting, but you finally have to pin down a version of each deity that you are going to detail out, whether you are the game-designer or running a game for you and your friends. It's really really hard, if not impossible to get an accurate read on who &quot;Hecate&quot; would be when she's at home (and your mom) if you try to go with every different myth about her, all the evidence of her cult that we have records of, supplemented by what archaeologists have ground-truthed. That's effectively dozens of different people, many of whom are mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> As much as one can look at the Loa through the lens of the Orisha or the Orisha through the lens of the Loa, the fact is that they AREN'T the same thing. Parts of the Orisha line up with parts of the Loa (and with those two, it's very nice that the Loa are sub-divided into the Nanchons, which pretty much map out that relationship). If you try to shoehorn the non-Orisha Nanchons into the Orisha, you've made a hard row to how for yourself. Maman Brigitte and pretty much ALL of the Ghede Nanchon fit into that category. There are a few distaff Orisha who are a little Ghede-like, but even they don't match up very well. Maybe as parents? Maybe the Ghede are Scions of the few appropriate Orisha that are associated pretty much exclusively with the New World? I could see some very grim (from &quot;laugh in the face of death&quot; to downright monstrous) figures arising from the awful conditions associated with the development of voudoun and other Caribbean religions.<br /> <br /> I think the whole idea of &quot;mantles&quot; is trying to deal with aspects of this situation. Whether or not they will work remains to be seen. Particularly in the context of moving the game away from a more exclusively &quot;gods&quot; part of mythology to a more &quot;Urban Fantasy&quot; centered around mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noting what Neall's said regarding the Theoi - that is, they have gods who belong solely to one of their various configurations - it's not too much of a leap to conclude that a similar thing is going on with the Yoruba, that there are gods who belong to the Loa without needing to belong to the Orishas.<br /> <br /> A sidenote is that 2e is apparently making God-born Scions playable - that is, Scions born solely of the gods, without any mortal blood. We don't know how that works yet, whether they run on the same rules as their mortal-born kin, but it does open up possibilities for new gods who weren't mortal-born.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:43:00-07:00","id":517177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517174#post517174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sidenote is that 2e is apparently making God-born Scions playable - that is, Scions born solely of the gods, without any mortal blood. We don't know how that works yet, whether they run on the same rules as their mortal-born kin, but it does open up possibilities for new gods who weren't mortal-born.</div> </div> </div> </div> This was also possible in in 1e, according to a sidebar in the Deva section of Companion. Glad to see it confirmed straight out of the gate, this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:57:10-07:00","id":517183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517093#post517093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Most, if not all, polytheistic religions are syncretic, which is problematic for a game that is trying to hit the &quot;target&quot; of a core mythology to represent in game terms that are accessible to someone who picks up the books because the idea of playing a mythologically-based game where you GET TO PLAY THE GODS (eventually). All the comparative mythology, comparative modern religion studies, are informative and interesting, but you finally have to pin down a version of each deity that you are going to detail out, whether you are the game-designer or running a game for you and your friends. It's really really hard, if not impossible to get an accurate read on who &quot;Hecate&quot; would be when she's at home (and your mom) if you try to go with every different myth about her, all the evidence of her cult that we have records of, supplemented by what archaeologists have ground-truthed. That's effectively dozens of different people, many of whom are mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> As much as one can look at the Loa through the lens of the Orisha or the Orisha through the lens of the Loa, the fact is that they AREN'T the same thing. Parts of the Orisha line up with parts of the Loa (and with those two, it's very nice that the Loa are sub-divided into the Nanchons, which pretty much map out that relationship). If you try to shoehorn the non-Orisha Nanchons into the Orisha, you've made a hard row to how for yourself. Maman Brigitte and pretty much ALL of the Ghede Nanchon fit into that category. There are a few distaff Orisha who are a little Ghede-like, but even they don't match up very well. Maybe as parents? Maybe the Ghede are Scions of the few appropriate Orisha that are associated pretty much exclusively with the New World? I could see some very grim (from &quot;laugh in the face of death&quot; to downright monstrous) figures arising from the awful conditions associated with the development of voudoun and other Caribbean religions.<br /> <br /> I think the whole idea of &quot;mantles&quot; is trying to deal with aspects of this situation. Whether or not they will work remains to be seen. Particularly in the context of moving the game away from a more exclusively &quot;gods&quot; part of mythology to a more &quot;Urban Fantasy&quot; centered around mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that we're trying to force together 2 different pantheons under the umbrella of Afro-American religions: the Loa whose African roots are Fon and Ewe, and the Orishas who are Yoruba. It's like trying include the Persian gods among the Vedic pantheon, or the Celtic gods among the Greek. They're obviously related but also clearly different and independent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:59:52-07:00","id":517184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517177#post517177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This was also possible in in 1e, according to a sidebar in the Deva section of Companion. Glad to see it confirmed straight out of the gate, this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. My impression from Companion was that they'd basically be running on exactly the same set-up as mortal-born Scions. I'm hoping this time there'll be some options for where they start off power-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:28:22-07:00","id":517239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517184#post517184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm. My impression from Companion was that they'd basically be running on exactly the same set-up as mortal-born Scions. I'm hoping this time there'll be some options for where they start off power-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Options for starting at every power level, pre-Visitation, Hero, Demigod and even God, would be nice. <br /> <br /> Conversion rules would also be nice. I know we've had several games fall apart when they hit Demigod (actually more like shattering when hitting a brick wall). It would be cool to be able to retrofit those characters into the new Demigod and pick up where we left off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:57:30-07:00","id":517272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517239#post517239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversion rules would also be nice. I know we've had several games fall apart when they hit Demigod (actually more like shattering when hitting a brick wall).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? What happened?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T16:03:27-07:00","id":517389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517239#post517239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Options for starting at every power level, pre-Visitation, Hero, Demigod and even God, would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll get them! (Eventually.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversion rules would also be nice. I know we've had several games fall apart when they hit Demigod (actually more like shattering when hitting a brick wall). It would be cool to be able to retrofit those characters into the new Demigod and pick up where we left off. </div> </div> </div>That, you won't get, though I think you'll be able to retrofit the characters without our guidance. If you kept track of your sessions with notes, I think you'll be able to rebuild the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-17-2015, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T17:01:22-07:00","id":517426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517272#post517272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? What happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which time? I've had it happen 3 times as ST (possibly more... I went back and looked but the summaries are not dispositive on two other games) and once as a player. You get to Demigod and you start playing and things just don't work. Particuarly if you aren't a combat oriented character. (Any combat character who dabbles in social matters will be just as powerful vs almost everything you deal with as a character who focuses solely on social matters. Mental focused characters are essentially shit-out-of-luck.) If you are combat oriented, all that matters is a very few things and slight differences in build mean insta-kill (or conversely insta-death). The options for powers are impoverished at best, or ill-conceived. There are some Boons no one will buy unless they are going for the Avatar. They are just so bad. Everything becomes irrelevant except Epics and a few decent Boons (and some MUCH have super-Boons). Most people I've talked to who played thru either hand-waved the rules away for the most part or filled in with massive amounts of house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T17:05:16-07:00","id":517431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517389#post517389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversion rules would also be nice. I know we've had several games fall apart when they hit Demigod (actually more like shattering when hitting a brick wall). It would be cool to be able to retrofit those characters into the new Demigod and pick up where we left off.<br /> <br /> That, you won't get, though I think you'll be able to retrofit the characters without our guidance. If you kept track of your sessions with notes, I think you'll be able to rebuild the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on decades of past experience with RPGs, that usually means that there really isn't any real way to make conversions. &lt;Sigh&gt; Too bad. It means those games are really OVER. It's unlikely that the outcome characters would appreciably resemble the characters they actually played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T01:02:36-07:00","id":517755,"title":"","content":"Hm. Neall, do you want a dedicated Q&amp;A thread, or are you happy commenting on whatever comes up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T06:50:10-07:00","id":517932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=517755#post517755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Neall, do you want a dedicated Q&amp;A thread, or are you happy commenting on whatever comes up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you want to make an Ask Neall thread, feel free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T14:34:28-07:00","id":520008,"title":"","content":"Just in case you're interested...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=516430#post516430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the relation between the Aos Si and the Tuatha De is pretty explicitly one of being the same people. After the Second Battle of Mag Tuired, the Tuatha agreed to leave Ireland to the Milesians. Those of the Tuatha that stayed agreed to move underground. They became the Daoine Sidh or Aos Si.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the funny thing about Diachronic versus Synchronic view of mythology. The author of the Leabhar Gabh\u00e1la and other texts certainly viewed things like this, but I know in the folkloric tradition they were separate. This is obviously because people forgot who the Aos S\u00ed were supposed to be. In folklore, the Aos S\u00ed were basically any supernatural creature that wasn't human, an angel or a demon. So vampires, little people, ghosts of dead humans, elves, will o' the wisp type creatures, e.t.c. In a lot of stories all these people/entities live together in forts underground.<br /> There's a story about a man being abducted by magical people who bring him to a cave where he is guarded by trolls and talks to human ghosts, all of these are considered Sithe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 05-19-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T06:57:29-07:00","id":524383,"title":"","content":"Sorry to step on the thread but I was wondering if the Vedas, Celestial Bureaucracy, Celts and Yazada were confirmed for the core-book or if we were just assuming?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T08:31:37-07:00","id":524493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=524383#post524383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to step on the thread but I was wondering if the Vedas, Celestial Bureaucracy, Celts and Yazada were confirmed for the core-book or if we were just assuming?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been told nine of the core/Companion pantheons are making it into Hero 2e, including all six of the original core. Neall's confirmed the Irish pantheon are making it in (the Origins cover sig character is a Scion of the Dagda), and I'd be pretty surprised if the Hindu and Chinese pantheons weren't the other two.<br /> <br /> The tenth pantheon is new, and has been mentioned on the first page of this thread, so it's not the Yazata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:04:14-07:00","id":524509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=524493#post524493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've been told nine of the core/Companion pantheons are making it into Hero 2e, including all six of the original core. Neall's confirmed the Irish pantheon are making it in (the Origins cover sig character is a Scion of the Dagda), and I'd be pretty surprised if the Hindu and Chinese pantheons weren't the other two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just confirm that now, sure. The tenth and other book's pantheons will have to wait for Gen Con.<br /> <br /> We've also got several stretch goal pantheons (though one of them isn't a true pantheon, but a collection of related gods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T15:37:23-07:00","id":524832,"title":"","content":"I'm so happy to hear that the Celestial Bureaucracy's going to make it in. I seriously adore and appreciate the attention to detail on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:43:21-08:00","id":750342,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463486#post463486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Originally posted by <b>Neall</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=463476#post463476\">View Post</a></i><br /> <i>Personally? I'd love to do a Gaulish pantheon as a prime example of a &quot;dead&quot; or destroyed pantheon as a potential Kickstarter goal or further PDF/POD book down the line. They got completely annihilated by a militant Scion of Venus. What strange strands does Fate weave for the dead...? When you walk in the footsteps of dead gods, do they then walk like you?</i><br /> Bring it! Take my money please!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>very agreed. plus, i'd love to get Epona back(possibly in the irish pantheon), seeing as a gaulish pantheon was included in a french-only supplement we never got.<br /> i'm eagerly awaiting the new editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T04:43:37-08:00","id":751159,"title":"","content":"I just had an idea. What about a pantheon based on the Zodiac constellations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T10:43:38-08:00","id":770827,"title":"","content":"It's clear to me that we'll want some sidebars on syncretic deities and Gods that work with multiple pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:23:37-07:00","id":957609,"title":"","content":"I know that this topic is kind of old, but...<br /> <br /> I think a Manichaean pantheon would be interesting, if very difficult, to work in and would love to see one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 11-01-2016, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T21:46:30-07:00","id":961433,"title":"","content":"So since this got resurrected... we know the 10 in the core:<br /> <br /> Aesir (Norse/Germanic)<br /> Deva (Indian)<br /> Kami (Japanese)<br /> Manitou (Algonquin)<br /> Netjer (Egyptian)<br /> Orisha (West African)<br /> Shen (Chinese)<br /> Teotl (Aztec)<br /> Theoi (Greco-Roman)<br /> Tuatha de Danann (Irish)<br /> <br /> And we know at leas three likely stretchgoal pantheons for the kickstarter:<br /> <br /> Loa (Caribbean expansion to the Orisha)<br /> Nemetondevos (Gaulish)<br /> Yazatas (Persian)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So that leaves that I'd like to see (a couple of these have been confirmed for later books already):<br /> <br /> Anga (Guarani [southern Amazon])<br /> Anunnaki (Mesopotamian)<br /> Apu (Incan)<br /> Atua (Polynesian)<br /> Bogovi (Slavic)<br /> Diwata (Philippine)<br /> Diyin Dine'e/Kachinas (the Navajo-Apachean and Puebloan-Hopi Pantheons that have been Fatebound together by centuries of conflict)<br /> Elohim (Phoenician/Abrahamic)<br /> Jumalat (Finnish)<br /> K'uh (Mayan)<br /> Mabinogion (Welsh - perhaps an overlapping sub-pantheon with the Tuatha, like the Orisha and the Loa)<br /> Miungu (Southern African Bantu coalition pantheon)<br /> Tjukurpa (Aboriginal Australian)<br /> Tngri (Turkic/Mongolian)<br /> Unipkaaqs (Inuit)<br /> Wakan Tanka (Sioux)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:21:25-07:00","id":961458,"title":"","content":"I think the Inuit gods and Atua have been actually confirmed for Demigod, and I'd kill to see the Mesopotamian and Mayan Pantheons as well. <br /> <br /> You'll have one hell of a time convincing them to touch the Elohim, but it might be a fun thought exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:45:31-07:00","id":961461,"title":"","content":"If the Deva are the on the table, I don't see why the Elohim shouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-01-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:49:13-07:00","id":961465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=961458#post961458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have one hell of a time convincing them to touch the Elohim, but it might be a fun thought exercise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall has the Canaanite/Phoenician pantheon on the slate for Demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T23:10:58-07:00","id":961470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=961465#post961465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neall has the Canaanite/Phoenician pantheon on the slate for Demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know what other Pantheons are planned for that book? I know the Atua were confirmed for it, but the line between &quot;this sounds cool&quot; and &quot;Neall actually said&quot; can get fuzzy after so many posts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm doing this myself. <br /> <br /> The planned stretch goals for the Hero Kickstarter seem to be the dead Gaulish gods, the Persian gods, and a Loa expansion for the Orisha.<br /> <br /> Canaanite is &quot;slated for Demigod,&quot; as are the Polynesian gods. <br /> <br /> The Filipino gods are mentioned for God, though it seems a little confusing as to whether or not this is referring to the Atua or specifically them as a separate thing. The Native Australian pantheon is also mentioned for God.<br /> <br /> The Guarani gods (of the Amazon) are mentioned as a later unspecified stretch goal. The Mesopotamian, Inuit, Mayan, and Inca gods are &quot;for later books.&quot; The Slavic gods are mentioned. The Welsh gods may have a dedicated book.<br /> <br /> I think that's everything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-01-2016, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T00:06:46-07:00","id":961491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=961470#post961470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know what other Pantheons are planned for that book? I know the Atua were confirmed for it, but the line between &quot;this sounds cool&quot; and &quot;Neall actually said&quot; can get fuzzy after so many posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, he's only mentioned the Polynesian and Canaanite pantheons for Demigod.<br /> <br /> Tagalog and Australian Aborigine are slated for God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:07:37-07:00","id":961638,"title":"","content":"I think that a Lithuanian, or if that's not possible then a more general Baltic, pantheon would be cool.<br /> <br /> In fact I'm currently working on a Dievs fan-expansion, though it's so slow going that 2E God will probably be release first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:11:27-07:00","id":961952,"title":"","content":"After some of my own research I don't think the Diwata (Filipine Gods) make sense as part of the Atua, save purely as a political alliance (i.e. Separate Virtues, Pantheon Purview, metaphysical realms, etc). They have a very distinct culture and mythology with little overlap. If anything the Pantheon they are closest to overlapping with are the Deva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:07:58-07:00","id":962023,"title":"","content":"&quot;Native Australian&quot; Pantheon is as over-inclusive lumping together every different North American culture into one pantheon.<br /> <br /> Having the Navajo and Pueblo Nations have one pantheon would be fairy inappropriate. It would be more accurate to, say, glom together the Persian and Indian pantheons and saying, &quot;Well, they're really just one pantheon tied together by a shared history&quot;. At least he Asuras &amp; Yazata, the Devas &amp; Divs have some actual cultural and historical relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:15:25-07:00","id":962026,"title":"","content":"There truly is an embarrassment of riches to choose from. With that in mind, I'd like to see the <i>starting selection</i> (that is, Hero+ Demigod+God) hit at least four distinct Pantheons per continent, excluding Antarctica and treating the Pacific Ocean as a continent for this purpose. It may not be possible (does Australia have enough distinct indigenous cultures to support four Pantheons?); But I'd like see them try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:46:17-07:00","id":962033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962023#post962023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Native Australian&quot; Pantheon is as over-inclusive lumping together every different North American culture into one pantheon.<br /> <br /> Having the Navajo and Pueblo Nations have one pantheon would be fairy inappropriate. It would be more accurate to, say, glom together the Persian and Indian pantheons and saying, &quot;Well, they're really just one pantheon tied together by a shared history&quot;. At least he Asuras &amp; Yazata, the Devas &amp; Divs have some actual cultural and historical relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for they have shared creation myth and a huge overlap of shared figures, to the point where you'd be redoing half the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying ignore the separate cultural groups, I'm saying in this case it'd make sense to highlight Fatebinding and pantheon overlap across cultural groups.<br /> <br /> Also for the Persian/Indian example - I am very interested to see how the game handles the Asura/Ahura vs Deva/Daeva issue. It would be completely valid to not draw up those figures vilified in one culture as distinct to them - and instead use cross-pantheon rivalry to explain who the Daeva &quot;Indra&quot; is (for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-01-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:48:34-07:00","id":962035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962026#post962026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There truly is an embarrassment of riches to choose from. With that in mind, I'd like to see the <i>starting selection</i> (that is, Hero+ Demigod+God) hit at least four distinct Pantheons per continent, excluding Antarctica and treating the Pacific Ocean as a continent for this purpose. It may not be possible (does Australia have enough distinct indigenous cultures to support four Pantheons?); But I'd like see them try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enough cultures? Yes. Enough distinct legend systems shared with outsiders to draw on is a very different story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:12:39-07:00","id":962139,"title":"","content":"Possibly relevant in regards to an Australian pantheon is that Neall's mentioned confederate pantheons, formed by an alliance of pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:39:55-07:00","id":962151,"title":"","content":"I don't claim to know all the different Aborigine beliefs, so I may very well be wrong about this, but... I just don't think that there are enough Legend 12 'dieties' in Australia to form multiple pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 09-02-2016, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:33:15-07:00","id":962303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962033#post962033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for they have shared creation myth and a huge overlap of shared figures, to the point where you'd be redoing half the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying ignore the separate cultural groups, I'm saying in this case it'd make sense to highlight Fatebinding and pantheon overlap across cultural groups.<br /> <br /> Also for the Persian/Indian example - I am very interested to see how the game handles the Asura/Ahura vs Deva/Daeva issue. It would be completely valid to not draw up those figures vilified in one culture as distinct to them - and instead use cross-pantheon rivalry to explain who the Daeva &quot;Indra&quot; is (for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>I need some sources on that, because everything I've ever seen, and I mean EVER, doesn't show them as having all that much in common as far as mythological figures or stories or myths. At least, insofar, as they are that much different than, say, from Aztec or Mayan. They are more distinct than Aztec is from Maya, if annything. In fact, there are uncanny similarities between Mayan and Pueblo myths that neither share overmuch with Navajo or Aztec. Unless you are willing to glom together all four, I can't see you putting those two together. (Or even worse, just sum all North American mythology into one undifferentiated mass.... kinda like my old chestnut of dropping all distinctions between pantheons of Indo-European origin.) And those are four very VERY different cultures in pretty much every way that cultures can be different - religious practices, kinship and marriage, power distribution, exchange mechanisms, language groups, historical origin, etc. This is not even close to having something like the differences between the Welsh (which wouldn't be Mabinogion, that's a book title meaning, effectively, &quot;stories about the youth... it would be like calling the figures of Christian/Abrahamic mythology &quot;Bible&quot;) and Irish (Tuatha De) pantheons.<br /> <br /> For one sub-section of one Scion cycle I ran awhile ago, I had no problem generating a Pueblo pantheon, PSP included, and differentiated it from Navajo with a few key figures from the latter's myths, the way that the detailed/mentioned pantheons have been to date (a la Irish/Welsh, Aztec/Mayan, etc.) <br /> <br /> I'm not buying a Fatebinding argument. Unless, say. you are willing to similarly fuse the Persian and Hindu mythos and have them Fatebound together as two interlocking opposing pantheons (our angels vs. your demons), even though the analogy isn't perfect as the Navajo and Pueblo mythologies don't depict the deities of one as the &quot;opposition&quot; to another... say, like having Masauwu and Hahti Wuhti appearing as inverse images to the Navajo (e.g. a scary-er fire/war guy and not so nice old woman spider woman). And I can't find any myths among the Navajo that duplicate the Pahana myth (though Quetzalcoatl mirrors it quite nicely). They both have a Hero Twin's like set of myths, but it's not that much different from the Mayan set-up and, in some ways, from the Aztec Quetzalcoatl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:44:23-07:00","id":962313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962151#post962151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't claim to know all the different Aborigine beliefs, so I may very well be wrong about this, but... I just don't think that there are enough Legend 12 'dieties' in Australia to form multiple pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are, quite understandably, wrong. Mushing all the different Australian mythologies together into one mass, or even confederacy is pretty much exactly the same as doing the same for North American pantheons. There are hundreds of distinct Aboriginal groups that have distinct areas of overlap, often on a regional basis, but the groups as different, if not more so, than, say the differences between Irish, Norse, Slavic, Graeco-Roman mythologies. And, yes, you can have multiple different Legend 12 figures, even if they are very similar in some ways. Unless, say, we can just say Zeus, Thor and Perun are really the same guy. <br /> <br /> And that's not even touching on, say, the mythologies of the many many different New Guinea tribes, which have some similarities to the Melanesians, which aren't like the Polynesian, but are more like (but different enough to warrant their own treatment) than those like some parts of the Phillippines... And then there's Africa. And South America. And Central Asia. And Siberia. <br /> <br /> The sources for lots of mythologies aren't readily available, particularly to a European-based audience, but that doesn't mean they aren't there. I have confidence the Scion team will try to make the necessary steps to reach out to people who are closer to the source material and who are willing to do the needed digging (as in &quot;massive excavation&quot;) needed to bring to light and the game the mythologies of groups most people don't even know exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:35:08-07:00","id":962623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962313#post962313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are, quite understandably, wrong. Mushing all the different Australian mythologies together into one mass, or even confederacy is pretty much exactly the same as doing the same for North American pantheons. There are hundreds of distinct Aboriginal groups that have distinct areas of overlap, often on a regional basis, but the groups as different, if not more so, than, say the differences between Irish, Norse, Slavic, Graeco-Roman mythologies. And, yes, you can have multiple different Legend 12 figures, even if they are very similar in some ways. Unless, say, we can just say Zeus, Thor and Perun are really the same guy.<br /> <br /> And that's not even touching on, say, the mythologies of the many many different New Guinea tribes, which have some similarities to the Melanesians, which aren't like the Polynesian, but are more like (but different enough to warrant their own treatment) than those like some parts of the Phillippines... And then there's Africa. And South America. And Central Asia. And Siberia.<br /> <br /> The sources for lots of mythologies aren't readily available, particularly to a European-based audience, but that doesn't mean they aren't there. I have confidence the Scion team will try to make the necessary steps to reach out to people who are closer to the source material and who are willing to do the needed digging (as in &quot;massive excavation&quot;) needed to bring to light and the game the mythologies of groups most people don't even know exist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am Australian and while I don't claim to be an expert on it, I'd like to think I know more about Aborigine beliefs than most people. I was not claiming that we should mush all of the different Australian pantheons together, though I can see how you might have gotten that from my post. I was responding to Datawaver's comment about having four Australian pantheons, though I forgot to quote them to make that clear.<br /> <br /> I do believe that there are lots of distinct cultures and that glomming all their beliefs together is a horrible idea, but I'm not really sure that four seperate pantheons is possible. A combination of legends not being shared, legends being lost, legends being similar between different culture groups, legends being about 'dieties' who (in my opinion) don't qualify as Legend 12 and people making up legends to try and draw in tourists in some areas has led to Australian 'mythology' being incredibly difficult to research. As a result, I'm just not sure that more than one pantheon is possible. Maybe two if they bust their asses.<br /> <br /> But hey, maybe I'm wrong. Maybe they could find enough Legend 12 'dieties' to form four pantheons. If they did, I would be very impressed and <i>very </i>happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:08:42-07:00","id":962677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962303#post962303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not even close to having something like the differences between the Welsh (which wouldn't be Mabinogion, that's a book title meaning, effectively, &quot;stories about the youth... it would be like calling the figures of Christian/Abrahamic mythology &quot;Bible&quot;) and Irish (Tuatha De) pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a hypothesis of the meaning of Mabinogion. We don't know what it means, but many also argue it means &quot;the Divine Sons&quot;. And I agree with you on Irish and Welsh Myth, that's why I suggested they'd make the most sense and extension/sub pantheon ala the Orisha and the Loa.<br /> <br /> As to the massive overlap in Navajo and Hopi legends, I don't have my literature with me at the moment, but I'd suggest looking at the ascent through the four previous worlds as the first major starting point off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> We know that Pantheons that are at one point separate can subsume each other through cultural exchange. It is a thing that happens in-setting. Just ask the surviving Sabine gods like Janus, Fontus, or Juturna...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:03:07-07:00","id":962867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962677#post962677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a hypothesis of the meaning of Mabinogion. We don't know what it means, but many also argue it means &quot;the Divine Sons&quot;. And I agree with you on Irish and Welsh Myth, that's why I suggested they'd make the most sense and extension/sub pantheon ala the Orisha and the Loa.<br /> <br /> As to the massive overlap in Navajo and Hopi legends, I don't have my literature with me at the moment, but I'd suggest looking at the ascent through the four previous worlds as the first major starting point off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> We know that Pantheons that are at one point separate can subsume each other through cultural exchange. It is a thing that happens in-setting. Just ask the surviving Sabine gods like Janus, Fontus, or Juturna...</div> </div> </div> </div>An entire post just got eaten, so I am disheartened to be answering this all over again, but:<br /> <br /> The etymology of &quot;Mabinogion&quot; isn't so much at issue as the fact it shouldn't be used as the name of the pantheon. Or else call the Tuatha &quot;the Labor&quot;. I don't agree the Welsh make any sense as a &quot;sub-pantheon&quot;. At all. They have more than enough deity level figures to have a full-on pantheon that stands toe to toe with the Irish, Norse, or anyone else for that matter. Two full families of divinity. (And sure, a lot of them are dead, but that never seems to stop Celtic gods.) And, yes, there is some really decent crossover. Lugh and Lleu really ca'tn be the same dude, but Manawydan and Mannanan sure as hell seem like one guy. Mannanan being the older version after the slew of Manawydan's adventures. <br /> <br /> If you are going to hold onto the &quot;journey up to this world&quot; you are still holding on to something that sets them up to be glomm-worthy with the Mesoamerican pantheons. There are substantive differences between those journeys. They don't always number the same number of worlds. The worlds journeyed aren't exactly the same. They don't end up in the same place. The various divine participants aren't the same. <br /> <br /> The whole thing about that &quot;subsumption&quot; argument is that it doesn't hold water when there are some places it's used to justify certain actions and elsewhere it is used to justify others. We are getting a differentiated Gaulish pantheon but the Welsh is part of the Tuatha. The Etruscan gets sucked up into the Greek (effectively, since those are pretty much all the myths), but the Mayan are separete from the Aztec? There is a fundamental question here and, when answered one way, leads to less stories, less choices and less options (with some possibility of it leading in an invidious direction) and the other maximizes choice, allows for more stories (both to be used and to create) and more options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T13:53:19-07:00","id":963369,"title":"","content":"So further research makes me agree that the Diyin Dine'e and the Kachinas shouldn't be competely Fatebound together, though strong attention should be given to their interrelationship, with Spider Grandmother being a Kachina primarily who is feared and respected by the Navajo none the less, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, let's not pretend that the game isn't full of conflated Pantheons. The Manitou being a single Pantheon is itself lumping together the Ojibwe, Wabanaki, and Cree (and thus Nanabozho, Glooskap, and Wiskadjek).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:14:54-07:00","id":967617,"title":"","content":"Next editions should have MORE than less pantheons.<br /> <br /> Slavic pantheon is a must if we want to respect old Europe land.<br /> Also Finnish and Baltic are fascinating.<br /> I loved Persian Yazata. There should be Hindu Deva + Asuras and Persian Daeva (Devils) + Ahuras (angels) dualism. That's natural conflict: old gods vs new gods and demonizing old gods.<br /> In hinduism Asuras are evil, but at beginning they were angelic - replaced with angelic deva. In persian mythos ahuras(asuras) are angelic and daevas are devils. I would love to see that conflict between two groups in one split pantheon in Scion game terms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> There should be also something like African or Polynesian mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T22:07:03-07:00","id":967766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=967617#post967617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next editions should have MORE than less pantheons.<br /> <br /> Slavic pantheon is a must if we want to respect old Europe land.<br /> Also Finnish and Baltic are fascinating.<br /> I loved Persian Yazata. There should be Hindu Deva + Asuras and Persian Daeva (Devils) + Ahuras (angels) dualism. That's natural conflict: old gods vs new gods and demonizing old gods.<br /> In hinduism Asuras are evil, but at beginning they were angelic - replaced with angelic deva. In persian mythos ahuras(asuras) are angelic and daevas are devils. I would love to see that conflict between two groups in one split pantheon in Scion game terms <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> There should be also something like African or Polynesian mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Polynesian is on track for Demigod, though whether they go Maori, Hawaiian, or something else remains to be seen. 'African' is massively too broad (can you imagine a 'European' Pantheon?), but there's both the Egyptian (some people get weird about whether or not North Africa counts for some reason) and Yoruba Pantheons in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:57:16-07:00","id":968057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=962867#post962867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The etymology of &quot;Mabinogion&quot; isn't so much at issue as the fact it shouldn't be used as the name of the pantheon. Or else call the Tuatha &quot;the Labor&quot;. I don't agree the Welsh make any sense as a &quot;sub-pantheon&quot;. At all. They have more than enough deity level figures to have a full-on pantheon that stands toe to toe with the Irish, Norse, or anyone else for that matter. Two full families of divinity. (And sure, a lot of them are dead, but that never seems to stop Celtic gods.) And, yes, there is some really decent crossover. Lugh and Lleu really ca'tn be the same dude, but Manawydan and Mannanan sure as hell seem like one guy. Mannanan being the older version after the slew of Manawydan's adventures.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, I recommended calling the Welsh pantheon the Plant D\u00f4n, and I think that's what we're going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:13:29-07:00","id":968068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968057#post968057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it helps, I recommended calling the Welsh pantheon the Plant D\u00f4n, and I think that's what we're going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two families though, Don and Llyr.... and it's to be a mouthful for have both together. I'd just go with Tylwythau (Kindreds/Families) or Dau Tylwythau (Two Families/Kindreds) or just Tylwyth. It has the benefits of parallelism with Tuatha and with a sorta-antecedent with the 'sidhe analogue&quot; being the Tylwyth Teg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:36:59-07:00","id":968077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=963369#post963369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So further research makes me agree that the Diyin Dine'e and the Kachinas shouldn't be competely Fatebound together, though strong attention should be given to their interrelationship, with Spider Grandmother being a Kachina primarily who is feared and respected by the Navajo none the less, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, let's not pretend that the game isn't full of conflated Pantheons. The Manitou being a single Pantheon is itself lumping together the Ojibwe, Wabanaki, and Cree (and thus Nanabozho, Glooskap, and Wiskadjek).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. To a point. A portion of the Cree and of the Ojibwe/Chippewa share a reservation and a linguistic association, but that doesn't make them the same folks with the same beliefs. Except, of course, it kinda does, as the Oji-Cree are considered a group in their own right and derive from exactly that mix. And the Oji-Cree, the Algonquian and the tribes of the Council of Three Fires (the Ojibwe/Chippewa, the Ottawa and the Potawatomi) are all the Anishinaabe. And the Anishinaabe are sometimes regarded as being a descendant group of the Abenaki in their own legends (and the Abenaki are the descendants of the Lenape in some of those same legends... And the Abenaki are part of the Wabanki Confederacy of tribes. BUT, the Cree legends state that the Anishinaabe are THEIR descendants... All of them speak Algonquian languages, but that's not really going to help things out... As a lot of the groups involved are more linguistic &quot;adoptees&quot; than anything else.<br /> <br /> However, after some poking around more than a little bit, it seems like most Algonquian groups have some concept of &quot;Manitou&quot; (with lots of different spellings and lots of different shades of meaning) that relates to supernatural creatures of some sort.... So what do you do? The cultures involved are, effectively, post-Apocalyptic. They have been pushed around and forced to live together in places far from home. It seems like a judgment call as to whether setting up an &quot;Algonquian&quot; pantheon is a good representation (with lots and lots of different names tacked onto each deity) or if it should be a set of pantheons in one of these cultural &quot;confederacies&quot; that is being floated for the Polynesian pantheons (or even, on a smaller scale, the Celts with the Irish/Welsh pantheons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:58:15-07:00","id":968129,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, the Iroquois conception of Manitou is apparently different enough that my writer wants to make them their own little group within a pantheon, with Ioskeha/Sapling/Good Mind and Tawiscara/Flint/Bad Mind being twin brothers who aren't terribly fond of their four cousins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:19:24-07:00","id":968137,"title":"","content":"I'd say it would be sort of an open question about identifying the Iroquois with all of the above mess. There wasn't a whole lot of love lost between them and many of the above. Like I said, how many pantheons do you want? How many pantheons can you reasonably establish? If it gets to the point that it's like trying to split the Greeks from the Romans or the Norse from their Germanic counterparts, it's gotten down to a very fine grain indeed. You CAN, but it's going to be a very specific game with a very specific audience and probably a very definite reason for doing so (like a Latin &amp;/or Sabine &amp;/or Etruscan &quot;revolution&quot; within the overall Graeco-Roman pantheon (which assumes the whole concept of pantheistic syncretism as deistic quasi-imperialism)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:29:58-07:00","id":968335,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Plus, let's not forget - this isn't the pantheons and the world as they were 2,000 years ago. This is a game of the pantheons as they are NOW, in a modern world with different cultures, borders, and issues for them to deal with. The Native American pantheon may be different, simply because their people are different now. Ditto Mesoamerica, Africa, and parts of Europe, to name a few. Let's not assume that everything is static in the world of Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:40:17-07:00","id":968643,"title":"","content":"To a point. This is not a &quot;belief determines reality&quot; based setting. The gods EXIST. They ARE. They don't depend on the mortals for their existence or shape or form or substance. Worship doesn't feed them. It may affect them or put limitations on them, but mana is mana, amrit is amrit, nectar is nectar, ichor is ichor and the gods derive their power from themselves and their connections to the forces of creation. <br /> <br /> So, the mortal world may be a muddle, but the gods of Greece don't care if part of Greece is Turkey. Halicarnassus is still THEIRS. And so on. In fact, the mortal muddle may have more to do with the gods absence than with any changes to themselves. Maybe the Norse would still go a-Viking if the Aesir hadn't contented themselves with other matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:17:13-07:00","id":968776,"title":"","content":"Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons. <br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:36:48-07:00","id":968795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons. <br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have plans for further stretch goals if this thing jumps the rails and is crazy successful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:02:22-07:00","id":968833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968643#post968643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a point. This is not a &quot;belief determines reality&quot; based setting. The gods EXIST. They ARE. They don't depend on the mortals for their existence or shape or form or substance. Worship doesn't feed them. It may affect them or put limitations on them, but mana is mana, amrit is amrit, nectar is nectar, ichor is ichor and the gods derive their power from themselves and their connections to the forces of creation.<br /> <br /> So, the mortal world may be a muddle, but the gods of Greece don't care if part of Greece is Turkey. Halicarnassus is still THEIRS. And so on. In fact, the mortal muddle may have more to do with the gods absence than with any changes to themselves. Maybe the Norse would still go a-Viking if the Aesir hadn't contented themselves with other matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly what I meant. Many folks are asking for pantheons that represent specific tribes of First Nations people in North America, Africa, and Australia. But in a world where the old Gods are REAL, but where monotheism isn't unknown, the borders of assorted cultures are going to be different from what we see in our world, and so a pantheon that is made up of deities from several tribes [who may have banded together to survive in the face of Western encroachment] isn't too far-fetched. Perhaps the Gods of different pantheons agreed to cooperate to resist outside influences, or because political alliances changed. Just because our real world has distinct [but not very well-documented] pantheons for all of these regions, doesn't mean that the game has to in order to still be good, fun, and representative of assorted beliefs. It isn't a religious text - it's an RPG. Our world froze many of these faiths in time because they were supplanted by our monotheistic systems and peoples, or their cultures were destroyed/absorbed/suppressed, but the world of Scion isn't like that [or at least, that isn't the core point of the game]; it is still a dynamic, changing world, where the Gods are real, and so beliefs and groupings would logically change through the centuries. To me, that seems a lot more fascinating and engaging than leaving the status quo as it was when [for example] Ancient Egypt ceased to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:16:44-07:00","id":968841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nemetondevos</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, just to clarify... Are the Nemetondevos that dead Gaul pantheon you've mentioned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:06:36-07:00","id":969016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons. <br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woo! Diyin Dine'e for the win!<br /> <br /> With the Slavic are you leaning more Russian or Baltic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:45:07-07:00","id":969031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968841#post968841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, just to clarify... Are the Nemetondevos that dead Gaul pantheon you've mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, originally written up for the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/94027/Scion--cran-du-Conteur\" target=\"_blank\">French-language Storyteller's Screen</a> for 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T23:27:41-07:00","id":969038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons.<br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, to the thread's original question then, beyond what Neall's confirmed here, my (unranked) top 10 list of &quot;Pantheons I want&quot; would be...<br /> <br /> - At least one Aboriginal Australian Pantheon. Not to say one Pantheon can incorporate the entire continent's worth of cultural lore, but find the tradition that is most well known and lean in there<br /> - At least one other African Pantheon. My main suggestions would be a Khoisan Pantheon, an Mbuti Pantheon, or a Bantu Pantheon [probably Zulu, but there are a lot of choices, with a ton of overlap]<br /> - Finnish<br /> - Hopi/Puebloan (Grandmother Spider would of course be great to see... she could show up in the Navajo Pantheon, but she's a much more major Puebloan figure; other Kachinas of note include Crow Mother, Kokopelli, Mongwa, Eototo, Mana the Corn Maiden, etc)<br /> - Inca<br /> - Indonesian<br /> - Inuit (we have to get Raven in somewhere! And here we also get the likes of Sedna, Igaluk, Nanook, etc!) <br /> - Philippines (the Diwatas defintely deserve to be a separate Pantheon from the Atua)<br /> - The OTHER major Slavic Pantheon, depending on whether the Demigod one is Baltic or Russian<br /> - Turkic/Mongol Pantheon of Tengrism and proto-Tengrism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T03:02:07-07:00","id":969114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=969038#post969038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - At least one other African Pantheon. My main suggestions would be a Khoisan Pantheon, an Mbuti Pantheon, or a Bantu Pantheon [probably Zulu, but there are a lot of choices, with a ton of overlap]<br /> - The OTHER major Slavic Pantheon, depending on whether the Demigod one is Baltic or Russian<br /> - Turkic/Mongol Pantheon of Tengrism and proto-Tengrism</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest Berber or Nubian for another African pantheon... if information on them wasn't so scarce they might as well have not existed. It's possible we could have one or both of them show up as a 'sub-pantheon' (or whatever the Loa are to the Orisha) of the Egyptians, though.<br /> <br /> I agree about having both sets of Slavic gods, though one could argue that there isn't a Baltic pantheon - there's the Lithuanian pantheon, Latvian pantheon and 'Prussian' pantheon. The Lithuanian and Latvian pantheons at least are similar enough that most people probably wouldn't mind too much if they were combined, though.<br /> <br /> Turkic/Mongolian mythology is... spotty, at best. I like it and if a 'Tengri pantheon' was a kickstarter goal for any of the Scion 2E books I'd be more than happy to pay, but information about that belief in it's own language is hard to get - information about it in english is practically nonexistant as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> --EDIT--<br /> <br /> I feel like I should clarify myself here a bit. I know that the Nubian and Berber mythologies aren't denominations of the Egyptian mythologies in any way, but they are very connected to the Netjer and that's why I mentioned making them a 'sub-pantheon'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":"09-14-2016, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:15:51-07:00","id":969208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968068#post968068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's two families though, Don and Llyr.... and it's to be a mouthful for have both together. I'd just go with Tylwythau (Kindreds/Families) or Dau Tylwythau (Two Families/Kindreds) or just Tylwyth. It has the benefits of parallelism with Tuatha and with a sorta-antecedent with the 'sidhe analogue&quot; being the Tylwyth Teg.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll keep that in mind. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:21:46-07:00","id":969213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=969038#post969038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- At least one Aboriginal Australian Pantheon. Not to say one Pantheon can incorporate the entire continent's worth of cultural lore, but find the tradition that is most well known and lean in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept of the Dreamtime is interesting to me, since it suggests - in Scion terms - a pantheon that has an Overworld and <i>not</i> an Underworld. There's a few that are the reverse or have Overworlds they rarely use (like the Netjer), but vanishingly few (like the Alihah) have just an Overworld and no Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:54:55-07:00","id":969229,"title":"","content":"Just reading over the scope of your future plans for Scion 2nd edition makes me feel like this game is going to be simply amazing. Thank you Neall for putting so much passion and effort into giving Scion 2nd Edition a true chance of being one of the best tabletops ever made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:12:40-07:00","id":969257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968833#post968833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly what I meant. Many folks are asking for pantheons that represent specific tribes of First Nations people in North America, Africa, and Australia. But in a world where the old Gods are REAL, but where monotheism isn't unknown, the borders of assorted cultures are going to be different from what we see in our world, and so a pantheon that is made up of deities from several tribes [who may have banded together to survive in the face of Western encroachment] isn't too far-fetched. Perhaps the Gods of different pantheons agreed to cooperate to resist outside influences, or because political alliances changed. Just because our real world has distinct [but not very well-documented] pantheons for all of these regions, doesn't mean that the game has to in order to still be good, fun, and representative of assorted beliefs. It isn't a religious text - it's an RPG. Our world froze many of these faiths in time because they were supplanted by our monotheistic systems and peoples, or their cultures were destroyed/absorbed/suppressed, but the world of Scion isn't like that [or at least, that isn't the core point of the game]; it is still a dynamic, changing world, where the Gods are real, and so beliefs and groupings would logically change through the centuries. To me, that seems a lot more fascinating and engaging than leaving the status quo as it was when [for example] Ancient Egypt ceased to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, it kinda does... If this pantheon of gods is real and that pantheon of gods is real and neither of them requires that it adhere to the vicissitudes of their respective mortal cultures (meaning the vector is not PEOPLE &gt; GODS, but, more likely, GODS &gt; PEOPLE) then why do they have to split up, merge, fall into decline, whatever along the same lines of what is happening to their peoples? Relationships between pantheons aren't really much of a thing in mythology, so that's all up in the air. E.g. the Hittities, the then current iteration of the Mesopotamian, Canaanite and Egyptian pantheons didn't have a big meeting about the incursion of the Sea Peoples, there isn't a myth about Isis and Osiris going to Olympus and hammering out an agreement for their introduction into the Roman sphere of cults.... not that those things can't have happened in Scion, the probably should have and did, but that's not something we can take from mythology. The ground always gets at least a little unstable when religion is being used as definition in Scion and not Scion. (And it's typically more than a little unstable. It's decisively divisive. And Scion is, as always, as about mythology tons and tons more than it's about religion). Sure, you could say &quot;One Pantheon&quot; for the Oji-Cree, but that's a made-up thing, since the two were completely separate peoples that ended up on the same reservation and there wasn't a conflation of their respective mythos insomuch as both syncretized to Christianity. <br /> <br /> What we probably shouldn't do is just start mashing distinct pantheons together for the sake convenience. Sure it's easier to deal with all the North American Native pantheons as one. But that's got all sorts of problems, and a lot of them are really bad ones. That badness doesn't go away completely by just doing it in big chunks that are more representative some arbitrary consideration that doesn't have anything to do with the mythologies involved. There are a lot ways to get around it: clearly shared deities, the so-called &quot;confedreacies&quot; of inter-related pantheons and so on. Those are all determined by the mythology, though, not just the religion (there might only need to be one Manannan between the Irish and Welsh pantheons and there may similarly be one Maui between the Maori and Hawaiian, but Tangaroa of the Maori and Tanaroa of the Hawaiians aren't the same dude at all, anymore than it's really possible to make Llew and Lugh into one guy without mental contortionism...) But, even though an Australian Aboriginee &quot;Confederacy&quot; might work (I don't think it would terribly well.. maybe 2-4 distinct groups... which could be big sprawling pantheons or smaller confederacies), you shouldn't glom together Native American groups that don't really have anything to do with each other other than the catastrophe of their histories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:51:44-07:00","id":969316,"title":"","content":"What's the status of the Iroquois pantheon in Scion, does anyone know? I'm part Mohawk, so this is of some personal interest to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","user":"notanautomaton","date":". 09-14-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:40:58-07:00","id":969584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=969316#post969316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the status of the Iroquois pantheon in Scion, does anyone know? I'm part Mohawk, so this is of some personal interest to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall mentioned on the previous page, that since there's the concept of Manitou, but a distinctly different idea and lore about them from the Algonquian concept, that the idea was that Ioskeha and Tawiscara could be related cousins of the (Algonquin) Manitou who don't get along with their relatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:29:25-07:00","id":969628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=969257#post969257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, it kinda does... If this pantheon of gods is real and that pantheon of gods is real and neither of them requires that it adhere to the vicissitudes of their respective mortal cultures (meaning the vector is not PEOPLE &gt; GODS, but, more likely, GODS &gt; PEOPLE) then why do they have to split up, merge, fall into decline, whatever along the same lines of what is happening to their peoples? Relationships between pantheons aren't really much of a thing in mythology, so that's all up in the air. E.g. the Hittities, the then current iteration of the Mesopotamian, Canaanite and Egyptian pantheons didn't have a big meeting about the incursion of the Sea Peoples, there isn't a myth about Isis and Osiris going to Olympus and hammering out an agreement for their introduction into the Roman sphere of cults.... not that those things can't have happened in Scion, the probably should have and did, but that's not something we can take from mythology. The ground always gets at least a little unstable when religion is being used as definition in Scion and not Scion. (And it's typically more than a little unstable. It's decisively divisive. And Scion is, as always, as about mythology tons and tons more than it's about religion). Sure, you could say &quot;One Pantheon&quot; for the Oji-Cree, but that's a made-up thing, since the two were completely separate peoples that ended up on the same reservation and there wasn't a conflation of their respective mythos insomuch as both syncretized to Christianity.<br /> <br /> What we probably shouldn't do is just start mashing distinct pantheons together for the sake convenience. Sure it's easier to deal with all the North American Native pantheons as one. But that's got all sorts of problems, and a lot of them are really bad ones. That badness doesn't go away completely by just doing it in big chunks that are more representative some arbitrary consideration that doesn't have anything to do with the mythologies involved. There are a lot ways to get around it: clearly shared deities, the so-called &quot;confedreacies&quot; of inter-related pantheons and so on. Those are all determined by the mythology, though, not just the religion (there might only need to be one Manannan between the Irish and Welsh pantheons and there may similarly be one Maui between the Maori and Hawaiian, but Tangaroa of the Maori and Tanaroa of the Hawaiians aren't the same dude at all, anymore than it's really possible to make Llew and Lugh into one guy without mental contortionism...) But, even though an Australian Aboriginee &quot;Confederacy&quot; might work (I don't think it would terribly well.. maybe 2-4 distinct groups... which could be big sprawling pantheons or smaller confederacies), you shouldn't glom together Native American groups that don't really have anything to do with each other other than the catastrophe of their histories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says the Gods DIDN'T have a big meeting about the Sea Peoples? Just because the human legends that we have don't say they did, if we're assuming they are real [and in Scion at least, they are], why would humanity know everything that the Gods actually discussed? The legends are specific to cultures, because the cultures on our world told the myths and stories. In a world of real Gods, that wouldn't necessarily be the case. As you say, GODS &gt; PEOPLE, and they don't need us or owe us an explanation or accounting of everything they did/do. I'm not arguing that different real-world cultures don't have valid, distinct, and important religions, faiths, and myths. They absolutely do. I'm just saying that an RPG isn't the place to try to give every one a valid, detailed, culturally accurate in-game accounting that can be used in games; there isn't time to research it all, there isn't enough solid info about many of them, and so guessing would be involved, and I honestly feel that anyone who is running a campaign that requires multiple First Nations pantheons in detail would probably do the research themselves anyway. We don't have to &quot;mash them up&quot;. We just have to say, &quot;The Aztecs, Mayans, Incans, and Guarani are enough to cover most of Mesoamerican and South American Myth for gaming, and we can leave the Olmecs, Toltecs, Moche, and Muisca for another time/place&quot;. The same goes for North America, Europe, Africa, Australia, and Asia - we can't get them all in, don't have details on every deity who was worshipped, and don't have space/time to cover it all unless we publish &quot;Pantheons of Scion, a work in 23 volumes&quot;. Which might be cool, but it isn't practical....There's room to cover additional pantheons later - but even so, not every one is worthy of a full treatment. And that's WITHOUT assuming that pantheons might have died out, gone to war, or joined together in the last 2,000+ years of history on a modern world with multiple deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:50:06-07:00","id":970247,"title":"","content":"I believe, if I am reading you correct, we are in complete agreement about cross-mythos interactions. There aren't any myths of multi-pantheon divine summits, but they almost certainly took place in the world of Scion. Unless the pantheon is really solipsistic, they are going to know that those guys over there worship somebody different and have different overworlds, underworlds etc.<br /> <br /> You CAN'T give a detailed description. Myths and religions and all are confusing things that create moving targets that are hard to pin down. Even when you have a LOT to work with, like, say the Greeks or the Hindu, you still have to settle on things and exclude others. It's an editorial choice or its unworkable chaos.<br /> <br /> You can say that pantheons will not be covered for practical reasons. Like &quot;They won't all fit into the books&quot; or &quot;We don't have money to pay people&quot; or &quot;Sure, fans can do it, but it won't be &quot;official&quot; because we're not having an open license for this game for various money related reasons&quot;. To say you CAN'T create pantheons for groups that have robust mythologies that just aren't well known is intellectual laziness... Why not? Because we're not going to plumb those myths for 12 gods, some monsters, whatever is replacing PSPs, and some magic items and a signature character or four? It's possible to put together a working pantheon for a game night in a few hours if it's going to see limited use. It's not too hard for a full on gaming company to do it up much better with the resources of several writers, a line developer, etc. It's just whether or not it's worth it. Nothing should be tossed for the sake of convenience. If it can't be done NOW, it shouldn't just be consigned to never-never land. &quot;Not only are we not detailing the pantheon of the Asmat/Chumash/Lenape/Saami/Waka/Athapaskan/Basque, WE NEVER WILL. We're just ignoring them and consigning them to Oblivion?&quot; Why?<br /> <br /> As for, &quot;We're not covering the Olmecs and Toltecs and Moche&quot; Of course they're not. At best, they can make them up, pretty much out of whole cloth. There's no there there. No mythology. It's archaeology. It's art. It's like the so-called &quot;Nemetondevos&quot;. You've got a handful of inscriptions, some art and a little bit of mention that's pretty much loaded with syncretism to the point of uselessness. And, for those tribes, you really have to go with just the art and archaeology. Sure, you can create it all and dress it up to make it look cool and ancient, but it's pretty much almost as fictional as the Atlantean pantheon, the Cthulhu pantheon or the Narnia pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:03:14-07:00","id":970354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=970247#post970247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe, if I am reading you correct, we are in complete agreement about cross-mythos interactions. There aren't any myths of multi-pantheon divine summits, but they almost certainly took place in the world of Scion. Unless the pantheon is really solipsistic, they are going to know that those guys over there worship somebody different and have different overworlds, underworlds etc.<br /> <br /> You CAN'T give a detailed description. Myths and religions and all are confusing things that create moving targets that are hard to pin down. Even when you have a LOT to work with, like, say the Greeks or the Hindu, you still have to settle on things and exclude others. It's an editorial choice or its unworkable chaos.<br /> <br /> You can say that pantheons will not be covered for practical reasons. Like &quot;They won't all fit into the books&quot; or &quot;We don't have money to pay people&quot; or &quot;Sure, fans can do it, but it won't be &quot;official&quot; because we're not having an open license for this game for various money related reasons&quot;. To say you CAN'T create pantheons for groups that have robust mythologies that just aren't well known is intellectual laziness... Why not? Because we're not going to plumb those myths for 12 gods, some monsters, whatever is replacing PSPs, and some magic items and a signature character or four? It's possible to put together a working pantheon for a game night in a few hours if it's going to see limited use. It's not too hard for a full on gaming company to do it up much better with the resources of several writers, a line developer, etc. It's just whether or not it's worth it. Nothing should be tossed for the sake of convenience. If it can't be done NOW, it shouldn't just be consigned to never-never land. &quot;Not only are we not detailing the pantheon of the Asmat/Chumash/Lenape/Saami/Waka/Athapaskan/Basque, WE NEVER WILL. We're just ignoring them and consigning them to Oblivion?&quot; Why?<br /> <br /> As for, &quot;We're not covering the Olmecs and Toltecs and Moche&quot; Of course they're not. At best, they can make them up, pretty much out of whole cloth. There's no there there. No mythology. It's archaeology. It's art. It's like the so-called &quot;Nemetondevos&quot;. You've got a handful of inscriptions, some art and a little bit of mention that's pretty much loaded with syncretism to the point of uselessness. And, for those tribes, you really have to go with just the art and archaeology. Sure, you can create it all and dress it up to make it look cool and ancient, but it's pretty much almost as fictional as the Atlantean pantheon, the Cthulhu pantheon or the Narnia pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are in agreement about the cross-pantheon stuff, absolutely. As for the rest, sure it's possible to come up with 12 gods and some other stuff for a given group - my point is, it isn't necessarily a requirement to make the game work. As long as &quot;build your own&quot; guidelines are in there, then the company doesn't need to make them all, and it isn't likely they would all get used anyway. Not because they don't matter, but because it's hair-splitting in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:33:28-07:00","id":972171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=969213#post969213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept of the Dreamtime is interesting to me, since it suggests - in Scion terms - a pantheon that has an Overworld and <i>not</i> an Underworld. There's a few that are the reverse or have Overworlds they rarely use (like the Netjer), but vanishingly few (like the Alihah) have just an Overworld and no Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm remembering my stories correctly, the Dreamtime was the age where the world was being ceated. The Dreaming is sort of the primordial chaos from before the world and the afterlife and the home of at least some of the 'gods'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:42:43-07:00","id":972177,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind a supplement of additional gods for the existing Pantheons, both exploring what it means to not be one of the major players of your Pantheon and because it gives us more player options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T00:16:12-07:00","id":972977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons.<br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's such a fun slate of things; I'm stoked to see pretty much all of this. Is Canaanite as close as you'll ever want to get to touching the oft-requested Abrahamic? And is there any hope of the Ainu sneaking in somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:03:25-07:00","id":974716,"title":"","content":"The OP should add the Yoruba to your list. The Loa and the Gallic Pantheons have been added to the Scion: Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-22-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:28:44-07:00","id":974731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=972977#post972977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's such a fun slate of things; I'm stoked to see pretty much all of this. Is Canaanite as close as you'll ever want to get to touching the oft-requested Abrahamic? And is there any hope of the Ainu sneaking in somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on the form of Abramic religion. The Caanites were related to all of them to some degree, but the Islamic faith is closer to the, Asnam (not the Vampire bloodline, the actual pre Islamic Arabian Pantheon, of which Allah was the moon god).<br /> <br /> Christianity has far more mixed influences and in fact the Voudon and Christianity share Saints.<br /> <br /> Of course you could just go with the Choir, Archangels Abrahamic pantheon.<br /> <br /> Abramhamic Pantheons aside Jainist, Tibetian, Lithuanian, Tengrian, Etrustrucan, Minoan, Inca, Hungarian, Orishas, some African, Siberian Pantheons could cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:07:06-07:00","id":974761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=974731#post974731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the form of Abramic religion. The Caanites were related to all of them to some degree, but the Islamic faith is closer to the, Asnam (not the Vampire bloodline, the actual pre Islamic Arabian Pantheon, of which Allah was the moon god).<br /> <br /> Christianity has far more mixed influences and in fact the Voudon and Christianity share Saints.<br /> <br /> Of course you could just go with the Choir, Archangels Abrahamic pantheon.<br /> <br /> Abramhamic Pantheons aside Jainist, Tibetian, Lithuanian, Tengrian, Etrustrucan, Minoan, Inca, Hungarian, Orishas, some African, Siberian Pantheons could cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Tibetan Pantheon that lets you be a Scion of one of the wrathful Herukas would be super cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T14:25:39-07:00","id":975696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=968776#post968776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, I'd like to have the Nemetondevos, Loa, and Yazata as stretch goals. So, 2.5 pantheons.<br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b>'s current slate is the Mespotamia, Mayan, Polynesian, Slavic, and Navajo pantheons. I'd <i>really</i> like to do the Welsh pantheon in a larger <b>Demigod</b>-era book of Arthurian myth. I'm also considering Lakota, Caananite, and Guarani for other supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arthurian Myth book with the Welsh Pantheon? yes please. <br /> <br /> question, the gallic pantheon is going to happen, so what is it? is it the nemetondevos? cause if so, im even more happy. <br /> <br /> The fact that you have ideas for bigger supplements and more just gets me more excited to see what you'll come up with next!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T16:12:52-07:00","id":975726,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Nemetondevos are the destroyed Gallic Pantheon that has potential to rise again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T18:23:50-07:00","id":975754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=975726#post975726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Nemetondevos are the destroyed Gallic Pantheon that has potential to rise again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more of a terminology thing. The Nemetondevos is the Gallic pantheon and and the Theoi is the Greek Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T20:18:11-07:00","id":975794,"title":"","content":"Yes? Did I imply otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:34:29-07:00","id":975854,"title":"","content":"In my feverish little dreams, I imagine the final stretch goal for the crowdfunding campaign is an Angelic Pantheon, which nicely sates the itch for an Abrahamic one without having the whole mess that comes with every Scion basically being a new Jesus. Bonus points if there's some sort of nod to the divide between angels mentioned in actual Jewish/Christian/Islamic texts and those that exist as the more recent creations of occultists since the 1600s.<br /> <br /> Hell, a Goetic Pantheon might be a fun pet project! Obviously not detailing all 72 of them (sorry, Stolas, you're adorable but we just can't spare the wordcount for an owl who teaches people about herbs), but some of the more popular demons could make perfectly fine divine (infernal?) parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:15:04-07:00","id":976751,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I've always said that the Abrahamic pantheons don't belong in Scion. First, because they are part of the real-world faiths that tend to get really hot under the collar when you try to personify them, and second, because it's a game of the ancient religions and myths, not modern ones. They aren't needed in order to make it a dynamic, immersive, and enjoyable fictional world, and trying to work out who to include, how to deal with &quot;Thou shalt have no other Gods&quot;, and how to try to shoehorn real-world faith alongside ancient faith [really, would Islam have allowed the Alihah to continue? Or Christianity to tolerate &quot;pagan&quot; faiths? They didn't in the real world], just make a whole lot of extra headaches for everyone, If you want to house rule Abrahamic faiths, go for it. But my vote is, keep them out of the official releases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T16:05:18-07:00","id":976780,"title":"","content":"I would like to add, however, that Scion already adds ways of life such as Shinto that are actually believed by people today in the world, along with other paths such as the Yoruba and others. So Scion already has to deal with real world believers (such as myself) when it comes to the depictions of dieties and so forth.<br /> <br /> I mean Christianity, Judaism and Islam can't be that intolerant of personification, can it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T16:08:47-07:00","id":976782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976780#post976780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to add, however, that Scion already adds ways of life such as Shinto that are actually believed by people today in the world, along with other paths such as the Yoruba and others. So Scion already has to deal with real world believers (such as myself) when it comes to the depictions of dieties and so forth.<br /> <br /> I mean Christianity, Judaism and Islam can't be that intolerant of personification, can it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Deva. Quite a few actually modern religions are represented in the various pantheons. What is it that makes Abrahamic faiths so special compared to other actual living religions?<br /> <br /> (just to be clear the question isn't aimed at Ostarion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:44:37-07:00","id":976835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976751#post976751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I've always said that the Abrahamic pantheons don't belong in Scion. First, because they are part of the real-world faiths that tend to get really hot under the collar when you try to personify them, and second, because it's a game of the ancient religions and myths, not modern ones. They aren't needed in order to make it a dynamic, immersive, and enjoyable fictional world, and trying to work out who to include, how to deal with &quot;Thou shalt have no other Gods&quot;, and how to try to shoehorn real-world faith alongside ancient faith [really, would Islam have allowed the Alihah to continue? Or Christianity to tolerate &quot;pagan&quot; faiths? They didn't in the real world], just make a whole lot of extra headaches for everyone, If you want to house rule Abrahamic faiths, go for it. But my vote is, keep them out of the official releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to the Deva, who <i>totally</i> don't have real-world followers. And the Abrahamic faiths aren't ancient? Really? 2000+ years is too modern for your table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:51:25-07:00","id":976840,"title":"","content":"They are the currently embraced Western faiths that seem to drive most of the emotion and frustration in today's world, which is what I mean by &quot;modern&quot;. Not being a Hindu/Sikh, I can't say whether the inclusion of that pantheon would offend the followers of the faith, and I'm sure there are living worshippers for pretty much anything you can come up with - we can't avoid offending everyone, it's true. But I personally [and it's my own opinion here] find that the inclusion of God/Jesus/Allah/Mohammed/Angels just gets people's dander up far too easily, and isn't worth it for the mileage you would get out of the inclusion of such a pantheon in Scion. But now that the &quot;Design your own pantheon&quot; rules are a stretch goal, it's all a moot point, because we can all write up whichever deities we want for our own games, and go crazy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:53:35-07:00","id":976842,"title":"","content":"You should probably use a descriptor other than &quot;modern&quot; to describe those &quot;currently embraced Western faiths,&quot; then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:54:08-07:00","id":976844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976780#post976780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to add, however, that Scion already adds ways of life such as Shinto that are actually believed by people today in the world, along with other paths such as the Yoruba and others. So Scion already has to deal with real world believers (such as myself) when it comes to the depictions of dieties and so forth.<br /> <br /> I mean Christianity, Judaism and Islam can't be that intolerant of personification, can it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some followers of Islam have declared Fatwah on people who represent Mohammed or Allah in fiction or imagery in recent memory, so, yes, they can. Christians and Jews are a little more forgiving, but there's still the matter of which version to represent, and there are as many opinions as people. I'm not trying to start a fight here - this is a very touchy topic. And that's why I'm suggesting we leave it out of an official game release, and let folks write up whatever works for them in their own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":".  Edited to clarify a definition and not make a sweeping generalisation. 09-26-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:55:20-07:00","id":976845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976844#post976844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Islam has declared Fatwah on people who represent Mohammed or Allah in fiction or imagery in recent memory, so, yes, they can. Christians and Jews are a little more forgiving, but there's still the matter of which version to represent, and there are as many opinions as people. I'm not trying to start a fight here - this is a very touch topic. And that's why I'm suggesting we leave it out of an official game release, and let folks write up whatever works for them in their own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Islam. Some Muslems. Don't try to paint the entire religion as an undifferentiated block of beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:56:26-07:00","id":976846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976842#post976842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should probably use a descriptor other than &quot;modern&quot; to describe those &quot;currently embraced Western faiths,&quot; then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, using &quot;modern&quot; is the wrong term - Hindiusm/Sikhism/Shintoism/Buddhism, and many more, are perfectly &quot;modern&quot;. Then let's use &quot;Abrahamic faiths&quot; to reference Christianity, Judaism, and Islam, and leave it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:57:55-07:00","id":976848,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that it is sacrosanct to represent the Prophet in image, as a written rule of Islam. How angry you get about breaking that rule is, of course, up to the individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:05:27-07:00","id":976851,"title":"","content":"Right, and I would say the majority of Muslims would not feel moved to kill people for doing it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in a world with <b>Preacher</b>, I find it hard to believe that representing Christianity in game mechanics would be a step too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:13:14-07:00","id":976854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976851#post976851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, and I would say the majority of Muslims would not feel moved to kill people for doing it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in a world with <b>Preacher</b>, I find it hard to believe that representing Christianity in game mechanics would be a step too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shin Megami Tensei series depicts YHVH as a selfish asshole that you can fight and kill, and the worst blowback it's ever had was one guy being mad that Krishna is depicted as a villain. This isn't the Satanic Panic anymore, and White Wolf already made the much more blasphemous Demon: the Fallen back in the day; I'm not sure &quot;hey, you can be a powerful servant of God!&quot; is really all that horrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-26-2016, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:23:35-07:00","id":976857,"title":"","content":"I guess the most controversial thing OP could do would be to explicitly make it henotheistic instead of strictly monotheistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T18:56:31-07:00","id":976872,"title":"","content":"I'll point out that White Wolf created the Asnam bloodline, the name of which is based on the pre Islamic Pantheon, of which Allah was a member, the Moon God.<br /> <br /> The OWOD leaned heavily towards to depicting monotheism. NWOD and CoD lean more towards polytheism, with perhaps agnostic elements over all, with one or two exceptions, and even those are iffy on the point.<br /> <br /> So my point is its not like White Wolf or Onyx Path has never dealt with Monotheism before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:08:51-07:00","id":977027,"title":"","content":"I guess part of my personal objection is that I see and hear enough of the Abraham faiths in the real world, and I want my escapism to be escapism. My own personal quirk, I admit, but I don't want Jesus in my Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:28:39-07:00","id":977039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977027#post977027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess part of my personal objection is that I see and hear enough of the Abraham faiths in the real world, and I want my escapism to be escapism. My own personal quirk, I admit, but I don't want Jesus in my Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Abrahamic faiths have enough interesting stuff to draw upon for a crazy mythological urban fantasy. While I can't speak for anyone else, I love the idea of playing a Chosen of Gabriel who's armed with a spear that contains a sliver of the Spear of Destiny who is fighting off Cyclopes and kitsune and all the other threats out of mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T03:00:01-07:00","id":977084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977039#post977039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Abrahamic faiths have enough interesting stuff to draw upon for a crazy mythological urban fantasy. While I can't speak for anyone else, I love the idea of playing a Chosen of Gabriel who's armed with a spear that contains a sliver of the Spear of Destiny who is fighting off Cyclopes and kitsune and all the other threats out of mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly an interesting idea, and there's more than enough to draw upon with the angelic hosts in terms of power and variety without going anywhere near the Big Guy Himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:17:13-07:00","id":977532,"title":"","content":"An idea I toyed with in a First edition game is that the Angelic Pantheon claim the other Pantheons are all Grigori, and their Scions are Nephilim. The Angels never reproduce with mortals (that's what got the Grigori kicked out), but will adopt Scions born to other Pantheons who reject their Grigori parent out of faith in the One True God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:05:10-07:00","id":977618,"title":"","content":"I remember thinking at one point that one thing that doesn't grok well with the Scion mechanics (feel free to say I'm wrong) with the Abrahamic Monotheistic religion? Well, a BIG thing about Scion's cosmology is that it's the Gods of old versus the ancient and impossibly powerful Titans.<br /> <br /> What Titans come from the Abrahamic religions? How does that grok with the belief of YHWH being an all-powerful, all-knowing, all-loving creator that sculpted the world from chaos... And that God is facing down the Titans, which supposedly are greater even than that God.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, if/when you make that Angelic Host pantheon? I'd be TOTALLY alright with putting that in one of my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:32:03-07:00","id":977629,"title":"","content":"I think in 2e not every pantheon has titans associated with them. In 1e some titans had to be shoehorned to fit in with some of the pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:39:16-07:00","id":977631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977618#post977618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember thinking at one point that one thing that doesn't grok well with the Scion mechanics (feel free to say I'm wrong) with the Abrahamic Monotheistic religion? Well, a BIG thing about Scion's cosmology is that it's the Gods of old versus the ancient and impossibly powerful Titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's much less big/all-encompassing in Second Edition, but it's worth noting that before &quot;Let there be light&quot; when the earth was formless void, there was still the waters. For a Middle Eastern religion that certainly echoes Nun and Tiamat.<br /> <br /> If you're leaning into Christian Angelic Lore for your &quot;deities&quot;, you can do a whole thing with Lucifer, the Lightbringer born from the words &quot;Let there be light&quot; having to battle back the primordial darkness/chaos/waters/whatever to make room for Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-28-2016, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:08:48-07:00","id":977882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976751#post976751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I've always said that the Abrahamic pantheons don't belong in Scion. First, because they are part of the real-world faiths that tend to get really hot under the collar when you try to personify them, and second, because it's a game of the ancient religions and myths, not modern ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on who you ask, Judaism is older than Greek mythology, though not quite as old as Egyptian mythology. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976751#post976751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't needed in order to make it a dynamic, immersive, and enjoyable fictional world, and trying to work out who to include, how to deal with &quot;Thou shalt have no other Gods&quot;, and how to try to shoehorn real-world faith alongside ancient faith [really, would Islam have allowed the Alihah to continue? Or Christianity to tolerate &quot;pagan&quot; faiths? They didn't in the real world], just make a whole lot of extra headaches for everyone, If you want to house rule Abrahamic faiths, go for it. But my vote is, keep them out of the official releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>OTOH, if you want a setting that even vaguely resembles the modern world, you need at least Christianity and Islam. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:15:26-07:00","id":977884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977629#post977629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in 2e not every pantheon has titans associated with them. In 1e some titans had to be shoehorned to fit in with some of the pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The \u00f2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0 and loa have no associated Titans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:20:34-07:00","id":977888,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah; the Loa. Exactly how do you do <i>them</i> in a setting without Christianity, considering that Voodoo blends African beliefs with Christian ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:38:03-07:00","id":977902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977888#post977888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah; the Loa. Exactly how do you do <i>them</i> in a setting without Christianity, considering that Voodoo blends African beliefs with Christian ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every religion that exists in the real world exists in the World as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:41:03-07:00","id":977905,"title":"","content":"My thing was less about YHWH not having a designated titan and more, well...<br /> <br /> Okay, one of the things in the Abrahamic faith is that the big singular creator God is Omnipotent. If this is the case, why is the Titan War a challenge for a literal all-powerful being?<br /> <br /> Of course I suppose that one could argue that YHWH is all-powerful when viewed through a human lens but even that being is not all-powerful within the Overworld and must lend aid against the Titans.<br /> <br /> And I suppose that one could play YHWH as one of those Primordial divine forces that aren't antagonistic, and yet are so overwhelmingly great that they're unable to manifest in The World and still have an overwhelming presence in the Overworld, and most of the interaction is done through angelic servitors, and when the other Pantheons asks if YHWH is there they just say &quot;Of course, he's simply busy&quot; and leave it at that...<br /> <br /> Actually that's something I'd be open to at my table. Hm, thoughts whirling...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:00:42-07:00","id":977917,"title":"","content":"Having an all-powerful God at the top of your Pantheon isn't something unique to the Abrahamic faiths. IIRC, the Devas have something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:48:49-07:00","id":977950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977905#post977905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thing was less about YHWH not having a designated titan and more, well...<br /> <br /> Okay, one of the things in the Abrahamic faith is that the big singular creator God is Omnipotent. If this is the case, why is the Titan War a challenge for a literal all-powerful being?<br /> <br /> Of course I suppose that one could argue that YHWH is all-powerful when viewed through a human lens but even that being is not all-powerful within the Overworld and must lend aid against the Titans.<br /> <br /> And I suppose that one could play YHWH as one of those Primordial divine forces that aren't antagonistic, and yet are so overwhelmingly great that they're unable to manifest in The World and still have an overwhelming presence in the Overworld, and most of the interaction is done through angelic servitors, and when the other Pantheons asks if YHWH is there they just say &quot;Of course, he's simply busy&quot; and leave it at that...<br /> <br /> Actually that's something I'd be open to at my table. Hm, thoughts whirling...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wouldn't have him be quite as powerful as people believe he is. I get the impression no one is omnipotent in Scion, so why make an exception?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:49:36-07:00","id":977951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977950#post977950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just wouldn't have him be quite as powerful as people believe he is. I get the impression no one is omnipotent in Scion, so why make an exception?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also possible. I admit I'm not a religious scholar, so I'm just throwing darts at random reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:00:24-07:00","id":977957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977951#post977951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also possible. I admit I'm not a religious scholar, so I'm just throwing darts at random reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the primordial idea probably works, I'm just hesitant to go there myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:03:36-07:00","id":977960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977888#post977888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah; the Loa. Exactly how do you do <i>them</i> in a setting without Christianity, considering that Voodoo blends African beliefs with Christian ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abrahamic faiths exist, they just likely make less Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:18:24-07:00","id":978022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=977917#post977917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having an all-powerful God at the top of your Pantheon isn't something unique to the Abrahamic faiths. IIRC, the Devas have something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's explicitly the position of the \u00d2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0 and Loa. Dev\u00e1s tend to alter their answer or viewpoint depending on with whom they're speaking at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:19:48-07:00","id":978023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=976751#post976751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I've always said that the Abrahamic pantheons don't belong in Scion. First, because they are part of the real-world faiths that tend to get really hot under the collar when you try to personify them, and second, because it's a game of the ancient religions and myths, not modern ones. They aren't needed in order to make it a dynamic, immersive, and enjoyable fictional world, and trying to work out who to include, how to deal with &quot;Thou shalt have no other Gods&quot;, and how to try to shoehorn real-world faith alongside ancient faith [really, would Islam have allowed the Alihah to continue? Or Christianity to tolerate &quot;pagan&quot; faiths? They didn't in the real world], just make a whole lot of extra headaches for everyone, If you want to house rule Abrahamic faiths, go for it. But my vote is, keep them out of the official releases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Thou shalt have no other gods BEFORE ME&quot; those last words are kind of significant in this situation.<br /> <br /> *does the just make them Henotheists dance*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:40:29-07:00","id":978070,"title":"","content":"In a setting where multiple Pantheons can be confirmed to exist, true monotheism is about as likely as true atheism. The Abrahamic faiths pretty much have to be some flavor of henotheistic, and the closest you're likely to get to an atheist is someone who acknowledges the existence of God-like beings but rejects their Divinity and refuses to worship any of them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T23:18:38-07:00","id":978239,"title":"","content":"Islam, however, has a bit of a problem - &quot;there is no God but God, and Muhammad is his messenger&quot; is part of the profession of faith, one of the pillars of Islam.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver's suggestion is one way around this; another, historically attested in regards to the Devas, is to say that these are manifestations of God in another guise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T23:39:18-07:00","id":978244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978070#post978070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a setting where multiple Pantheons can be confirmed to exist, true monotheism is about as likely as true atheism. The Abrahamic faiths pretty much have to be some flavor of henotheistic, and the closest you're likely to get to an atheist is someone who acknowledges the existence of God-like beings but rejects their Divinity and refuses to worship any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... misotheism, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:14:31-07:00","id":978278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978070#post978070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a setting where multiple Pantheons can be confirmed to exist, true monotheism is about as likely as true atheism. The Abrahamic faiths pretty much have to be some flavor of henotheistic, and the closest you're likely to get to an atheist is someone who acknowledges the existence of God-like beings but rejects their Divinity and refuses to worship any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. This is further compounded by the fact that powerful people in 1st Edition could throw giant buckets of successes into convincing you that there are indeed gods and they are indeed awesome and worthy of worship. What's a poor mortal atheist gonna do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T04:47:31-07:00","id":978310,"title":"","content":"We could go the complete &quot;you wants Jehovah and Allah? You won't like it&quot; route, linking Jehovah with El and Allah with the pre-Islamic Arabian pantheon's moon God. That'd fit Scion's world.<br /> <br /> It would also anger just about everyone.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a good thing Neall's in charge if this, not me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T04:59:58-07:00","id":978313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978310#post978310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could go the complete &quot;you wants Jehovah and Allah? You won't like it&quot; route, linking Jehovah with El and Allah with the pre-Islamic Arabian pantheon's moon God. That'd fit Scion's world.<br /> <br /> It would also anger just about everyone.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a good thing Neall's in charge if this, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you think saying God is the Primordial of Light and his Archangels and Angels are his legend 12 &quot;gods&quot; and Jesus Christ was said primordial scion could also be a good idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-29-2016, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:29:35-07:00","id":978423,"title":"","content":"Is everyone really all that likely to sit down with Scion 2nd edition, look through the 12 pantheons we'really currently getting, and decide to make Christianity the centre-point of their games? Honestly, the theme is &quot;Old Faiths, New World&quot;, and with Odin's apocalypse-dodging schemes, Zeus' womanizing, and all the multitude of other God's and Goddesses to work with, why would you limit yourself to the activities of faiths that are all around you in the real world? I'm not saying you can't, or shouldn't, but this isn't In Nomine, or Supernatural, and shouldn't we be talking about pantheon with other origins? The Inue, Incans, Koreans, or more solitary beings like Makemake or Ranga come to mind, and are more a part of Scion than angels and an all-powerful jealous God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:33:48-07:00","id":978428,"title":"","content":"Including Abrahamic mythology in the setting is not the same thing as making Christianity the centerpoint of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:35:22-07:00","id":978429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978313#post978313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you think saying God is the Primordial of Light and his Archangels and Angels are his legend 12 &amp;quot;gods&amp;quot; and Jesus Christ was said primordial scion could also be a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. I'm not saying people can't do that for their own games (more power to them, and the pantheon creation system would be ideal for that), but I would be bothered if it was canon. The angels and archangels always seem to be servants of God, rather than Gods in their own right. If they are depicted as the equals of the Gods of other pantheons, then it implies the supremacy of one over all the others. It gives Scions of that pantheon the ability to honestly say &quot;The servants of my God are as great as the king of your Gods.&quot; I think that that would bother a lot of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:58:17-07:00","id":978439,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that other faiths (including Hinduism) have many tales of heroes (the titular Scions) who were the offspring or incarnations of the Gods themselves. There aren't a lot of similar stories from Abrahamic faiths, and Islam doesn't even accept that Jesus was the literal son of God. They just don't fit well with the concept of the game, even as background colour, without doing a fair bit of bending, reshaping, and alteration - and then you don't have the original faith anyway. It's simply extremely unlikely that a single being, with no associates, and with no history of siring Scions (with one possible exception, depending who you ask), would be a major player in the Scion world of large, complex, and dynamic pantheons all over the globe. If you want Abrahamic faiths, use the &quot;build your own patheon&quot; rules, but I don't think the game itself needs to spend a lot of time on them, for the sake of theme and space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:03:51-07:00","id":978457,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'll probably use whatever pantheons fit the story that pops into my head. No singular pantheon will ever claim complete dominance or anything that would be considered the center of my games. As I've been discussing on the kickstarter comments, its really only a matter of letting our opinions known about how they could potentially incorporate it without having it take center stage. That doesn't lessen my complete interest in every other pantheon currently confirmed for the game. I am quite content waiting for the Canaanite pantheon to be done even if its after Demigod or with God. If people can't wait though, they got the create a pantheon rules. Anyone expecting a God figure to appear usable in the core or companion is likely going to be disappointed. I'm going to enjoy what we already have... and it is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:13:43-07:00","id":978560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978429#post978429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't. I'm not saying people can't do that for their own games (more power to them, and the pantheon creation system would be ideal for that), but I would be bothered if it was canon. The angels and archangels always seem to be servants of God, rather than Gods in their own right. If they are depicted as the equals of the Gods of other pantheons, then it implies the supremacy of one over all the others. It gives Scions of that pantheon the ability to honestly say &quot;The servants of my God are as great as the king of your Gods.&quot; I think that that would bother a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, the Orisha have been confirmed to hold exactly this view (as have the Loa, and sometimes the Devas). I am curious whether these Pantheons will each include among their ranks suitable Primordials to represent the \u201chigher order of being\u201d that they say they serve, once <b>Scion: God</b> 2e comes out and we get into the Godrealms where such claims can be verified or falsified. I think they're greater contenders for the tour of offense that you're describing than the Abrahamic faiths are, as I could easily see the latter being written up as angels and demons being (almost?) entirely demigod-level beings, with the possible exception of the highest orders of angelic beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978439#post978439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the fact that other faiths (including Hinduism) have many tales of heroes (the titular Scions) who were the offspring or incarnations of the Gods themselves. There aren't a lot of similar stories from Abrahamic faiths, and Islam doesn't even accept that Jesus was the literal son of God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus as the literal son of God is all but unique to Christianity, to the extent that the Messianic Jews are viewed by the Jewish community as Christians masquerading as Jews and/or heretics even beyond <i>atheistic</i> Jews. I'd say that it's the defining feature of Christianity, if not for the existence of self-identified Christian sects that don't buy that notion. But yeah, I'll agree that Abrahamic mythology doesn't have much in the way of scions; and the ones it <i>does</i> have are almost entirely of the Chosen Origin: e.g., the Judge Samson, and the Prophet Elijah. Ironically, I think that <b>Scion: Origin</b> (for the mortal worshippers) and <b>Scion: Demigod</b> (for the angels) would be the tiers where Abrahamic-based characters would fit into the setting of <b>Scion</b> most comfortably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978439#post978439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want Abrahamic faiths, use the &quot;build your own patheon&quot; rules, but I don't think the game itself needs to spend a lot of time on them, for the sake of theme and space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a lot of space needs to be devoted to them. I'd be fine with, say, a text box in <b>Origins</b> describing <b>Scion</b>'s take on the Abrahamic faiths with advice on how to do Abrahamic prophets, and then something in Demigod or God about angels \u2014 just not 1e's ham-handed \u201cangels are Titanspawn of the evil Titan of Light\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978457#post978457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'll probably use whatever pantheons fit the story that pops into my head. No singular pantheon will ever claim complete dominance or anything that would be considered the center of my games. As I've been discussing on the kickstarter comments, its really only a matter of letting our opinions known about how they could potentially incorporate it without having it take center stage. That doesn't lessen my complete interest in every other pantheon currently confirmed for the game. I am quite content waiting for the Canaanite pantheon to be done even if its after Demigod or with God. If people can't wait though, they got the create a pantheon rules. Anyone expecting a God figure to appear usable in the core or companion is likely going to be disappointed. I'm going to enjoy what we already have... and it is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wary of trying it too closely to the Canaanite Pantheon. Sure, Judaism's earliest origins have a strong connection to the Canaanites (though Abraham was called out of the land of the Mesopotamians, and Moses brought the fledgeling people of Israel out of the land of Egypt); but a case could be made that Christianity had strong Greek roots as well as its core Hebrew beliefs, and that Islam arguably owes as much or more to Arabian mythology than to Canaanite mythology. Mantles can potentially help with some of this; but ultimately, I don't want to see the Abrahamic faiths presented strictly part of the Canaanite Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:05:59-07:00","id":978607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978429#post978429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't. I'm not saying people can't do that for their own games (more power to them, and the pantheon creation system would be ideal for that), but I would be bothered if it was canon. The angels and archangels always seem to be servants of God, rather than Gods in their own right. If they are depicted as the equals of the Gods of other pantheons, then it implies the supremacy of one over all the others. It gives Scions of that pantheon the ability to honestly say &quot;The servants of my God are as great as the king of your Gods.&quot; I think that that would bother a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>but both the Yoruba and Aztec faith mentions their gods were spawned by all-powerful &quot;god of everything&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:18:13-07:00","id":978622,"title":"","content":"Running tally of Pantheons that feature a supreme being: Loa, Orisha, Teotl, Vedas(?). Any others? Does the leader of the Celestial Bureaucracy count? How about the Yazata?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:50:25-07:00","id":978650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978622#post978622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running tally of Pantheons that feature a supreme being: Loa, Orisha, Teotl, Vedas(?). Any others? Does the leader of the Celestial Bureaucracy count? How about the Yazata?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you counting Omni-Deities in the tally? That might bump up your total. The Yazata do I'm almost positive, and the CB have Tian, but they're... not really a person, so I don't know if that would count. Places that got touched by Buddhism may in some sects pick up a supreme being too.<br /> <br /> You could probably count Atum-Ra as a borderline supreme being, and Svarog could count. Atum-Ra is able to end creation whenever he feels like it by blinking, and Svarog is going to when he wakes up to create it again, possibly without maiming himself in the process this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:06:16-07:00","id":978662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978650#post978650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you counting Omni-Deities in the tally? That might bump up your total. The Yazata do I'm almost positive, and the CB have Tian, but they're... not really a person, so I don't know if that would count. Places that got touched by Buddhism may in some sects pick up a supreme being too.<br /> <br /> You could probably count Atum-Ra as a borderline supreme being, and Svarog could count. Atum-Ra is able to end creation whenever he feels like it by blinking, and Svarog is going to when he wakes up to create it again, possibly without maiming himself in the process this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>so,we could argue that in the scionverse all those primordial exist together,and God is one of them,not superior nor inferior than any other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:03:13-07:00","id":978692,"title":"","content":"Or, in a manner similar to Mantles, there might only be one supreme deity, who manifests differently in different Pantheons. Maybe. But yeah; \u201cwe believe in a supreme god who is above all others\u201d isn't as big of a hurdle for Scion 2e as one might initially think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:11:18-07:00","id":978695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978310#post978310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could go the complete &amp;quot;you wants Jehovah and Allah? You won't like it&amp;quot; route, linking Jehovah with El and Allah with the pre-Islamic Arabian pantheon's moon God. That'd fit Scion's world.<br /> <br /> It would also anger just about everyone.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a good thing Neall's in charge if this, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now I have Jack Chick's horriblarious MOON GOD!? in my head and it won't leave, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:17:14-07:00","id":978696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978310#post978310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could go the complete &quot;you wants Jehovah and Allah? You won't like it&quot; route, linking Jehovah with El and Allah with the pre-Islamic Arabian pantheon's moon God. That'd fit Scion's world.<br /> <br /> It would also anger just about everyone.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a good thing Neall's in charge if this, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I mean, I'd love that. That's the kind of stretch goal I'd double my pledge for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-29-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:19:53-07:00","id":978699,"title":"","content":"Why don't we let the nice people at Onyx Path completely dodge the issue so that any wrath coming <i>doesn't</i> fall on their heads, and then we the <i>gamers</i> can make up what we feel is necessary? I find it hard to believe that modern gamers are allergic to adding homebrew to their settings, it's practically part and parcel of roleplaying. So why don't we the fans figure something out and let the writers go on not addressing the issue in print?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:11:03-07:00","id":978729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978699#post978699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't we let the nice people at Onyx Path completely dodge the issue so that any wrath coming <i>doesn't</i> fall on their heads, and then we the <i>gamers</i> can make up what we feel is necessary? I find it hard to believe that modern gamers are allergic to adding homebrew to their settings, it's practically part and parcel of roleplaying. So why don't we the fans figure something out and let the writers go on not addressing the issue in print?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah,not saying something just because it might upset others is just silly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:16:12-07:00","id":978814,"title":"","content":"I don't think they're avoiding the issue because they're afraid of offending anyone - I think it just a) doesn't fit into the Pantheon balance and thematic focus of the corebook, and b) it's a complicated question (how monotheistic religions metaphysically fits into a polytheistic setting) they want to take their time with. We know the &quot;Elohim&quot; Pantheon (Caananite/Phoenician) is in the cards, so the issue will be addressed in some form there if it isn't beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:33:00-07:00","id":978822,"title":"","content":"Neall once said that he's holding off on addressing it because he only plans to do so once, and he wants to get it right when he does.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I do think there's a way to address it that will satisfy most fans, as long as you disregard the shattenfreud types who won't be satisfied unless someone else is thoroughly offended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:57:02-07:00","id":978832,"title":"","content":"I have high hopes for the Canaanite Pantheon, but I do think a more straight-on take as a pie in the sky stretch goal for a crowdfunding campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:15:24-07:00","id":979637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978832#post978832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have high hopes for the Canaanite Pantheon, but I do think a more straight-on take as a pie in the sky stretch goal for a crowdfunding campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah the Caanite Patheon would be my top choice for a stretch goal., followed by the Sumerians , Asnam, and Jainist Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Giving that the Loa, Gallic, and Altantis pantheons are in the Companion already, and the Persian Pantheon is next, the question becomes which Pantheon does he offer next time he offers one as a stretch goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-01-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:23:23-07:00","id":979644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=978310#post978310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could go the complete &quot;you wants Jehovah and Allah? You won't like it&quot; route, linking Jehovah with El and Allah with the pre-Islamic Arabian pantheon's moon God. That'd fit Scion's world.<br /> <br /> It would also anger just about everyone.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a good thing Neall's in charge if this, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's exactly what I would like, as it fits perfectly as its historically accurate. I would love it.<br /> <br /> Why so you think everyone would hate it, from a Scion point of view, it makes sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-01-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:16:29-07:00","id":979708,"title":"","content":"Because in a game which its motto is &quot;All Myths are True&quot;, it's kinda not nice for it to specifically say that yours is not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":".  worst grammar ever 10-01-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T22:51:29-07:00","id":984265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=979637#post979637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the Caanite Patheon would be my top choice for a stretch goal., followed by the Sumerians , Asnam, and Jainist Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Neall's mentioned he's aiming for the God book for the Elohim. As for Sumerian, that's likely the same Pantheon as the Babylonian via different names/mantles. They (the Anunna) are slated for Demigod. No idea on the possibility of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:51:18-07:00","id":984630,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Tengrism, Finnish Pantheon, and/or Shawnee Mythology. I'm drawn to the more obscure mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T10:11:55-07:00","id":984928,"title":"","content":"So with the Frost purview being a thing that's going to be created, I hope another stretch goal is to put another ice themed pantheon in the companion. Specifically, one of my players as requested a polar bear god, so I'm hoping the Inuit pantheon comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T10:13:47-07:00","id":984930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=984928#post984928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the Frost purview being a thing that's going to be created, I hope another stretch goal is to put another ice themed pantheon in the companion. Specifically, one of my players as requested a polar bear god, so I'm hoping the Inuit pantheon comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last we knew, Neall had the Inuit on the slate for a future supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:59:41-07:00","id":985574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want#post444750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, new in this case means that The Greek, Egyptian, Norse, Aztec, Voodoo, Japanese, Persian, Irish, Vedic, and Chinese, pantheons are already covered. Which other non-fictional pantheons do the people on these boards want? Note: Fictional Pantheons would describe the Atlantean Pantheon and the Nationalistic Pantheons in the WWII setting in the Scion Companion. It would also cover Tolkien's elvish pantheons or anything by Moorcock or Fritz Lieber. This thread focuses on mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of gods from the Americas bothered me considerably.<br /> <br /> While it isn't a treatise on comparative religion, I think it'd be nice, especially for the people who want to explore the ancient stories of their ancestors. I'm already covered with the Germanic/Norse and the Greek, but someone coming in from a native American perspective is going to be sorely left out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-11-2016, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:24:50-07:00","id":985598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=985574#post985574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of gods from the Americas bothered me considerably.<br /> <br /> While it isn't a treatise on comparative religion, I think it'd be nice, especially for the people who want to explore the ancient stories of their ancestors. I'm already covered with the Germanic/Norse and the Greek, but someone coming in from a native American perspective is going to be sorely left out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Algonquian is in Hero, Mayan and Navajo are in Demigod, and then the Lakota, Inuit, and Guarani have all been mentioned as stretch goals for later crowdfunding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:23:52-07:00","id":985627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=985598#post985598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Algonquian is in Hero, Mayan and Navajo are in Demigod, and then the Lakota, Inuit, and Guarani have all been mentioned as stretch goals for later crowdfunding.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Mm. All Neall's said on the Lakota, Inuit and Guarani is they're slated for later supplements. Doesn't necessarily mean crowdfunded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:53:09-07:00","id":985697,"title":"","content":"i'm waiting for the anansi's pantheon and the russian one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:41:15-07:00","id":998665,"title":"","content":"Sorry for, once again, reviving this thread, but... how dumb/weird would it be to try and make the Germanic pantheon their own entity, instead of just alternate titles [and in some cases, Mantles] for the Aesir?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:51:56-07:00","id":998683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=998665#post998665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for, once again, reviving this thread, but... how dumb/weird would it be to try and make the Germanic pantheon their own entity, instead of just alternate titles [and in some cases, Mantles] for the Aesir?</div> </div> </div> </div>I one time tried to make writeups for having the Alicorns from Friendship is Magic as patron goddesses. There was discussion earlier about possibly using Batman as a God.<br /> <br /> Your idea isn't even a blip on the Weird Idea O-Meter. Go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T01:53:54-08:00","id":999125,"title":"","content":"Well if we're doing