class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=998683#post998683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I one time tried to make writeups for having the Alicorns from Friendship is Magic as patron goddesses. There was discussion earlier about possibly using Batman as a God.<br /> <br /> Your idea isn't even a blip on the Weird Idea O-Meter. Go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Odin: Oh I see, you have a reckless sibling as well? Don't feel too bad about trapping her within the moon, when my brother acts up I chain him up in a cave with his son's own entrails, and a poisonous serpent dripping venom into his eyes.<br /> <br /> Celestia: *Horrified* &quot;I... I think I'll be going now, it was lovely speaking with you!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:29:38-08:00","id":999403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999214#post999214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's someone else's IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>So just don't SELL it. Say &quot;Hey all I made this free supplement if you wanted to play the son of Sarenrae!&quot;<br /> <br /> (And why wouldn't you want to play a Scion of Sarenrae? Sarenrae is fucking awesome)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:54:20-08:00","id":999413,"title":"","content":"Sorry I thought they were saying they wanted to see it printed in an actual release. If that's not what they meant, I agree someone can write it up online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:12:50-08:00","id":999425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=985574#post985574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of gods from the Americas bothered me considerably.<br /> <br /> While it isn't a treatise on comparative religion, I think it'd be nice, especially for the people who want to explore the ancient stories of their ancestors. I'm already covered with the Germanic/Norse and the Greek, but someone coming in from a native American perspective is going to be sorely left out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused about what you mean - the Manitou (Algonquin) and the Teotl (Aztec) are among the core 10!<br /> <br /> We've also had Navajo and Mayan confirmed for Demigod. Lakota, Inuit, Inca, and Guarani have been mentioned as waiting down the line as well (I personally would also hope for a Hopi/Puebloan Kachina Pantheon, but that's unconfirmed at this point).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:32:33-08:00","id":999666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999425#post999425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally would also hope for a Hopi/Puebloan Kachina Pantheon, but that's unconfirmed at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they give me some Hopi/Puebloan mythology I will have all the boners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:16:37-08:00","id":999826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999425#post999425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused about what you mean - the Manitou (Algonquin) and the Teotl (Aztec) are among the core 10!<br /> <br /> We've also had Navajo and Mayan confirmed for Demigod. Lakota, Inuit, Inca, and Guarani have been mentioned as waiting down the line as well (I personally would also hope for a Hopi/Puebloan Kachina Pantheon, but that's unconfirmed at this point).</div> </div> </div> </div>So would Sedna be part of the Inuit or Algonquin pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:25:30-08:00","id":999831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999826#post999826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So would Sedna be part of the Inuit or Algonquin pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sedna is an Inuit goddess, belonging in particular to the communities inhabitating the eastern shores of Canada, and Greenland. The set of deities revered by the different Inuit communities is quite environment-specific, so a sea goddess like Sedna is virtually unknown in the more landlocked areas. While both are thus artificial labels for internally quite diverse cultures, Inuit and Algonquian peoples are in no way related. The Inuit, in fact, are not even Native Americans in the traditional sense, belonging (as other Arctic and Northwestern peoples of America) to a different, much later, and genetically and culturally unrelated wave of migration than the rest of the American peoples.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:49:54-08:00","id":999928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999831#post999831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sedna is an Inuit goddess, belonging in particular to the communities inhabitating the eastern shores of Canada, and Greenland. The set of deities revered by the different Inuit communities is quite environment-specific, so a sea goddess like Sedna is virtually unknown in the more landlocked areas. While both are thus artificial labels for internally quite diverse cultures, Inuit and Algonquian peoples are in no way related. The Inuit, in fact, are not even Native Americans in the traditional sense, belonging (as other Arctic and Northwestern peoples of America) to a different, much later, and genetically and culturally unrelated wave of migration than the rest of the American peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm hoping for. It's hard to find any good English sources about the Manitou and I didn't know if they were going to do the Inuit (Inue a good pantheon name?) or not so I thought they might sneak in Sedna for the sake of convience. But now that I know they plan on doing multiple Native American pantheons, it's good to know so many distinct deities won't be mashed together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:58:04-08:00","id":999931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999826#post999826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So would Sedna be part of the Inuit or Algonquin pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sedna is an Inuit deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:01:42-08:00","id":999933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999928#post999928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what I'm hoping for. It's hard to find any good English sources about the Manitou and I didn't know if they were going to do the Inuit (Inue a good pantheon name?) or not so I thought they might sneak in Sedna for the sake of convience. But now that I know they plan on doing multiple Native American pantheons, it's good to know so many distinct deities won't be mashed together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Inue fits as a name, although there are of course a number of different variants and dialects - also, I've only read a few books on the subject, so I'm hardly an expert. Regarding English sources on the Manitou, specifically as the gods of the Ojibwe/Anishinaabe, I'd recommend anything by Basil Johnston to you. On Inuit mythology, the best starting point is Daniel Merkur's &quot;Powers Which We Do Not Know&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:23:42-08:00","id":999946,"title":"","content":"Slavic pantheon would be great. And please,I begging the authors if they read this, PLEASE - give wolf of associated animal to some god. To any one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:58:04-08:00","id":1000001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999946#post999946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slavic pantheon would be great. And please,I begging the authors if they read this, PLEASE - give wolf of associated animal to some god. To any one!</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the central Algonquin figures, Chibiabos, is a major Wolf god and God of the dead. I'd be shocked if he wasn't one of the Manitou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:04:24-08:00","id":1000100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=999946#post999946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slavic pantheon would be great. And please,I begging the authors if they read this, PLEASE - give wolf of associated animal to some god. To any one!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If Chibiabos doesn't make the Manitou like Glamourweaver said, then surely the Inuit pantheon will have Amarok. He's a trickster god who's a wolf (from what I can tell from my research).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:25:34-08:00","id":1000113,"title":"","content":"I still do, more than anything, want the Turkic/Mongolian/Tengri gods. I know that they're obscure and hard to research (and believe me, <i>I <b>do </b>know</i>) but I just... love them and wish they get included.<br /> <br /> If worst comes to worst I can always try to make my own expansion for them, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:19:25-08:00","id":1000132,"title":"","content":"May be these guys?<br /> <span style=\"color:#2C2E30\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Jumala Gods of Finlad <br /> <img src=\"http://static3.comicvine.com/uploads/original/5/56904/1960685-jumala_of_finland.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>I don't know about them and where Marvel find them, but this art looks cool.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:44:45-08:00","id":1000140,"title":"","content":"Jumalat would be the actual plural (Jumala just means &quot;God&quot; and is the word Finnish translations of the Bible use) - and yeah, the Finnish gods should be a definite possibility! They're pretty much the primary unconfirmed European Pantheon we could hope to see.<br /> <br /> The big blank on the map though are other African Pantheons besides the Netjer and Orisha. Possibilities that come to mind are: Igbo, Dinka, Mbuti, Khoisan, and Zulu (or a broader Bantu Pantheon, but if you're going to focus on a specific Bantu culture I'd go with Zulu). Ashanti is possible just to get Anansi, but there aren't a lot of other active figures to draw on - I'm kind of inclined just to make Anansi a roving trickster figure who doesn't act as part of a greater Pantheon, as Nyame and Asase Ye that bore him are just names of the distant Sky and Earth Primordials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:14:13-08:00","id":1000148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1000132#post1000132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May be these guys?<br /> <span style=\"color:#2C2E30\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Jumala Gods of Finlad <br /> <img src=\"http://static3.comicvine.com/uploads/original/5/56904/1960685-jumala_of_finland.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>I don't know about them and where Marvel find them, but this art looks cool.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can learn more about Finnish mythology from their national epic, the Kalevala. Definitely would like to see Vainamoinen in Scion sometime down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T23:13:47-08:00","id":1000163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1000148#post1000148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can learn more about Finnish mythology from their national epic, the Kalevala. Definitely would like to see Vainamoinen in Scion sometime down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <br /> Also, I would really like to have BOTH Persian and Sumerian pantheons. There is some fan-made of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:39:07-08:00","id":1000233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1000163#post1000163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> Also, I would really like to have BOTH Persian and Sumerian pantheons. There is some fan-made of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Persian pantheon, the Yazata, are coming in the companion, and im thinking Sumerian is sitting in the list of things we could see coming.<br /> <br /> Finnish pantheon? sure. sounds like a lovely time.<br /> <br /> And another African pantheon would be good, if only for more options and to learn more about the various gods in that region.<br /> I would love to see more gods in general. <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> that sounds like a lovely idea for Anansi. I think that may be a houserule for me in the making, if he's not included into any other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T06:36:50-08:00","id":1000247,"title":"","content":"The Mesopotamian/Sumerian pantheon are set for Demigod, last we heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:24:28-08:00","id":1000835,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Korean deities at some point. I can't help thinking that, if the Japanese and Chinese gods are featured, it would only be fair. Not to mention that there are lots of interesting things in Korean mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:13:35-08:00","id":1000924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1000835#post1000835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Korean deities at some point. I can't help thinking that, if the Japanese and Chinese gods are featured, it would only be fair. Not to mention that there are lots of interesting things in Korean mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I don't know a lot about KOREAN myths, so that'd be pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:52:42-08:00","id":1001099,"title":"","content":"I'll just add my vote right here for both the Finnish and Korean Pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:07:23-08:00","id":1027816,"title":"","content":"Any one want an accurate Roman Pantheon? It wasn't really anything like the Greek Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:10:24-08:00","id":1027818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1027816#post1027816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any one want an accurate Roman Pantheon? It wasn't really anything like the Greek Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scion take is that they're Mantles of the Greek gods, which seems perfectly fine to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:11:25-08:00","id":1029000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1000835#post1000835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Korean deities at some point. I can't help thinking that, if the Japanese and Chinese gods are featured, it would only be fair. Not to mention that there are lots of interesting things in Korean mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sad how the Mongolian Empire, the Occupation by Imperial Japan, and the Korean War North Korea butchered, slaughtered, pillaged and raped both the people and the cultural wealth of our country. I wouldn't be surprised if the Korean pantheon is in a similar situation to the Nemetondevos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:14:06-08:00","id":1029002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1027818#post1027818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Scion take is that they're Mantles of the Greek gods, which seems perfectly fine to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to criticize you, but still it's amusing how people think some gods are perfectly fine to be assimilated into other cultures, while the idea of identifying some gods as being one-and-the-same with other gods in the same culture is treated akin to blasphemy in the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:12:15-08:00","id":1029034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1029002#post1029002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not trying to criticize you, but still it's amusing how people think some gods are perfectly fine to be assimilated into other cultures, while the idea of identifying some gods as being one-and-the-same with other gods in the same culture is treated akin to blasphemy in the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's seems like a thing that most pantheons would not be happy with. In fact, I'd imagine that's one of the major reasons why most decided to stop overtly interacting with the World in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:22:59-08:00","id":1029045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1029002#post1029002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not trying to criticize you, but still it's amusing how people think some gods are perfectly fine to be assimilated into other cultures, while the idea of identifying some gods as being one-and-the-same with other gods in the same culture is treated akin to blasphemy in the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you could argue your claim - as those who've complained in the past have - instead of being vaguely condescending. I grasp that the Romans had unique Etruscan deities and spins on their gods, but many of their myths are straight-up Greek stories with the names changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:03:09-08:00","id":1029307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1029045#post1029045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe you could argue your claim - as those who've complained in the past have - instead of being vaguely condescending. I grasp that the Romans had unique Etruscan deities and spins on their gods, but many of their myths are straight-up Greek stories with the names changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not here to argue academic details in what is ultimately an internet forum for games, despite its high level of knowledge and expertise (both in the forums and the games). Like you said, people already have backed up their respective claims before, so I see know reason to repeat all that. I'm only here as a player and a consumer - in which perspective, my only argument is that Scion would benefit from having more pantheons. So, just as I want to see the Egyptian goddesses as separate beings more than alternate identities of each other, I want to see a spin on the Roman deities before they were assimilated into the Greek mythos.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the last one on Romans is a fixation of mine related to my disappointment over how much of the surviving Korean mythos has been painted over by Chinese and/or Japanese mythos. &quot;The remaining myths of this culture are largely a renamed version of another culture's myths, so there's no reason to study them deeper&quot; may be fine for cultures already gone, but I'm ever wary about that logic extending to cultures belonging to peoples who are still well alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T20:08:46-08:00","id":1035599,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the Holy People/<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Diyin Din\u00e9 of the</span></span></span> Navajo/Din<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u00e9, since I've been a big fan of Tony Hillerman's books for a number of years now.<br /> <br /> Also cool to see would be the Zulu, the Cherokee, Native Hawaiian, and Finnish. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:55:35-08:00","id":1035624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1035599#post1035599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Native Hawaiian</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I heard, Neall wants to put a Polynesian Pantheon in the Demigod book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:34:14-08:00","id":1036306,"title":"","content":"I confess that this is weird, but it would be fun as an April 1st thing to release a PDF or something of a &quot;generic European&quot; pantheon, done in the style of how the native North American beliefs always used to get jumbled up into a single pantheon of &quot;Great Spirit, Thunderbird, Coyote, etc.&quot; in RPG sourcebooks back in the day (the 2nd ed AD&amp;D Deities &amp; Demigods book springs to mind). You know, where you have Zeus and The Virgin Mary with their kids Thor and Jesus who go on adventures together. Work in Puck, Robin Hood, Fafnir, Barbarossa and Jack the Ripper for good measure. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:17:51-08:00","id":1058140,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the Hopi, Hittite, Australian Aboriginal, Finnish, Guarani, Canaanite, Inuit, Basque, Filipino, Dogon, Inca, Arabian, Welsh, Mongol-Turkic, Cherokee (Maybe. If they can find enough suitable characters), Baltic, Tibetan, Zulu, Lakota, Armenian, Taino, Indonesian, Mapuche, Siberian, Elamitic, Sami, Korean, and Circassian pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 03-12-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:44:03-08:00","id":1058154,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder what role Baphomet serves in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:49:36-08:00","id":1058159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1058154#post1058154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder what role Baphomet serves in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think he was some really minor Titanspawn who through sheer guts and determination became divine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:53:02-08:00","id":1058161,"title":"","content":"One thing this thread has impressed on me is just how many potential Pantheons there are: the devs are unlikely to run out any time soon. With that in mind, I'd be curious to know which Pantheons you <i>don't</i> want to see (or at least which ones you're fine with being postponed indefinitely), and why not. Try to focus on Pantheons that you <i>like</i>, but would still not recommend because they are in some way problematic and/or redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:43:41-08:00","id":1058179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1058161#post1058161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing this thread has impressed on me is just how many potential Pantheons there are: the devs are unlikely to run out any time soon. With that in mind, I'd be curious to know which Pantheons you <i>don't</i> want to see (or at least which ones you're fine with being postponed indefinitely), and why not. Try to focus on Pantheons that you <i>like</i>, but would still not recommend because they are in some way problematic and/or redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun, okay, I like this idea! Let's see...<br /> <br /> The <b>Etruscans</b> pretty clearly had some very different ideas of Divinity to the Latins to the south of them. The idea of Deities who are less Anthropomorphic, and the Haruspication are really interesting, but we just know so absolute little about them due to having limited written records, and then not having the ability to translate all of their language adding to the problems.<br /> <br /> I am going to make a single explanation for various Celtic groups. I would <i>love</i> to have a flourishing collection of Celtic Pantheons, but, we have scant to no records for most of them. The <b>Manx</b>, the <b>Picts</b>, the <b>Cornish</b>, and the <b>Iberians</b> are all not really capable of being a Pantheon, we just know next to nothing about what their religious systems, or sometimes anything about them anymore. Also, while I love the Celts, it would add to the Eurocentric bloat.<br /> <br /> The <b>Basque Pantheon</b> interests me as a non-PIE European culture. However, things are so incredibly spotty that I am unsure they could really be written up. Since we know nothing about them, their Pantheon plot would almost surely get tied up arguing with the Proto-Indo-European peoples around them, and for a reason I am about to get into, I think avoiding that topic would save an enormous amount of headache. Also more Eurocentric bloat.<br /> <br /> The <b>Proto-Indo-European</b> <b>Pantheon</b> is something I have seen come up very, very rarely. We know pretty much nothing about them, so including them would be almost entirely fiction to start with which isn't really up my personal alley. However, for everyone else, the PIE Pantheon would be an utter mess for everything. It would start getting into the nitty gritty of where a ton of Pantheons have their Genesis from, gets into the tricky realm of how Gods come to be, starts to challenge the All-Myths-Are-True system in a weird way. I would avoid proto-Pantheons like a plague just because they cause <i>so many</i> issues, even just by acknowledging they exist. They just... complicate everything by their very existence. Further, it would add to the Eurocentric bloat, at least in part. And furthermore would probably get into some metaplot mainly involving their progeny Pantheons, which with the existing Eurocentric bloat means that it would involve a lot of European Pantheons at the exclusion of most of the world with PIE cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":".  Still bad at formatting. 03-04-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T19:31:37-08:00","id":1058741,"title":"","content":"I would love to see some form of Slavic Pantheon as that is a very large region of the world unrepresented [Plus fuck I'd like to see what twisted shit would come out of whoever made Baba Yaga without that stupid ass &quot;Nationality&quot; bit to her]<br /> <br /> With the Polynesian Pantheon yes it is true that each group have their on distinctive narrative, but each of the regions all form from the same group. Just as with how Greece and Rome view the gods different [Rome saw Mars as a Strategic Military Genius whereas in Greece he was a Savage Brute who lusted for nothing more than battlefield carnage] they have enough similarities that they can be unified under a single pantheon. Will it be perfect? No not really. What it will do is save us from far to much redundancy in the aspectst that are similar. Something has been said [don't ask where, I forget] about gods who take on various persona's, such as The Morrigan who can either be 3 faces of the same god, or 3 Goddesses all called The Morrigan. They would all be the same gods, just varying by how each group views them in their narrrative. <br /> <br /> If we're going to narrow it down to a single Native American group for which to have a Pantheon than i would suggest either the Navajo or Cherokee as they were the two most numerous tribes in the United States.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T21:56:36-08:00","id":1058776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1058741#post1058741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see some form of Slavic Pantheon as that is a very large region of the world unrepresented [Plus fuck I'd like to see what twisted shit would come out of whoever made Baba Yaga without that stupid ass &quot;Nationality&quot; bit to her]</div> </div> </div> </div>Slavic Pantheon is coming in Demigod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we're going to narrow it down to a single Native American group for which to have a Pantheon </div> </div> </div>Why would we do that? Algonquian is coming in Hero, but that doesn't stop anyone from doing anything else. North America is an <i>entire continent!</i> You wouldn't advocate for a 'European Pantheon,' would you?<br /> <br /> I think Neall has mentioned wanting to do Lakota and Inuit Pantheons down the line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:26:12-08:00","id":1058783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1058776#post1058776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would we do that? Algonquian is coming in Hero, but that doesn't stop anyone from doing anything else. North America is an <i>entire continent!</i> You wouldn't advocate for a 'European Pantheon,' would you?<br /> <br /> I think Neall has mentioned wanting to do Lakota and Inuit Pantheons down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think The Dude means he only wants one Native American Pantheon in the game, he's suggesting those two as the ones he thinks are the most important to include. Similar to how I could go, &quot;Well, I like most Trickster Gods, but if I had to pick only one as my favorite I would say the Raven from the Haida.&quot; He might want forty Native American Pantheons, but presenting the two he considers most important for inclusion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:48:41-08:00","id":1059176,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know of all the pantheons that have been mentioned as potential ones down the line that the developers want to cover? Like Lakota and Inuit were just mentioned. Any others?<br /> <br /> And I don't mean Slavic, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, Navajo, and Mayan, which are slated for Demigod I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:54:07-08:00","id":1059182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1058776#post1058776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would we do that? Algonquian is coming in Hero, but that doesn't stop anyone from doing anything else. North America is an <i>entire continent!</i> You wouldn't advocate for a 'European Pantheon,' would you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember seeing, I think it was on Tumblr, someone making a joke about an RPG book about gods having a distinctive breakdown of regional/tribal pantheons and beliefs... And then there's this ONE European Pantheon that has Loki, Thor, Ares, and King Arthur in the same pantheon, to make a point about people who put Coyote and Thunderbird in a catch-all &quot;Native American&quot; Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:08:44-08:00","id":1059195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1059176#post1059176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know of all the pantheons that have been mentioned as potential ones down the line that the developers want to cover? Like Lakota and Inuit were just mentioned. Any others?<br /> <br /> And I don't mean Slavic, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, Navajo, and Mayan, which are slated for Demigod I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have fun sifting through all this! <a href=\"https://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ttrarchive.com/store/ind...:_What_We_Know</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T23:20:42-08:00","id":1059363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1059176#post1059176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know of all the pantheons that have been mentioned as potential ones down the line that the developers want to cover? Like Lakota and Inuit were just mentioned. Any others?<br /> <br /> And I don't mean Slavic, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, Navajo, and Mayan, which are slated for Demigod I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incan, Inuit, Canaanite, Tagalog, Welsh, Lakota, Guarani, Siberian, Steppe, and at least one Native Australian have all been mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:01:47-08:00","id":1059696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1059363#post1059363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incan, Inuit, Canaanite, Tagalog, Welsh, Lakota, Guarani, Siberian, Steppe, and at least one Native Australian have all been mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's completely and utterly awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:14:07-08:00","id":1059808,"title":"","content":"If there's one thing I've learned about Neall in the Kickstarter and the leadup? Him and other culturess pantheons is a bit like a kid in a toy store. &quot;OH OH OH CAN I PUT IN THE WELSH?! Oh, the Lakota Pantheon's awesome! Oh oh oh oh how about the Incan or the Polynesian?!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T15:33:42-08:00","id":1060685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1059808#post1059808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's one thing I've learned about Neall in the Kickstarter and the leadup? Him and other culturess pantheons is a bit like a kid in a toy store. &quot;OH OH OH CAN I PUT IN THE WELSH?! Oh, the Lakota Pantheon's awesome! Oh oh oh oh how about the Incan or the Polynesian?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat man loves his job. It's heartwarming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:28:35-08:00","id":1061238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1059182#post1059182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember seeing, I think it was on Tumblr, someone making a joke about an RPG book about gods having a distinctive breakdown of regional/tribal pantheons and beliefs... And then there's this ONE European Pantheon that has Loki, Thor, Ares, and King Arthur in the same pantheon, to make a point about people who put Coyote and Thunderbird in a catch-all &quot;Native American&quot; Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that may have been <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1036306#post1036306\">me</a>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />/<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 03-11-2017, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T10:34:01-08:00","id":1061286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> 